Mark	Mk	48	11	31	But they thought with themselves, saying: If we say, From heaven; he will say, Why then did you not believe him?
Mark	Mk	48	11	32	If we say, From men, we fear the people. For all men counted John that he was a prophet indeed.
Mark	Mk	48	11	33	And they answering, say to Jesus: We know not. And Jesus answering, saith to them: Neither do I tell you by what authority I do these things.
Mark	Mk	48	12	1	And he began to speak to them in parables: A certain man planted a vineyard and made a hedge about it, and dug a place for the winevat, and built a tower, and let it to husbandmen; and went into a far country.
Mark	Mk	48	12	2	And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant to receive of the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.
Mark	Mk	48	12	3	Who having laid hands on him, beat him, and sent him away empty.
Mark	Mk	48	12	4	And again he sent to them another servant; and him they wounded in the head, and used him reproachfully.
Mark	Mk	48	12	5	And again he sent another, and him they killed: and many others, of whom some they beat, and others they killed.
Mark	Mk	48	12	6	Therefore having yet one son, most dear to him; he also sent him unto them last of all, saying: They will reverence my son.
Mark	Mk	48	12	7	But the husbandmen said one to another: This is the heir; come let us kill him; and the inheritance shall be ours.
Mark	Mk	48	12	8	And laying hold on him, they killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard.
Mark	Mk	48	12	9	What therefore will the lord of the vineyard do? He will come and destroy those husbandmen; and will give the vineyard to others.
Mark	Mk	48	12	10	And have you not read this scripture, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is made the head of the corner:
Mark	Mk	48	12	11	By the Lord has this been done, and it is wonderful in our eyes.
Mark	Mk	48	12	12	And they sought to lay hands on him, but they feared the people. For they knew that he spoke this parable to them. And leaving him, they went their way.
Mark	Mk	48	12	13	And they sent to him some of the Pharisees and of the Herodians; that they should catch him in his words.
Mark	Mk	48	12	14	Who coming, say to him: Master, we know that thou art a true speaker, and carest not for any man; for thou regardest not the person of men, but teachest the way of God in truth. Is it lawful to give tribute to Caesar; or shall we not give it?
Mark	Mk	48	12	15	Who knowing their wiliness, saith to them: Why tempt you me? bring me a penny that I may see it.
Mark	Mk	48	12	16	And they brought it him. And he saith to them: Whose is this image and inscription? They say to him, Caesar's.
Mark	Mk	48	12	17	And Jesus answering, said to them: Render therefore to Caesar the things that are Caesar's, and to God the things that are God's. And they marvelled at him.
Mark	Mk	48	12	18	And there came to him the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection; and they asked him, saying:
Mark	Mk	48	12	19	Master, Moses wrote unto us, that if any man's brother die, and leave his wife behind him, and leave no children, his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed to his brother.
Mark	Mk	48	12	20	Now there were seven brethren; and the first took a wife, and died leaving no issue.
Mark	Mk	48	12	21	And the second took her, and died: and neither did he leave any issue. And the third in like manner.
Mark	Mk	48	12	22	And the seven all took her in like manner; and did not leave issue. Last of all the woman also died.
Mark	Mk	48	12	23	In the resurrection therefore, when they shall rise again, whose wife shall she be of them? for the seven had her to wife.
Mark	Mk	48	12	24	And Jesus answering, saith to them: Do ye not therefore err, because you know not the scriptures, nor the power of God?
Mark	Mk	48	12	25	For when they shall rise again from the dead, they shall neither marry, nor be married, but are as the angels in heaven.
Mark	Mk	48	12	26	And as concerning the dead that they rise again, have you not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spoke to him, saying: I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?
Mark	Mk	48	12	27	He is not the God of the dead, but of the living. You therefore do greatly err.
Mark	Mk	48	12	28	And there came one of the scribes that had heard them reasoning together, and seeing that he had answered them well, asked him which was the first commandment of all.
Mark	Mk	48	12	29	And Jesus answered him: The first commandment of all is, Hear, O Israel: the Lord thy God is one God.
Mark	Mk	48	12	30	And thou shalt love the Lord thy God, with thy whole heart, and with thy whole soul, and with thy whole mind, and with thy whole strength. This is the first commandment.
Mark	Mk	48	12	31	And the second is like to it: Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is no other commandment greater than these.
Mark	Mk	48	12	32	And the scribe said to him: Well, Master, thou hast said in truth, that there is one God, and there is no other besides him.
Mark	Mk	48	12	33	And that he should be loved with the whole heart, and with the whole understanding, and with the whole soul, and with the whole strength; and to love one's neighbour as one's self, is a greater thing than all holocausts and sacrifices.
Mark	Mk	48	12	34	And Jesus seeing that he had answered wisely, said to him: Thou art not far from the kingdom of God. And no man after that durst ask him any question.
