Mark	Mk	48	13	1	And as he was going out of the temple, one of his disciples said to him: Master, behold what manner of stones and what buildings are here.
Mark	Mk	48	13	2	And Jesus answering, said to him: Seest thou all these great buildings? There shall not be left a stone upon a stone, that shall not be thrown down.
Mark	Mk	48	13	3	And as he sat on the mount of Olivet over against the temple, Peter and James and John and Andrew asked him apart:
Mark	Mk	48	13	4	Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign when all these things shall begin to be fulfilled?
Mark	Mk	48	13	5	And Jesus answering, began to say to them, Take heed lest any man deceive you.
Mark	Mk	48	13	6	For many shall come in my name, saying, I am he; and they shall deceive many.
Mark	Mk	48	13	7	And when you shall hear of wars and rumours of wars, fear ye not. For such things must needs be, but the end is not yet.
Mark	Mk	48	13	8	For nation shall rise against nation and kingdom against kingdom, and there shall be earthquakes in divers places, and famines. These things are the beginning of sorrows.
Mark	Mk	48	13	9	But look to yourselves. For they shall deliver you up to councils, and in the synagogues you shall be beaten, and you shall stand before governors and kings for my sake, for a testimony unto them.
Mark	Mk	48	13	10	And unto all nations the gospel must first be preached.
Mark	Mk	48	13	11	And when they shall lead you and deliver you up, be not thoughtful beforehand what you shall speak; but whatsoever shall be given you in that hour, that speak ye. For it is not you that speak, but the Holy Ghost.
Mark	Mk	48	13	12	And the brother shall betray his brother unto death, and the father his son; and children shall rise up against the parents, and shall work their death.
Mark	Mk	48	13	13	And you shall be hated by all men for my name's sake. But he that shall endure unto the end, he shall be saved.
Mark	Mk	48	13	14	And when you shall see the abomination of desolation, standing where it ought not: he that readeth let him understand: then let them that are in Judea, flee unto the mountains:
Mark	Mk	48	13	15	And let him that is on the housetop, not go down into the house, nor enter therein to take any thing out of the house:
Mark	Mk	48	13	16	And let him that shall be in the field, not turn back to take up his garment.
Mark	Mk	48	13	17	And woe to them that are with child, and that give suck in those days.
Mark	Mk	48	13	18	But pray ye, that these things happen not in winter.
Mark	Mk	48	13	19	For in those days shall be such tribulations, as were not from the beginning of the creation which God created until now, neither shall be.
Mark	Mk	48	13	20	And unless the Lord had shortened the days, no flesh should be saved: but for the sake of the elect which he hath chosen, he hath shortened the days.
Mark	Mk	48	13	21	And then if any man shall say to you, Lo, here is Christ; lo, he is here: do not believe.
Mark	Mk	48	13	22	For there will rise up false Christs and false prophets, and they shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce (if it were possible) even the elect.
Mark	Mk	48	13	23	Take you heed therefore; behold I have foretold you all things.
Mark	Mk	48	13	24	But in those days, after that tribulation, the sun shall be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light.
Mark	Mk	48	13	25	And the stars of heaven shall be falling down, and the powers that are in heaven, shall be moved.
Mark	Mk	48	13	26	And then shall they see the Son of man coming in the clouds, with great power and glory.
Mark	Mk	48	13	27	And then shall he send his angels, and shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth to the uttermost part of heaven.
Mark	Mk	48	13	28	Now of the fig tree learn ye a parable. When the branch thereof is now tender, and the leaves are come forth, you know that summer is very near.
Mark	Mk	48	13	29	So you also when you shall see these things come to pass, know ye that it is very nigh, even at the doors.
Mark	Mk	48	13	30	Amen I say to you, that this generation shall not pass, until all these things be done.
Mark	Mk	48	13	31	Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my word shall not pass away.
Mark	Mk	48	13	32	But of that day or hour no man knoweth, neither the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but the Father.
Mark	Mk	48	13	33	Take ye heed, watch and pray. For ye know not when the time is.
