Mark	Mk	48	15	37	And Jesus having cried out with a loud voice, gave up the ghost.
Mark	Mk	48	15	38	And the veil of the temple was rent in two, from the top to the bottom.
Mark	Mk	48	15	39	And the centurion who stood over against him, seeing that crying out in this manner he had given up the ghost, said: Indeed this man was the son of God.
Mark	Mk	48	15	40	And there were also women looking on afar off: among whom was Mary Magdalen, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joseph, and Salome:
Mark	Mk	48	15	41	Who also when he was in Galilee followed him, and ministered to him, and many other women that came up with him to Jerusalem.
Mark	Mk	48	15	42	And when evening was now come, (because it was the Parasceve, that is, the day before the sabbath,)
Mark	Mk	48	15	43	Joseph of Arimathea, a noble counsellor, who was also himself looking for the kingdom of God, came and went in boldly to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus.
Mark	Mk	48	15	44	But Pilate wondered that he should be already dead. And sending for the centurion, he asked him if he were already dead.
Mark	Mk	48	15	45	And when he had understood it by the centurion, he gave the body to Joseph.
Mark	Mk	48	15	46	And Joseph buying fine linen, and taking him down, wrapped him up in the fine linen, and laid him in a sepulchre which was hewed out of a rock. And he rolled a stone to the door of the sepulchre.
Mark	Mk	48	15	47	And Mary Magdalen, and Mary the mother of Joseph, beheld where he was laid.
Mark	Mk	48	16	1	And when the sabbath was past, Mary Magdalen, and Mary the mother of James, and Salome, bought sweet spices, that coming, they might anoint Jesus.
Mark	Mk	48	16	2	And very early in the morning, the first day of the week, they come to the sepulchre, the sun being now risen.
Mark	Mk	48	16	3	And they said one to another: Who shall roll us back the stone from the door of the sepulchre?
Mark	Mk	48	16	4	And looking, they saw the stone rolled back. For it was very great.
Mark	Mk	48	16	5	And entering into the sepulchre, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, clothed with a white robe: and they were astonished.
Mark	Mk	48	16	6	Who saith to them: Be not affrighted; you seek Jesus of Nazareth, who was crucified: he is risen, he is not here, behold the place where they laid him.
Mark	Mk	48	16	7	But go, tell his disciples and Peter that he goeth before you into Galilee; there you shall see him, as he told you.
Mark	Mk	48	16	8	But they going out, fled from the sepulchre. For a trembling and fear had seized them: and they said nothing to any man; for they were afraid.
Mark	Mk	48	16	9	But he rising early the first day of the week, appeared first to Mary Magdalen, out of whom he had cast seven devils.
Mark	Mk	48	16	10	She went and told them that had been with him, who were mourning and weeping.
Mark	Mk	48	16	11	And they hearing that he was alive, and had been seen by her, did not believe.
Mark	Mk	48	16	12	And after that he appeared in another shape to two of them walking, as they were going into the country.
Mark	Mk	48	16	13	And they going told it to the rest: neither did they believe them.
Mark	Mk	48	16	14	At length he appeared to the eleven as they were at table: and he upbraided them with their incredulity and hardness of heart, because they did not believe them who had seen him after he was risen again.
Mark	Mk	48	16	15	And he said to them: Go ye into the whole world, and preach the gospel to every creature.
Mark	Mk	48	16	16	He that believeth and is baptized, shall be saved: but he that believeth not shall be condemned.
Mark	Mk	48	16	17	And these signs shall follow them that believe: In my name they shall cast out devils: they shall speak with new tongues.
Mark	Mk	48	16	18	They shall take up serpents; and if they shall drink any deadly thing, it shall not hurt them: they shall lay their hands upon the sick, and they shall recover.
Mark	Mk	48	16	19	And the Lord Jesus, after he had spoken to them, was taken up into heaven, and sitteth on the right hand of God.
Mark	Mk	48	16	20	But they going forth preached everywhere: the Lord working withal, and confirming the word with signs that followed.
Luke	Lk	49	1	1	Forasmuch as many have taken in hand to set forth in order a narration of the things that have been accomplished among us;
Luke	Lk	49	1	2	According as they have delivered them unto us, who from the beginning were eyewitnesses and ministers of the word:
Luke	Lk	49	1	3	It seemed good to me also, having diligently attained to all things from the beginning, to write to thee in order, most excellent Theophilus,
Luke	Lk	49	1	4	That thou mayest know the verity of those words in which thou hast been instructed.
Luke	Lk	49	1	5	There was in the days of Herod, the king of Judea, a certain priest named Zachary, of the course of Abia; and his wife was of the daughters of Aaron, and her name Elizabeth.
Luke	Lk	49	1	6	And they were both just before God, walking in all the commandments and justifications of the Lord without blame.
Luke	Lk	49	1	7	And they had no son, for that Elizabeth was barren, and they both were well advanced in years.
Luke	Lk	49	1	8	And it came to pass, when he executed the priestly function in the order of his course before God,
Luke	Lk	49	1	9	According to the custom of the priestly office, it was his lot to offer incense, going into the temple of the Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	1	10	And all the multitude of the people was praying without, at the hour of incense.
Luke	Lk	49	1	11	And there appeared to him an angel of the Lord, standing on the right side of the altar of incense.
Luke	Lk	49	1	12	And Zachary seeing him, was troubled, and fear fell upon him.
Luke	Lk	49	1	13	But the angel said to him: Fear not, Zachary, for thy prayer is heard; and thy wife Elizabeth shall bear thee a son, and thou shalt call his name John:
Luke	Lk	49	1	14	And thou shalt have joy and gladness, and many shall rejoice in his nativity.
Luke	Lk	49	1	15	For he shall be great before the Lord; and shall drink no wine nor strong drink: and he shall be filled with the Holy Ghost, even from his mother's womb.
Luke	Lk	49	1	16	And he shall convert many of the children of Israel to the Lord their God.
Luke	Lk	49	1	17	And he shall go before him in the spirit and power of Elias; that he may turn the hearts of the fathers unto the children, and the incredulous to the wisdom of the just, to prepare unto the Lord a perfect people.
Luke	Lk	49	1	18	And Zachary said to the angel: Whereby shall I know this? for I am an old man, and my wife is advanced in years.
Luke	Lk	49	1	19	And the angel answering, said to him: I am Gabriel, who stand before God: and am sent to speak to thee, and to bring thee these good tidings.
Luke	Lk	49	1	20	And behold, thou shalt be dumb, and shalt not be able to speak until the day wherein these things shall come to pass, because thou hast not believed my words, which shall be fulfilled in their time.
Luke	Lk	49	1	21	And the people were waiting for Zachary; and they wondered that he tarried so long in the temple.
Luke	Lk	49	1	22	And when he came out, he could not speak to them: and they understood that he had seen a vision in the temple. And he made signs to them, and remained dumb.
Luke	Lk	49	1	23	And it came to pass, after the days of his office were accomplished, he departed to his own house.
Luke	Lk	49	1	24	And after those days, Elizabeth his wife conceived, and hid herself five months, saying:
Luke	Lk	49	1	25	Thus hath the Lord dealt with me in the days wherein he hath had regard to take away my reproach among men.
Luke	Lk	49	1	26	And in the sixth month, the angel Gabriel was sent from God into a city of Galilee, called Nazareth,
Luke	Lk	49	1	27	To a virgin espoused to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David; and the virgin's name was Mary.
Luke	Lk	49	1	28	And the angel being come in, said unto her: Hail, full of grace, the Lord is with thee: blessed art thou among women.
Luke	Lk	49	1	29	Who having heard, was troubled at his saying, and thought with herself what manner of salutation this should be.
Luke	Lk	49	1	30	And the angel said to her: Fear not, Mary, for thou hast found grace with God.
Luke	Lk	49	1	31	Behold thou shalt conceive in thy womb, and shalt bring forth a son; and thou shalt call his name Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	1	32	He shall be great, and shall be called the Son of the most High; and the Lord God shall give unto him the throne of David his father; and he shall reign in the house of Jacob for ever.
Luke	Lk	49	1	33	And of his kingdom there shall be no end.
Luke	Lk	49	1	34	And Mary said to the angel: How shall this be done, because I know not man?
Luke	Lk	49	1	35	And the angel answering, said to her: The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the most High shall overshadow thee. And therefore also the Holy which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God.
Luke	Lk	49	1	36	And behold thy cousin Elizabeth, she also hath conceived a son in her old age; and this is the sixth month with her that is called barren:
Luke	Lk	49	1	37	Because no word shall be impossible with God.
Luke	Lk	49	1	38	And Mary said: Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it done to me according to thy word. And the angel departed from her.
Luke	Lk	49	1	39	And Mary rising up in those days, went into the hill country with haste into a city of Juda.
Luke	Lk	49	1	40	And she entered into the house of Zachary, and saluted Elizabeth.
Luke	Lk	49	1	41	And it came to pass, that when Elizabeth heard the salutation of Mary, the infant leaped in her womb. And Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Ghost:
Luke	Lk	49	1	42	And she cried out with a loud voice, and said: Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb.
Luke	Lk	49	1	43	And whence is this to me, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?
Luke	Lk	49	1	44	For behold as soon as the voice of thy salutation sounded in my ears, the infant in my womb leaped for joy.
Luke	Lk	49	1	45	And blessed art thou that hast believed, because those things shall be accomplished that were spoken to thee by the Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	1	46	And Mary said: My soul doth magnify the Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	1	47	And my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Saviour.
Luke	Lk	49	1	48	Because he hath regarded the humility of his handmaid; for behold from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.
Luke	Lk	49	1	49	Because he that is mighty, hath done great things to me; and holy is his name.
Luke	Lk	49	1	50	And his mercy is from generation unto generations, to them that fear him.
Luke	Lk	49	1	51	He hath shewed might in his arm: he hath scattered the proud in the conceit of their heart.
Luke	Lk	49	1	52	He hath put down the mighty from their seat, and hath exalted the humble.
Luke	Lk	49	1	53	He hath filled the hungry with good things; and the rich he hath sent empty away.
Luke	Lk	49	1	54	He hath received Israel his servant, being mindful of his mercy:
Luke	Lk	49	1	55	As he spoke to our fathers, to Abraham and to his seed for ever.
Luke	Lk	49	1	56	And Mary abode with her about three months; and she returned to her own house.
Luke	Lk	49	1	57	Now Elizabeth's full time of being delivered was come, and she brought forth a son.
Luke	Lk	49	1	58	And her neighbours and kinsfolks heard that the Lord had shewed his great mercy towards her, and they congratulated with her.
Luke	Lk	49	1	59	And it came to pass, that on the eighth day they came to circumcise the child, and they called him by his father's name Zachary.
Luke	Lk	49	1	60	And his mother answering, said: Not so; but he shall be called John.
Luke	Lk	49	1	61	And they said to her: There is none of thy kindred that is called by this name.
Luke	Lk	49	1	62	And they made signs to his father, how he would have him called.
Luke	Lk	49	1	63	And demanding a writing table, he wrote, saying: John is his name. And they all wondered.
Luke	Lk	49	1	64	And immediately his mouth was opened, and his tongue loosed, and he spoke, blessing God.
Luke	Lk	49	1	65	And fear came upon all their neighbours; and all these things were noised abroad over all the hill country of Judea.
Luke	Lk	49	1	66	And all they that had heard them laid them up in their heart, saying: What an one, think ye, shall this child be? For the hand of the Lord was with him.
Luke	Lk	49	1	67	And Zachary his father was filled with the Holy Ghost; and he prophesied, saying:
Luke	Lk	49	1	68	Blessed be the Lord God of Israel; because he hath visited and wrought the redemption of his people:
Luke	Lk	49	1	69	And hath raised up an horn of salvation to us, in the house of David his servant:
Luke	Lk	49	1	70	As he spoke by the mouth of his holy prophets, who are from the beginning:
Luke	Lk	49	1	71	Salvation from our enemies, and from the hand of all that hate us:
Luke	Lk	49	1	72	To perform mercy to our fathers, and to remember his holy testament,
Luke	Lk	49	1	73	The oath, which he swore to Abraham our father, that he would grant to us,
Luke	Lk	49	1	74	That being delivered from the hand of our enemies, we may serve him without fear,
Luke	Lk	49	1	75	In holiness and justice before him, all our days.
Luke	Lk	49	1	76	And thou, child, shalt be called the prophet of the Highest: for thou shalt go before the face of the Lord to prepare his ways:
Luke	Lk	49	1	77	To give knowledge of salvation to his people, unto the remission of their sins:
Luke	Lk	49	1	78	Through the bowels of the mercy of our God, in which the Orient from on high hath visited us:
Luke	Lk	49	1	79	To enlighten them that sit in darkness, and in the shadow of death: to direct our feet into the way of peace.
Luke	Lk	49	1	80	And the child grew, and was strengthened in spirit; and was in the deserts until the day of his manifestation to Israel.
Luke	Lk	49	2	1	And it came to pass, that in those days there went out a decree from Caesar Augustus, that the whole world should be enrolled.
Luke	Lk	49	2	2	This enrolling was first made by Cyrinus, the governor of Syria.
Luke	Lk	49	2	3	And all went to be enrolled, every one into his own city.
Luke	Lk	49	2	4	And Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the city of Nazareth into Judea, to the city of David, which is called Bethlehem: because he was of the house and family of David,
Luke	Lk	49	2	5	To be enrolled with Mary his espoused wife, who was with child.
Luke	Lk	49	2	6	And it came to pass, that when they were there, her days were accomplished, that she should be delivered.
Luke	Lk	49	2	7	And she brought forth her firstborn son, and wrapped him up in swaddling clothes, and laid him in a manger; because there was no room for them in the inn.
Luke	Lk	49	2	8	And there were in the same country shepherds watching, and keeping the night watches over their flock.
Luke	Lk	49	2	9	And behold an angel of the Lord stood by them, and the brightness of God shone round about them; and they feared with a great fear.
Luke	Lk	49	2	10	And the angel said to them: Fear not; for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, that shall be to all the people:
Luke	Lk	49	2	11	For, this day, is born to you a Saviour, who is Christ the Lord, in the city of David.
Luke	Lk	49	2	12	And this shall be a sign unto you. You shall find the infant wrapped in swaddling clothes, and laid in a manger.
Luke	Lk	49	2	13	And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly army, praising God, and saying:
Luke	Lk	49	2	14	Glory to God in the highest; and on earth peace to men of good will.
Luke	Lk	49	2	15	And it came to pass, after the angels departed from them into heaven, the shepherds said one to another: Let us go over to Bethlehem, and let us see this word that is come to pass, which the Lord hath shewed to us.
Luke	Lk	49	2	16	And they came with haste; and they found Mary and Joseph, and the infant lying in the manger.
Luke	Lk	49	2	17	And seeing, they understood of the word that had been spoken to them concerning this child.
Luke	Lk	49	2	18	And all that heard, wondered; and at those things that were told them by the shepherds.
Luke	Lk	49	2	19	But Mary kept all these words, pondering them in her heart.
Luke	Lk	49	2	20	And the shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God, for all the things they had heard and seen, as it was told unto them.
Luke	Lk	49	2	21	And after eight days were accomplished, that the child should be circumcised, his name was called JESUS, which was called by the angel, before he was conceived in the womb.
Luke	Lk	49	2	22	And after the days of her purification, according to the law of Moses, were accomplished, they carried him to Jerusalem, to present him to the Lord:
Luke	Lk	49	2	23	As it is written in the law of the Lord: Every male opening the womb shall be called holy to the Lord:
Luke	Lk	49	2	24	And to offer a sacrifice, according as it is written in the law of the Lord, a pair of turtledoves, or two young pigeons:
Luke	Lk	49	2	25	And behold there was a man in Jerusalem named Simeon, and this man was just and devout, waiting for the consolation of Israel; and the Holy Ghost was in him.
Luke	Lk	49	2	26	And he had received an answer from the Holy Ghost, that he should not see death, before he had seen the Christ of the Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	2	27	And he came by the Spirit into the temple. And when his parents brought in the child Jesus, to do for him according to the custom of the law,
Luke	Lk	49	2	28	He also took him into his arms, and blessed God, and said:
Luke	Lk	49	2	29	Now thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord, according to thy word in peace;
Luke	Lk	49	2	30	Because my eyes have seen thy salvation,
Luke	Lk	49	2	31	Which thou hast prepared before the face of all peoples:
Luke	Lk	49	2	32	A light to the revelation of the Gentiles, and the glory of thy people Israel.
Luke	Lk	49	2	33	And his father and mother were wondering at those things which were spoken concerning him.
Luke	Lk	49	2	34	And Simeon blessed them, and said to Mary his mother: Behold this child is set for the fall, and for the resurrection of many in Israel, and for a sign which shall be contradicted;
Luke	Lk	49	2	35	And thy own soul a sword shall pierce, that, out of many hearts, thoughts may be revealed.
Luke	Lk	49	2	36	And there was one Anna, a prophetess, the daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Aser; she was far advanced in years, and had lived with her husband seven years from her virginity.
Luke	Lk	49	2	37	And she was a widow until fourscore and four years; who departed not from the temple, by fastings and prayers serving night and day.
Luke	Lk	49	2	38	Now she, at the same hour, coming in, confessed to the Lord; and spoke of him to all that looked for the redemption of Israel.
Luke	Lk	49	2	39	And after they had performed all things according to the law of the Lord, they returned into Galilee, to their city Nazareth.
Luke	Lk	49	2	40	And the child grew, and waxed strong, full of wisdom; and the grace of God was in him.
Luke	Lk	49	2	41	And his parents went every year to Jerusalem, at the solemn day of the pasch,
Luke	Lk	49	2	42	And when he was twelve years old, they going up into Jerusalem, according to the custom of the feast,
Luke	Lk	49	2	43	And having fulfilled the days, when they returned, the child Jesus remained in Jerusalem; and his parents knew it not.
Luke	Lk	49	2	44	And thinking that he was in the company, they came a day's journey, and sought him among their kinsfolks and acquaintance.
Luke	Lk	49	2	45	And not finding him, they returned into Jerusalem, seeking him.
Luke	Lk	49	2	46	And it came to pass, that, after three days, they found him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the doctors, hearing them, and asking them questions.
Luke	Lk	49	2	47	And all that heard him were astonished at his wisdom and his answers.
Luke	Lk	49	2	48	And seeing him, they wondered. And his mother said to him: Son, why hast thou done so to us? behold thy father and I have sought thee sorrowing.
Luke	Lk	49	2	49	And he said to them: How is it that you sought me? did you not know, that I must be about my father's business?
Luke	Lk	49	2	50	And they understood not the word that he spoke unto them.
Luke	Lk	49	2	51	And he went down with them, and came to Nazareth, and was subject to them. And his mother kept all these words in her heart.
Luke	Lk	49	2	52	And Jesus advanced in wisdom, and age, and grace with God and men.
Luke	Lk	49	3	1	Now in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, Pontius Pilate being governor of Judea, and Herod being tetrarch of Galilee, and Philip his brother tetrarch of Iturea, and the country of Trachonitis, and Lysanias tetrarch of Abilina;
Luke	Lk	49	3	2	Under the high priests Annas and Caiphas; the word of the Lord was made unto John, the son of Zachary, in the desert.
Luke	Lk	49	3	3	And he came into all the country about the Jordan, preaching the baptism of penance for the remission of sins;
Luke	Lk	49	3	4	As it was written in the book of the sayings of Isaias the prophet: A voice of one crying in the wilderness: Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make straight his paths.
Luke	Lk	49	3	5	Every valley shall be filled; and every mountain and hill shall be brought low; and the crooked shall be made straight; and the rough ways plain;
Luke	Lk	49	3	6	And all flesh shall see the salvation of God.
Luke	Lk	49	3	7	He said therefore to the multitudes that went forth to be baptized by him: Ye offspring of vipers, who hath shewed you to flee from the wrath to come?
Luke	Lk	49	3	8	Bring forth therefore fruits worthy of penance; and do not begin to say, We have Abraham for our father. For I say unto you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children to Abraham.
Luke	Lk	49	3	9	For now the axe is laid to the root of the trees. Every tree therefore that bringeth not forth good fruit, shall be cut down and cast into the fire.
Luke	Lk	49	3	10	And the people asked him, saying: What then shall we do?
Luke	Lk	49	3	11	And he answering, said to them: He that hath two coats, let him give to him that hath none; and he that hath meat, let him do in like manner.
Luke	Lk	49	3	12	And the publicans also came to be baptized, and said to him: Master, what shall we do?
Luke	Lk	49	3	13	But he said to them: Do nothing more than that which is appointed you.
Luke	Lk	49	3	14	And the soldiers also asked him, saying: And what shall we do? And he said to them: Do violence to no man; neither calumniate any man; and be content with your pay.
Luke	Lk	49	3	15	And as the people were of opinion, and all were thinking in their hearts of John, that perhaps he might be the Christ;
Luke	Lk	49	3	16	John answered, saying unto all: I indeed baptize you with water; but there shall come one mightier than I, the latchet of whose shoes I am not worthy to loose: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost, and with fire:
Luke	Lk	49	3	17	Whose fan is in his hand, and he will purge his floor, and will gather the wheat into his barn; but the chaff he will burn with unquenchable fire.
Luke	Lk	49	3	18	And many other things exhorting, did he preach to the people.
Luke	Lk	49	3	19	But Herod the tetrarch, when he was reproved by him for Herodias, his brother's wife, and for all the evils which Herod had done;
Luke	Lk	49	3	20	He added this also above all, and shut up John in prison.
Luke	Lk	49	3	21	Now it came to pass, when all the people were baptized, that Jesus also being baptized and praying, heaven was opened;
Luke	Lk	49	3	22	And the Holy Ghost descended in a bodily shape, as a dove upon him; and a voice came from heaven: Thou art my beloved Son; in thee I am well pleased.
Luke	Lk	49	3	23	And Jesus himself was beginning about the age of thirty years; being (as it was supposed) the son of Joseph, who was of Heli, who was of Mathat,
Luke	Lk	49	3	24	Who was of Levi, who was of Melchi, who was of Janne, who was of Joseph,
Luke	Lk	49	3	25	Who was of Mathathias, who was of Amos, who was of Nahum, who was of Hesli, who was of Nagge,
Luke	Lk	49	3	26	Who was of Mahath, who was of Mathathias, who was of Semei, who was of Joseph, who was of Juda,
Luke	Lk	49	3	27	Who was of Joanna, who was of Reza, who was of Zorobabel, who was of Salathiel, who was of Neri,
Luke	Lk	49	3	28	Who was of Melchi, who was of Addi, who was of Cosan, who was of Helmadan, who was of Her,
Luke	Lk	49	3	29	Who was of Jesus, who was of Eliezer, who was of Jorim, who was of Mathat, who was of Levi,
Luke	Lk	49	3	30	Who was of Simeon, who was of Judas, who was of Joseph, who was of Jona, who was of Eliakim,
Luke	Lk	49	3	31	Who was of Melea, who was of Menna, who was of Mathatha, who was of Nathan, who was of David,
Luke	Lk	49	3	32	Who was of Jesse, who was of Obed, who was of Booz, who was of Salmon, who was of Naasson,
Luke	Lk	49	3	33	Who was of Aminadab, who was of Aram, who was of Esron, who was of Phares, who was of Judas,
Luke	Lk	49	3	34	Who was of Jacob, who was of Isaac, who was of Abraham, who was of Thare, who was of Nachor,
Luke	Lk	49	3	35	Who was of Sarug, who was of Ragau, who was of Phaleg, who was of Heber, who was of Sale,
Luke	Lk	49	3	36	Who was of Cainan, who was of Arphaxad, who was of Sem, who was of Noe, who was of Lamech,
Luke	Lk	49	3	37	Who was of Mathusale, who was of Henoch, who was of Jared, who was of Malaleel, who was of Cainan,
Luke	Lk	49	3	38	Who was of Henos, who was of Seth, who was of Adam, who was of God.
Luke	Lk	49	4	1	And Jesus being full of the Holy Ghost, returned from the Jordan, and was led by the Spirit into the desert,
Luke	Lk	49	4	2	For the space of forty days; and was tempted by the devil. And he ate nothing in those days; and when they were ended, he was hungry.
Luke	Lk	49	4	3	And the devil said to him: If thou be the Son of God, say to this stone that it be made bread.
Luke	Lk	49	4	4	And Jesus answered him: It is written, that Man liveth not by bread alone, but by every word of God.
Luke	Lk	49	4	5	And the devil led him into a high mountain, and shewed him all the kingdoms of the world in a moment of time;
Luke	Lk	49	4	6	And he said to him: To thee will I give all this power, and the glory of them; for to me they are delivered, and to whom I will, I give them.
Luke	Lk	49	4	7	If thou therefore wilt adore before me, all shall be thine.
Luke	Lk	49	4	8	And Jesus answering said to him: It is written: Thou shalt adore the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.
Luke	Lk	49	4	9	And he brought him to Jerusalem, and set him on a pinnacle of the temple, and he said to him: If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself from hence.
Luke	Lk	49	4	10	For it is written, that He hath given his angels charge over thee, that they keep thee.
Luke	Lk	49	4	11	And that in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest perhaps thou dash thy foot against a stone.
Luke	Lk	49	4	12	And Jesus answering, said to him: It is said: Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.
Luke	Lk	49	4	13	And all the temptation being ended, the devil departed from him for a time.
Luke	Lk	49	4	14	And Jesus returned in the power of the spirit, into Galilee, and the fame of him went out through the whole country.
Luke	Lk	49	4	15	And he taught in their synagogues, and was magnified by all.
Luke	Lk	49	4	16	And he came to Nazareth, where he was brought up: and he went into the synagogue, according to his custom, on the sabbath day; and he rose up to read.
Luke	Lk	49	4	17	And the book of Isaias the prophet was delivered unto him. And as he unfolded the book, he found the place where it was written:
Luke	Lk	49	4	18	The Spirit of the Lord is upon me. Wherefore he hath anointed me to preach the gospel to the poor, he hath sent me to heal the contrite of heart,
Luke	Lk	49	4	19	To preach deliverance to the captives, and sight to the blind, to set at liberty them that are bruised, to preach the acceptable year of the Lord, and the day of reward.
Luke	Lk	49	4	20	And when he had folded the book, he restored it to the minister, and sat down. And the eyes of all in the synagogue were fixed on him.
Luke	Lk	49	4	21	And he began to say to them: This day is fulfilled this scripture in your ears.
Luke	Lk	49	4	22	And all gave testimony to him: and they wondered at the words of grace that proceeded from his mouth, and they said: Is not this the son of Joseph?
Luke	Lk	49	4	23	And he said to them: Doubtless you will say to me this similitude: Physician, heal thyself: as great things as we have heard done in Capharnaum, do also here in thy own country.
Luke	Lk	49	4	24	And he said: Amen I say to you, that no prophet is accepted in his own country.
Luke	Lk	49	4	25	In truth I say to you, there were many widows in the days of Elias in Israel, when heaven was shut up three years and six months, when there was a great famine throughout all the earth.
Luke	Lk	49	4	26	And to none of them was Elias sent, but to Sarepta of Sidon, to a widow woman.
Luke	Lk	49	4	27	And there were many lepers in Israel in the time of Eliseus the prophet: and none of them was cleansed but Naaman the Syrian.
Luke	Lk	49	4	28	And all they in the synagogue, hearing these things, were filled with anger.
Luke	Lk	49	4	29	And they rose up and thrust him out of the city; and they brought him to the brow of the hill, whereon their city was built, that they might cast him down headlong.
Luke	Lk	49	4	30	But he passing through the midst of them, went his way.
Luke	Lk	49	4	31	And he went down into Capharnaum, a city of Galilee, and there he taught them on the sabbath days.
Luke	Lk	49	4	32	And they were astonished at his doctrine: for his speech was with power.
Luke	Lk	49	4	33	And in the synagogue there was a man who had an unclean devil, and he cried out with a loud voice,
Luke	Lk	49	4	34	Saying: Let us alone, what have we to do with thee, Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the holy one of God.
Luke	Lk	49	4	35	And Jesus rebuked him, saying: Hold thy peace, and go out of him. And when the devil had thrown him into the midst, he went out of him, and hurt him not at all.
Luke	Lk	49	4	36	And there came fear upon all, and they talked among themselves, saying: What word is this, for with authority and power he commandeth the unclean spirits, and they go out?
Luke	Lk	49	4	37	And the fame of him was published into every place of the country.
Luke	Lk	49	4	38	And Jesus rising up out of the synagogue, went into Simon's house. And Simon's wife's mother was taken with a great fever, and they besought him for her.
Luke	Lk	49	4	39	And standing over her, he commanded the fever, and it left her. And immediately rising, she ministered to them.
Luke	Lk	49	4	40	And when the sun was down, all they that had any sick with divers diseases, brought them to him. But he laying his hands on every one of them, healed them.
Luke	Lk	49	4	41	And devils went out from many, crying out and saying: Thou art the Son of God. And rebuking them he suffered them not to speak, for they knew that he was Christ.
Luke	Lk	49	4	42	And when it was day, going out he went into a desert place, and the multitudes sought him, and came unto him: and they stayed him that he should not depart from them.
Luke	Lk	49	4	43	To whom he said: To other cities also I must preach the kingdom of God: for therefore am I sent.
Luke	Lk	49	4	44	And he was preaching in the synagogues of Galilee.
Luke	Lk	49	5	1	And it came to pass, that when the multitudes pressed upon him to hear the word of God, he stood by the lake of Genesareth,
Luke	Lk	49	5	2	And saw two ships standing by the lake: but the fishermen were gone out of them, and were washing their nets.
Luke	Lk	49	5	3	And going into one of the ships that was Simon's, he desired him to draw back a little from the land. And sitting he taught the multitudes out of the ship.
Luke	Lk	49	5	4	Now when he had ceased to speak, he said to Simon: Launch out into the deep, and let down your nets for a draught.
Luke	Lk	49	5	5	And Simon answering said to him: Master, we have labored all the night, and have taken nothing: but at thy word I will let down the net.
Luke	Lk	49	5	6	And when they had done this, they enclosed a very great multitude of fishes, and their net broke.
Luke	Lk	49	5	7	And they beckoned to their partners that were in the other ship, that they should come and help them. And they came, and filled both the ships, so that they were almost sinking.
Luke	Lk	49	5	8	Which when Simon Peter saw, he fell down at Jesus' knees, saying: Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, O Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	5	9	For he was wholly astonished, and all that were with him, at the draught of the fishes which they had taken.
Luke	Lk	49	5	10	And so were also James and John the sons of Zebedee, who were Simon's partners. And Jesus saith to Simon: Fear not: from henceforth thou shalt catch men.
Luke	Lk	49	5	11	And having brought their ships to land, leaving all things, they followed him.
Luke	Lk	49	5	12	And it came to pass, when he was in a certain city, behold a man full of leprosy, who seeing Jesus, and falling on his face, besought him, saying: Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.
Luke	Lk	49	5	13	And stretching forth his hand, he touched him, saying: I will. Be thou cleansed. And immediately the leprosy departed from him.
Luke	Lk	49	5	14	And he charged him that he should tell no man, but, Go, shew thyself to the priest, and offer for thy cleansing according as Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.
Luke	Lk	49	5	15	But the fame of him went abroad the more, and great multitudes came together to hear, and to be healed by him of their infirmities.
Luke	Lk	49	5	16	And he retired into the desert, and prayed.
Luke	Lk	49	5	17	And it came to pass on a certain day, as he sat teaching, that there were also Pharisees and doctors of the law sitting by, that were come out of every town of Galilee, and Judea and Jerusalem: and the power of the Lord was to heal them.
Luke	Lk	49	5	18	And behold, men brought in a bed a man, who had the palsy: and they sought means to bring him in, and to lay him before him.
Luke	Lk	49	5	19	And when they could not find by what way they might bring him in, because of the multitude, they went up upon the roof, and let him down through the tiles with his bed into the midst before Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	5	20	Whose faith when he saw, he said: Man, thy sins are forgiven thee.
Luke	Lk	49	5	21	And the scribes and Pharisees began to think, saying: Who is this who speaketh blasphemies? Who can forgive sins, but God alone?
Luke	Lk	49	5	22	And when Jesus knew their thoughts, answering, he said to them: What is it you think in your hearts?
Luke	Lk	49	5	23	Which is easier to say, Thy sins are forgiven thee; or to say, Arise and walk?
Luke	Lk	49	5	24	But that you may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins, (he saith to the sick of the palsy,) I say to thee, Arise, take up thy bed, and go into thy house.
Luke	Lk	49	5	25	And immediately rising up before them, he took up the bed on which he lay; and he went away to his own house, glorifying God.
Luke	Lk	49	5	26	And all were astonished; and they glorified God. And they were filled with fear, saying: We have seen wonderful things today.
Luke	Lk	49	5	27	And after these things he went forth, and saw a publican named Levi, sitting at the receipt of custom, and he said to him: Follow me.
Luke	Lk	49	5	28	And leaving all things, he rose up and followed him.
Luke	Lk	49	5	29	And Levi made him a great feast in his own house; and there was a great company of publicans, and of others, that were at table with them.
Luke	Lk	49	5	30	But the Pharisees and scribes murmured, saying to his disciples: Why do you eat and drink with publicans and sinners?
Luke	Lk	49	5	31	And Jesus answering, said to them: They that are whole, need not the physician: but they that are sick.
Luke	Lk	49	5	32	I came not to call the just, but sinners to penance.
Luke	Lk	49	5	33	And they said to him: Why do the disciples of John fast often, and make prayers, and the disciples of the Pharisees in like manner; but thine eat and drink?
Luke	Lk	49	5	34	To whom he said: Can you make the children of the bridegroom fast, whilst the bridegroom is with them?
Luke	Lk	49	5	35	But the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, then shall they fast in those days.
Luke	Lk	49	5	36	And he spoke also a similitude to them: That no man putteth a piece from a new garment upon an old garment; otherwise he both rendeth the new, and the piece taken from the new agreeth not with the old.
Luke	Lk	49	5	37	And no man putteth new wine into old bottles: otherwise the new wine will break the bottles, and it will be spilled, and the bottles will be lost.
Luke	Lk	49	5	38	But new wine must be put into new bottles; and both are preserved.
Luke	Lk	49	5	39	And no man drinking old, hath presently a mind to new: for he saith, The old is better.
Luke	Lk	49	6	1	And it came to pass on the second first sabbath, that as he went through the corn fields, his disciples plucked the ears, and did eat, rubbing them in their hands.
Luke	Lk	49	6	2	And some of the Pharisees said to them: Why do you that which is not lawful on the sabbath days?
Luke	Lk	49	6	3	And Jesus answering them, said: Have you not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was hungry, and they that were with him:
Luke	Lk	49	6	4	How he went into the house of God, and took and ate the bread of proposition, and gave to them that were with him, which is not lawful to eat but only for the priests?
Luke	Lk	49	6	5	And he said to them: The Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.
Luke	Lk	49	6	6	And it came to pass also on another sabbath, that he entered into the synagogue, and taught. And there was a man, whose right hand was withered.
Luke	Lk	49	6	7	And the scribes and Pharisees watched if he would heal on the sabbath; that they might find an accusation against him.
Luke	Lk	49	6	8	But he knew their thoughts; and said to the man who had the withered hand: Arise, and stand forth in the midst. And rising he stood forth.
Luke	Lk	49	6	9	Then Jesus said to them: I ask you, if it be lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil; to save life, or to destroy?
Luke	Lk	49	6	10	And looking round about on them all, he said to the man: Stretch forth thy hand. And he stretched it forth: and his hand was restored.
Luke	Lk	49	6	11	And they were filled with madness; and they talked one with another, what they might do to Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	6	12	And it came to pass in those days, that he went out into a mountain to pray, and he passed the whole night in the prayer of God.
Luke	Lk	49	6	13	And when day was come, he called unto him his disciples; and he chose twelve of them (whom also he named apostles).
Luke	Lk	49	6	14	Simon, whom he surnamed Peter, and Andrew his brother, James and John, Philip and Bartholomew,
Luke	Lk	49	6	15	Matthew and Thomas, James the son of Alpheus, and Simon who is called Zelotes,
Luke	Lk	49	6	16	And Jude, the brother of James, and Judas Iscariot, who was the traitor.
Luke	Lk	49	6	17	And coming down with them, he stood in a plain place, and the company of his disciples, and a very great multitude of people from all Judea and Jerusalem, and the sea coast both of Tyre and Sidon,
Luke	Lk	49	6	18	Who were come to hear him, and to be healed of their diseases. And they that were troubled with unclean spirits, were cured.
Luke	Lk	49	6	19	And all the multitude sought to touch him, for virtue went out from him, and healed all.
Luke	Lk	49	6	20	And he, lifting up his eyes on his disciples, said: Blessed are ye poor, for yours is the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	6	21	Blessed are ye that hunger now: for you shall be filled. Blessed are ye that weep now: for you shall laugh.
Luke	Lk	49	6	22	Blessed shall you be when men shall hate you, and when they shall separate you, and shall reproach you, and cast out your name as evil, for the Son of man's sake.
Luke	Lk	49	6	23	Be glad in that day and rejoice; for behold, your reward is great in heaven. For according to these things did their fathers to the prophets.
Luke	Lk	49	6	24	But woe to you that are rich: for you have your consolation.
Luke	Lk	49	6	25	Woe to you that are filled: for you shall hunger. Woe to you that now laugh: for you shall mourn and weep.
Luke	Lk	49	6	26	Woe to you when men shall bless you: for according to these things did their fathers to the false prophets.
Luke	Lk	49	6	27	But I say to you that hear: Love your enemies, do good to them that hate you.
Luke	Lk	49	6	28	Bless them that curse you, and pray for them that calumniate you.
Luke	Lk	49	6	29	And to him that striketh thee on the one cheek, offer also the other. And him that taketh away from thee thy cloak, forbid not to take thy coat also.
Luke	Lk	49	6	30	Give to every one that asketh thee, and of him that taketh away thy goods, ask them not again.
Luke	Lk	49	6	31	And as you would that men should do to you, do you also to them in like manner.
Luke	Lk	49	6	32	And if you love them that love you, what thanks are to you? for sinners also love those that love them.
Luke	Lk	49	6	33	And if you do good to them who do good to you, what thanks are to you? for sinners also do this.
Luke	Lk	49	6	34	And if you lend to them of whom you hope to receive, what thanks are to you? for sinners also lend to sinners, for to receive as much.
Luke	Lk	49	6	35	But love ye your enemies: do good, and lend, hoping for nothing thereby: and your reward shall be great, and you shall be the sons of the Highest; for he is kind to the unthankful, and to the evil.
Luke	Lk	49	6	36	Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.
Luke	Lk	49	6	37	Judge not, and you shall not be judged. Condemn not, and you shall not be condemned. Forgive, and you shall be forgiven.
Luke	Lk	49	6	38	Give, and it shall be given to you: good measure and pressed down and shaken together and running over shall they give into your bosom. For with the same measure that you shall mete withal, it shall be measured to you again.
Luke	Lk	49	6	39	And he spoke also to them a similitude: Can the blind lead the blind? do they not both fall into the ditch?
Luke	Lk	49	6	40	The disciple is not above his master: but every one shall be perfect, if he be as his master.
Luke	Lk	49	6	41	And why seest thou the mote in thy brother's eye: but the beam that is in thy own eye thou considerest not?
Luke	Lk	49	6	42	Or how canst thou say to thy brother: Brother, let me pull the mote out of thy eye, when thou thyself seest not the beam in thy own eye? Hypocrite, cast first the beam out of thy own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to take out the mote from thy brother's eye.
Luke	Lk	49	6	43	For there is no good tree that bringeth forth evil fruit; nor an evil tree that bringeth forth good fruit.
Luke	Lk	49	6	44	For every tree is known by its fruit. For men do not gather figs from thorns; nor from a bramble bush do they gather the grape.
Luke	Lk	49	6	45	A good man out of the good treasure of his heart bringeth forth that which is good: and an evil man out of the evil treasure bringeth forth that which is evil. For out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.
Luke	Lk	49	6	46	And why call you me, Lord, Lord; and do not the things which I say?
Luke	Lk	49	6	47	Every one that cometh to me, and heareth my words, and doth them, I will shew you to whom he is like.
Luke	Lk	49	6	48	He is like to a man building a house, who digged deep, and laid the foundation upon a rock. And when a flood came, the stream beat vehemently upon that house, and it could not shake it; for it was founded on a rock.
Luke	Lk	49	6	49	But he that heareth, and doth not, is like to a man building his house upon the earth without a foundation: against which the stream beat vehemently, and immediately it fell, and the ruin of that house was great.
Luke	Lk	49	7	1	And when he had finished all his words in the hearing of the people, he entered into Capharnaum.
Luke	Lk	49	7	2	And the servant of a certain centurion, who was dear to him, being sick, was ready to die.
Luke	Lk	49	7	3	And when he had heard of Jesus, he sent unto him the ancients of the Jews, desiring him to come and heal his servant.
Luke	Lk	49	7	4	And when they came to Jesus, they besought him earnestly, saying to him: He is worthy that thou shouldest do this for him.
Luke	Lk	49	7	5	For he loveth our nation; and he hath built us a synagogue.
Luke	Lk	49	7	6	And Jesus went with them. And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent his friends to him, saying: Lord, trouble not thyself; for I am not worthy that thou shouldest enter under my roof.
Luke	Lk	49	7	7	For which cause neither did I think myself worthy to come to thee; but say the word, and my servant shall be healed.
Luke	Lk	49	7	8	For I also am a man subject to authority, having under me soldiers: and I say to one, Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doth it.
Luke	Lk	49	7	9	Which Jesus hearing, marvelled: and turning about to the multitude that followed him, he said: Amen I say to you, I have not found so great faith, not even in Israel.
Luke	Lk	49	7	10	And they who were sent, being returned to the house, found the servant whole who had been sick.
Luke	Lk	49	7	11	And it came to pass afterwards, that he went into a city that is called Naim; and there went with him his disciples, and a great multitude.
Luke	Lk	49	7	12	And when he came nigh to the gate of the city, behold a dead man was carried out, the only son of his mother; and she was a widow: and a great multitude of the city was with her.
Luke	Lk	49	7	13	Whom when the Lord had seen, being moved with mercy towards her, he said to her: Weep not.
Luke	Lk	49	7	14	And he came near and touched the bier. And they that carried it, stood still. And he said: Young man, I say to thee, arise.
Luke	Lk	49	7	15	And he that was dead, sat up, and began to speak. And he gave him to his mother.
Luke	Lk	49	7	16	And there came a fear on them all: and they glorified God, saying: A great prophet is risen up among us: and, God hath visited his people.
Luke	Lk	49	7	17	And this rumour of him went forth throughout all Judea, and throughout all the country round about.
Luke	Lk	49	7	18	And John's disciples told him of all these things.
Luke	Lk	49	7	19	And John called to him two of his disciples, and sent them to Jesus, saying: Art thou he that art to come; or look we for another?
Luke	Lk	49	7	20	And when the men were come unto him, they said: John the Baptist hath sent us to thee, saying: Art thou he that art to come; or look we for another?
Luke	Lk	49	7	21	(And in that same hour, he cured many of their diseases, and hurts, and evil spirits: and to many that were blind he gave sight.)
Luke	Lk	49	7	22	And answering, he said to them: Go and relate to John what you have heard and seen: the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are made clean, the deaf hear, the dead rise again, to the poor the gospel is preached:
Luke	Lk	49	7	23	And blessed is he whosoever shall not be scandalized in me.
Luke	Lk	49	7	24	And when the messengers of John were departed, he began to speak to the multitudes concerning John. What went ye out into the desert to see? a reed shaken with the wind?
Luke	Lk	49	7	25	But what went you out to see? a man clothed in soft garments? Behold they that are in costly apparel and live delicately, are in the houses of kings.
Luke	Lk	49	7	26	But what went you out to see? a prophet? Yea, I say to you, and more than a prophet.
Luke	Lk	49	7	27	This is he of whom it is written: Behold I send my angel before thy face, who shall prepare thy way before thee.
Luke	Lk	49	7	28	For I say to you: Amongst those that are born of women, there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist. But he that is the lesser in the kingdom of God, is greater than he.
Luke	Lk	49	7	29	And all the people hearing, and the publicans, justified God, being baptized with John's baptism.
Luke	Lk	49	7	30	But the Pharisees and the lawyers despised the counsel of God against themselves, being not baptized by him.
Luke	Lk	49	7	31	And the Lord said: Whereunto then shall I liken the men of this generation? and to what are they like?
Luke	Lk	49	7	32	They are like to children sitting in the marketplace, and speaking one to another, and saying: We have piped to you, and you have not danced: we have mourned, and you have not wept.
Luke	Lk	49	7	33	For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine; and you say: He hath a devil.
Luke	Lk	49	7	34	The Son of man is come eating and drinking: and you say: Behold a man that is a glutton and a drinker of wine, a friend of publicans and sinners.
Luke	Lk	49	7	35	And wisdom is justified by all her children.
Luke	Lk	49	7	36	And one of the Pharisees desired him to eat with him. And he went into the house of the Pharisee, and sat down to meat.
Luke	Lk	49	7	37	And behold a woman that was in the city, a sinner, when she knew that he sat at meat in the Pharisee's house, brought an alabaster box of ointment;
Luke	Lk	49	7	38	And standing behind at his feet, she began to wash his feet, with tears, and wiped them with the hairs of her head, and kissed his feet, and anointed them with the ointment.
Luke	Lk	49	7	39	And the Pharisee, who had invited him, seeing it, spoke within himself, saying: This man, if he were a prophet, would know surely who and what manner of woman this is that toucheth him, that she is a sinner.
Luke	Lk	49	7	40	And Jesus answering, said to him: Simon, I have somewhat to say to thee. But he said: Master, say it.
Luke	Lk	49	7	41	A certain creditor had two debtors, the one who owed five hundred pence, and the other fifty.
Luke	Lk	49	7	42	And whereas they had not wherewith to pay, he forgave them both. Which therefore of the two loveth him most?
Luke	Lk	49	7	43	Simon answering, said: I suppose that he to whom he forgave most. And he said to him: Thou hast judged rightly.
Luke	Lk	49	7	44	And turning to the woman, he said unto Simon: Dost thou see this woman? I entered into thy house, thou gavest me no water for my feet; but she with tears hath washed my feet, and with her hairs hath wiped them.
Luke	Lk	49	7	45	Thou gavest me no kiss; but she, since she came in, hath not ceased to kiss my feet.
Luke	Lk	49	7	46	My head with oil thou didst not anoint; but she with ointment hath anointed my feet.
Luke	Lk	49	7	47	Wherefore I say to thee: Many sins are forgiven her, because she hath loved much. But to whom less is forgiven, he loveth less.
Luke	Lk	49	7	48	And he said to her: Thy sins are forgiven thee.
Luke	Lk	49	7	49	And they that sat at meat with him began to say within themselves: Who is this that forgiveth sins also?
Luke	Lk	49	7	50	And he said to the woman: Thy faith hath made thee safe, go in peace.
Luke	Lk	49	8	1	And it came to pass afterwards, that he travelled through the cities and towns, preaching and evangelizing the kingdom of God; and the twelve with him:
Luke	Lk	49	8	2	And certain women who had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities; Mary who is called Magdalen, out of whom seven devils were gone forth,
Luke	Lk	49	8	3	And Joanna the wife of Chusa, Herod's steward, and Susanna, and many others who ministered unto him of their substance.
Luke	Lk	49	8	4	And when a very great multitude was gathered together, and hastened out of the cities unto him, he spoke by a similitude.
Luke	Lk	49	8	5	The sower went out to sow his seed. And as he sowed, some fell by the way side, and it was trodden down, and the fowls of the air devoured it.
Luke	Lk	49	8	6	And other some fell upon a rock: and as soon as it was sprung up, it withered away, because it had no moisture.
Luke	Lk	49	8	7	And other some fell among thorns, and the thorns growing up with it, choked it.
Luke	Lk	49	8	8	And other some fell upon good ground; and being sprung up, yielded fruit a hundredfold. Saying these things, he cried out: He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.
Luke	Lk	49	8	9	And his disciples asked him what this parable might be.
Luke	Lk	49	8	10	To whom he said: To you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God; but to the rest in parables, that seeing they may not see, and hearing may not understand.
Luke	Lk	49	8	11	Now the parable is this: The seed is the word of God.
Luke	Lk	49	8	12	And they by the way side are they that hear; then the devil cometh, and taketh the word out of their heart, lest believing they should be saved.
Luke	Lk	49	8	13	Now they upon the rock, are they who when they hear, receive the word with joy: and these have no roots; for they believe for a while, and in time of temptation, they fall away.
Luke	Lk	49	8	14	And that which fell among thorns, are they who have heard, and going their way, are choked with the cares and riches and pleasures of this life, and yield no fruit.
Luke	Lk	49	8	15	But that on the good ground, are they who in a good and perfect heart, hearing the word, keep it, and bring forth fruit in patience.
Luke	Lk	49	8	16	Now no man lighting a candle covereth it with a vessel, or putteth it under a bed; but setteth it upon a candlestick, that they who come in may see the light.
Luke	Lk	49	8	17	For there is not any thing secret that shall not be made manifest, nor hidden, that shall not be known and come abroad.
Luke	Lk	49	8	18	Take heed therefore how you hear. For whosoever hath, to him shall be given: and whosoever hath not, that also which he thinketh he hath, shall be taken away from him.
Luke	Lk	49	8	19	And his mother and brethren came unto him; and they could not come at him for the crowd.
Luke	Lk	49	8	20	And it was told him: Thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to see thee.
Luke	Lk	49	8	21	Who answering, said to them: My mother and my brethren are they who hear the word of God, and do it.
Luke	Lk	49	8	22	And it came to pass on a certain day that he went into a little ship with his disciples, and he said to them: Let us go over to the other side of the lake. And they launched forth.
Luke	Lk	49	8	23	And when they were sailing, he slept; and there came down a storm of wind upon the lake, and they were filled, and were in danger.
Luke	Lk	49	8	24	And they came and awaked him, saying: Master, we perish. But he arising, rebuked the wind and the rage of the water; and it ceased, and there was a calm.
Luke	Lk	49	8	25	And he said to them: Where is your faith? Who being afraid, wondered, saying one to another: Who is this, (think you), that he commandeth both the winds and the sea, and they obey him?
Luke	Lk	49	8	26	And they sailed to the country of the Gerasens, which is over against Galilee.
Luke	Lk	49	8	27	And when he was come forth to the land, there met him a certain man who had a devil now a very long time, and he wore no clothes, neither did he abide in a house, but in the sepulchres.
Luke	Lk	49	8	28	And when he saw Jesus, he fell down before him; and crying out with a loud voice, he said: What have I to do with thee, Jesus, Son of the most high God? I beseech thee, do not torment me.
Luke	Lk	49	8	29	For he commanded the unclean spirit to go out of the man. For many times it seized him, and he was bound with chains, and kept in fetters; and breaking the bonds, he was driven by the devil into the deserts.
Luke	Lk	49	8	30	And Jesus asked him, saying: What is thy name? But he said: Legion; because many devils were entered into him.
Luke	Lk	49	8	31	And they besought him that he would not command them to go into the abyss.
Luke	Lk	49	8	32	And there was there a herd of many swine feeding on the mountain; and they besought him that he would suffer them to enter into them. And he suffered them.
Luke	Lk	49	8	33	The devils therefore went out of the man, and entered into the swine; and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the lake, and were stifled.
Luke	Lk	49	8	34	Which when they that fed them saw done, they fled away, and told it in the city and in the villages.
Luke	Lk	49	8	35	And they went out to see what was done; and they came to Jesus, and found the man, out of whom the devils were departed, sitting at his feet, clothed, and in his right mind; and they were afraid.
Luke	Lk	49	8	36	And they also that had seen, told them how he had been healed from the legion.
Luke	Lk	49	8	37	And all the multitude of the country of the Gerasens besought him to depart from them; for they were taken with great fear. And he, going up into the ship, returned back again.
Luke	Lk	49	8	38	Now the man, out of whom the devils were departed, besought him that he might be with him. But Jesus sent him away, saying:
Luke	Lk	49	8	39	Return to thy house, and tell how great things God hath done to thee. And he went through the whole city, publishing how great things Jesus had done to him.
Luke	Lk	49	8	40	And it came to pass, that when Jesus was returned, the multitude received him: for they were all waiting for him.
Luke	Lk	49	8	41	And behold there came a man whose name was Jairus, and he was a ruler of the synagogue: and he fell down at the feet of Jesus, beseeching him that he would come into his house:
Luke	Lk	49	8	42	For he had an only daughter, almost twelve years old, and she was dying. And it happened as he went, that he was thronged by the multitudes.
Luke	Lk	49	8	43	And there was a certain woman having an issue of blood twelve years, who had bestowed all her substance on physicians, and could not be healed by any.
Luke	Lk	49	8	44	She came behind him, and touched the hem of his garment; and immediately the issue of her blood stopped.
Luke	Lk	49	8	45	And Jesus said: Who is it that touched me? And all denying, Peter and they that were with him said: Master, the multitudes throng and press thee, and dost thou say, Who touched me?
Luke	Lk	49	8	46	And Jesus said: Somebody hath touched me; for I know that virtue is gone out from me.
Luke	Lk	49	8	47	And the woman seeing that she was not hid, came trembling, and fell down before his feet, and declared before all the people for what cause she had touched him, and how she was immediately healed.
Luke	Lk	49	8	48	But he said to her: Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go thy way in peace.
Luke	Lk	49	8	49	As he was yet speaking, there cometh one to the ruler of the synagogue, saying to him: Thy daughter is dead, trouble him not.
Luke	Lk	49	8	50	And Jesus hearing this word, answered the father of the maid: Fear not; believe only, and she shall be safe.
Luke	Lk	49	8	51	And when he was come to the house, he suffered not any man to go in with him, but Peter and James and John, and the father and mother of the maiden.
Luke	Lk	49	8	52	And all wept and mourned for her. But he said: Weep not; the maid is not dead, but sleepeth.
Luke	Lk	49	8	53	And they laughed him to scorn, knowing that she was dead.
Luke	Lk	49	8	54	But he taking her by the hand, cried out, saying: Maid, arise.
Luke	Lk	49	8	55	And her spirit returned, and she arose immediately. And he bid them give her to eat.
Luke	Lk	49	8	56	And her parents were astonished, whom he charged to tell no man what was done.
Luke	Lk	49	9	1	Then calling together the twelve apostles, he gave them power and authority over all devils, and to cure diseases.
Luke	Lk	49	9	2	And he sent them to preach the kingdom of God, and to heal the sick.
Luke	Lk	49	9	3	And he said to them: Take nothing for your journey; neither staff, nor scrip, nor bread, nor money; neither have two coats.
Luke	Lk	49	9	4	And whatsoever house you shall enter into, abide there, and depart not from thence.
Luke	Lk	49	9	5	And whosoever will not receive you, when ye go out of that city, shake off even the dust of your feet, for a testimony against them.
Luke	Lk	49	9	6	And going out, they went about through the towns, preaching the gospel, and healing everywhere.
Luke	Lk	49	9	7	Now Herod, the tetrarch, heard of all things that were done by him; and he was in a doubt, because it was said
Luke	Lk	49	9	8	By some, that John was risen from the dead: but by other some, that Elias had appeared; and by others, that one of the old prophets was risen again.
Luke	Lk	49	9	9	And Herod said: John I have beheaded; but who is this of whom I hear such things? And he sought to see him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	10	And the apostles, when they were returned, told him all they had done. And taking them, he went aside into a desert place, apart, which belongeth to Bethsaida.
Luke	Lk	49	9	11	Which when the people knew, they followed him; and he received them, and spoke to them of the kingdom of God, and healed them who had need of healing.
Luke	Lk	49	9	12	Now the day began to decline. And the twelve came and said to him: Send away the multitude, that going into the towns and villages round about, they may lodge and get victuals; for we are here in a desert place.
Luke	Lk	49	9	13	But he said to them: Give you them to eat. And they said: We have no more than five loaves and two fishes; unless perhaps we should go and buy food for all this multitude.
Luke	Lk	49	9	14	Now there were about five thousand men. And he said to his disciples: Make them sit down by fifties in a company.
Luke	Lk	49	9	15	And they did so; and made them all sit down.
Luke	Lk	49	9	16	And taking the five loaves and the two fishes, he looked up to heaven, and blessed them; and he broke, and distributed to his disciples, to set before the multitude.
Luke	Lk	49	9	17	And they did all eat, and were filled. And there were taken up of fragments that remained to them, twelve baskets.
Luke	Lk	49	9	18	And it came to pass, as he was alone praying, his disciples also were with him: and he asked them, saying: Whom do the people say that I am?
Luke	Lk	49	9	19	But they answered, and said: John the Baptist; but some say Elias; and others say that one of the former prophets is risen again.
Luke	Lk	49	9	20	And he said to them: But whom do you say that I am? Simon Peter answering, said: The Christ of God.
Luke	Lk	49	9	21	But he strictly charging them, commanded they should tell this to no man.
Luke	Lk	49	9	22	Saying: The Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected by the ancients and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and the third day rise again.
Luke	Lk	49	9	23	And he said to all: If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me.
Luke	Lk	49	9	24	For whosoever will save his life, shall lose it; for he that shall lose his life for my sake, shall save it.
Luke	Lk	49	9	25	For what is a man advantaged, if he gain the whole world, and lose himself, and cast away himself?
Luke	Lk	49	9	26	For he that shall be ashamed of me and of my words, of him the Son of man shall be ashamed, when he shall come in his majesty, and that of his Father, and of the holy angels.
Luke	Lk	49	9	27	But I tell you of a truth: There are some standing here that shall not taste death, till they see the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	9	28	And it came to pass about eight days after these words, that he took Peter, and James, and John, and went up into a mountain to pray.
Luke	Lk	49	9	29	And whilst he prayed, the shape of his countenance was altered, and his raiment became white and glittering.
Luke	Lk	49	9	30	And behold two men were talking with him. And they were Moses and Elias,
Luke	Lk	49	9	31	Appearing in majesty. And they spoke of his decease that he should accomplish in Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	9	32	But Peter and they that were with him were heavy with sleep. And waking, they saw his glory, and the two men that stood with him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	33	And it came to pass, that as they were departing from him, Peter saith to Jesus: Master, it is good for us to be here; and let us make three tabernacles, one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias; not knowing what he said.
Luke	Lk	49	9	34	And as he spoke these things, there came a cloud, and overshadowed them; and they were afraid, when they entered into the cloud.
Luke	Lk	49	9	35	And a voice came out of the cloud, saying: This is my beloved Son; hear him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	36	And whilst the voice was uttered, Jesus was found alone. And they held their peace, and told no man in those days any of these things which they had seen.
Luke	Lk	49	9	37	And it came to pass the day following, when they came down from the mountain, there met him a great multitude.
Luke	Lk	49	9	38	And behold a man among the crowd cried out, saying: Master, I beseech thee, look upon my son, because he is my only one.
Luke	Lk	49	9	39	And lo, a spirit seizeth him, and he suddenly crieth out, and he throweth him down and teareth him, so that he foameth; and bruising him, he hardly departeth from him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	40	And I desired thy disciples to cast him out, and they could not.
Luke	Lk	49	9	41	And Jesus answering, said: O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you, and suffer you? Bring hither thy son.
Luke	Lk	49	9	42	And as he was coming to him, the devil threw him down, and tore him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	43	And Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, and cured the boy, and restored him to his father.
Luke	Lk	49	9	44	And all were astonished at the mighty power of God. But while all wondered at all the things he did, he said to his disciples: Lay you up in your hearts these words, for it shall come to pass, that the Son of man shall be delivered into the hands of men.
Luke	Lk	49	9	45	But they understood not this word; and it was hid from them, so that they perceived it not. And they were afraid to ask him concerning this word.
Luke	Lk	49	9	46	And there entered a thought into them, which of them should be greater.
Luke	Lk	49	9	47	But Jesus seeing the thoughts of their heart, took a child and set him by him,
Luke	Lk	49	9	48	And said to them: Whosoever shall receive this child in my name, receiveth me; and whosoever shall receive me, receiveth him that sent me. For he that is the lesser among you all, he is the greater.
Luke	Lk	49	9	49	And John, answering, said: Master, we saw a certain man casting out devils in thy name, and we forbade him, because he followeth not with us.
Luke	Lk	49	9	50	And Jesus said to him: Forbid him not; for he that is not against you, is for you.
Luke	Lk	49	9	51	And it came to pass, when the days of his assumption were accomplishing, that he steadfastly set his face to go to Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	9	52	And he sent messengers before his face; and going, they entered into a city of the Samaritans, to prepare for him.
Luke	Lk	49	9	53	And they received him not, because his face was of one going to Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	9	54	And when his disciples James and John had seen this, they said: Lord, wilt thou that we command fire to come down from heaven, and consume them?
Luke	Lk	49	9	55	And turning, he rebuked them, saying: You know not of what spirit you are.
Luke	Lk	49	9	56	The Son of man came not to destroy souls, but to save. And they went into another town.
Luke	Lk	49	9	57	And it came to pass, as they walked in the way, that a certain man said to him: I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.
Luke	Lk	49	9	58	Jesus said to him: The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head.
Luke	Lk	49	9	59	But he said to another: Follow me. And he said: Lord, suffer me first to go, and to bury my father.
Luke	Lk	49	9	60	And Jesus said to him: Let the dead bury their dead: but go thou, and preach the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	9	61	And another said: I will follow thee, Lord; but let me first take my leave of them that are at my house.
Luke	Lk	49	9	62	Jesus said to him: No man putting his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	10	1	And after these things the Lord appointed also other seventy-two: and he sent them two and two before his face into every city and place whither he himself was to come.
Luke	Lk	49	10	2	And he said to them: The harvest indeed is great, but the labourers are few. Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he send labourers into his harvest.
Luke	Lk	49	10	3	Go: Behold I send you as lambs among wolves.
Luke	Lk	49	10	4	Carry neither purse, nor scrip, nor shoes; and salute no man by the way.
Luke	Lk	49	10	5	Into whatsoever house you enter, first say: Peace be to this house.
Luke	Lk	49	10	6	And if the son of peace be there, your peace shall rest upon him; but if not, it shall return to you.
Luke	Lk	49	10	7	And in the same house, remain, eating and drinking such things as they have: for the labourer is worthy of his hire. Remove not from house to house.
Luke	Lk	49	10	8	And into what city soever you enter, and they receive you, eat such things as are set before you.
Luke	Lk	49	10	9	And heal the sick that are therein, and say to them: The kingdom of God is come nigh unto you.
Luke	Lk	49	10	10	But into whatsoever city you enter, and they receive you not, going forth into the streets thereof, say:
Luke	Lk	49	10	11	Even the very dust of your city that cleaveth to us, we wipe off against you. Yet know this, that the kingdom of God is at hand.
Luke	Lk	49	10	12	I say to you, it shall be more tolerable at that day for Sodom, than for that city.
Luke	Lk	49	10	13	Woe to thee, Corozain, woe to thee, Bethsaida. For if in Tyre and Sidon had been wrought the mighty works that have been wrought in you, they would have done penance long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes.
Luke	Lk	49	10	14	But it shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment, than for you.
Luke	Lk	49	10	15	And thou, Capharnaum, which art exalted unto heaven, thou shalt be thrust down to hell.
Luke	Lk	49	10	16	He that heareth you, heareth me; and he that despiseth you, despiseth me; and he that despiseth me, despiseth him that sent me.
Luke	Lk	49	10	17	And the seventy-two returned with joy, saying: Lord, the devils also are subject to us in thy name.
Luke	Lk	49	10	18	And he said to them: I saw Satan like lightning falling from heaven.
Luke	Lk	49	10	19	Behold, I have given you power to tread upon serpents and scorpions, and upon all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall hurt you.
Luke	Lk	49	10	20	But yet rejoice not in this, that spirits are subject unto you; but rejoice in this, that your names are written in heaven.
Luke	Lk	49	10	21	In that same hour, he rejoiced in the Holy Ghost, and said: I confess to thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hidden these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them to little ones. Yea, Father, for so it hath seemed good in thy sight.
Luke	Lk	49	10	22	All things are delivered to me by my Father; and no one knoweth who the Son is, but the Father; and who the Father is, but the Son, and to whom the Son will reveal him.
Luke	Lk	49	10	23	And turning to his disciples, he said: Blessed are the eyes that see the things which you see.
Luke	Lk	49	10	24	For I say to you, that many prophets and kings have desired to see the things that you see, and have not seen them; and to hear the things that you hear, and have not heard them.
Luke	Lk	49	10	25	And behold a certain lawyer stood up, tempting him, and saying, Master, what must I do to possess eternal life?
Luke	Lk	49	10	26	But he said to him: What is written in the law? how readest thou?
Luke	Lk	49	10	27	He answering, said: Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with thy whole heart, and with thy whole soul, and with all thy strength, and with all thy mind: and thy neighbour as thyself.
Luke	Lk	49	10	28	And he said to him: Thou hast answered right: this do, and thou shalt live.
Luke	Lk	49	10	29	But he willing to justify himself, said to Jesus: And who is my neighbour?
Luke	Lk	49	10	30	And Jesus answering, said: A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and fell among robbers, who also stripped him, and having wounded him went away, leaving him half dead.
Luke	Lk	49	10	31	And it chanced, that a certain priest went down the same way: and seeing him, passed by.
Luke	Lk	49	10	32	In like manner also a Levite, when he was near the place and saw him, passed by.
Luke	Lk	49	10	33	But a certain Samaritan being on his journey, came near him; and seeing him, was moved with compassion.
Luke	Lk	49	10	34	And going up to him, bound up his wounds, pouring in oil and wine: and setting him upon his own beast, brought him to an inn, and took care of him.
Luke	Lk	49	10	35	And the next day he took out two pence, and gave to the host, and said: Take care of him; and whatsoever thou shalt spend over and above, I, at my return, will repay thee.
Luke	Lk	49	10	36	Which of these three, in thy opinion, was neighbour to him that fell among the robbers?
Luke	Lk	49	10	37	But he said: He that shewed mercy to him. And Jesus said to him: Go, and do thou in like manner.
Luke	Lk	49	10	38	Now it came to pass as they went, that he entered into a certain town: and a certain woman named Martha, received him into her house.
Luke	Lk	49	10	39	And she had a sister called Mary, who sitting also at the Lord's feet, heard his word.
Luke	Lk	49	10	40	But Martha was busy about much serving. Who stood and said: Lord, hast thou no care that my sister hath left me alone to serve? speak to her therefore, that she help me.
Luke	Lk	49	10	41	And the Lord answering, said to her: Martha, Martha, thou art careful, and art troubled about many things:
Luke	Lk	49	10	42	But one thing is necessary. Mary hath chosen the best part, which shall not be taken away from her.
Luke	Lk	49	11	1	And it came to pass, that as he was in a certain place praying, when he ceased, one of his disciples said to him: Lord, teach us to pray, as John also taught his disciples.
Luke	Lk	49	11	2	And he said to them: When you pray, say: Father, hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come.
Luke	Lk	49	11	3	Give us this day our daily bread.
Luke	Lk	49	11	4	And forgive us our sins, for we also forgive every one that is indebted to us. And lead us not into temptation.
Luke	Lk	49	11	5	And he said to them: Which of you shall have a friend, and shall go to him at midnight, and shall say to him: Friend, lend me three loaves,
Luke	Lk	49	11	6	Because a friend of mine is come off his journey to me, and I have not what to set before him.
Luke	Lk	49	11	7	And he from within should answer, and say: Trouble me not, the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed; I cannot rise and give thee.
Luke	Lk	49	11	8	Yet if he shall continue knocking, I say to you, although he will not rise and give him, because he is his friend; yet, because of his importunity, he will rise, and give him as many as he needeth.
Luke	Lk	49	11	9	And I say to you, Ask, and it shall be given you: seek, and you shall find: knock, and it shall be opened to you.
Luke	Lk	49	11	10	For every one that asketh, receiveth; and he that seeketh, findeth; and to him that knocketh, it shall be opened.
Luke	Lk	49	11	11	And which of you, if he ask his father bread, will he give him a stone? or a fish, will he for a fish give him a serpent?
Luke	Lk	49	11	12	Or if he shall ask an egg, will he reach him a scorpion?
Luke	Lk	49	11	13	If you then, being evil, know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father from heaven give the good Spirit to them that ask him?
Luke	Lk	49	11	14	And he was casting out a devil, and the same was dumb: and when he had cast out the devil, the dumb spoke: and the multitudes were in admiration at it:
Luke	Lk	49	11	15	But some of them said: He casteth out devils by Beelzebub, the prince of devils.
Luke	Lk	49	11	16	And others tempting, asked of him a sign from heaven.
Luke	Lk	49	11	17	But he seeing their thoughts, said to them: Every kingdom divided against itself, shall be brought to desolation, and house upon house shall fall.
Luke	Lk	49	11	18	And if Satan also be divided against himself, how shall his kingdom stand? because you say, that through Beelzebub I cast out devils.
Luke	Lk	49	11	19	Now if I cast out devils by Beelzebub; by whom do your children cast them out? Therefore they shall be your judges.
Luke	Lk	49	11	20	But if I by the finger of God cast out devils; doubtless the kingdom of God is come upon you.
Luke	Lk	49	11	21	When a strong man armed keepeth his court, those things are in peace which he possesseth.
Luke	Lk	49	11	22	But if a stronger than he come upon him, and overcome him; he will take away all his armour wherein he trusted, and will distribute his spoils.
Luke	Lk	49	11	23	He that is not with me, is against me; and he that gathereth not with me, scattereth.
Luke	Lk	49	11	24	When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through places without water, seeking rest; and not finding, he saith: I will return into my house whence I came out.
Luke	Lk	49	11	25	And when he is come, he findeth it swept and garnished.
Luke	Lk	49	11	26	Then he goeth and taketh with him seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and entering in they dwell there. And the last state of that man becomes worse than the first.
Luke	Lk	49	11	27	And it came to pass, as he spoke these things, a certain woman from the crowd, lifting up her voice, said to him: Blessed is the womb that bore thee, and the paps that gave thee suck.
Luke	Lk	49	11	28	But he said: Yea rather, blessed are they who hear the word of God, and keep it.
Luke	Lk	49	11	29	And the multitudes running together, he began to say: This generation is a wicked generation: it asketh a sign, and a sign shall not be given it, but the sign of Jonas the prophet.
Luke	Lk	49	11	30	For as Jonas was a sign to the Ninivites; so shall the Son of man also be to this generation.
Luke	Lk	49	11	31	The queen of the south shall rise in the judgment with the men of this generation, and shall condemn them: because she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold more than Solomon here.
Luke	Lk	49	11	32	The men of Ninive shall rise in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it; because they did penance at the preaching of Jonas; and behold more than Jonas here.
Luke	Lk	49	11	33	No man lighteth a candle, and putteth it in a hidden place, nor under a bushel; but upon a candlestick, that they that come in, may see the light.
Luke	Lk	49	11	34	The light of thy body is thy eye. If thy eye be single, thy whole body will be lightsome: but if it be evil, thy body also will be darksome.
Luke	Lk	49	11	35	Take heed therefore, that the light which is in thee, be not darkness.
Luke	Lk	49	11	36	If then thy whole body be lightsome, having no part of darkness; the whole shall be lightsome; and as a bright lamp, shall enlighten thee.
Luke	Lk	49	11	37	And as he was speaking, a certain Pharisee prayed him, that he would dine with him. And he going in, sat down to eat.
Luke	Lk	49	11	38	And the Pharisee began to say, thinking within himself, why he was not washed before dinner.
Luke	Lk	49	11	39	And the Lord said to him: Now you Pharisees make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter; but your inside is full of rapine and iniquity.
Luke	Lk	49	11	40	Ye fools, did not he that made that which is without, make also that which is within?
Luke	Lk	49	11	41	But yet that which remaineth, give alms; and behold, all things are clean unto you.
Luke	Lk	49	11	42	But woe to you, Pharisees, because you tithe mint and rue and every herb; and pass over judgment, and the charity of God. Now these things you ought to have done, and not to leave the other undone.
Luke	Lk	49	11	43	Woe to you, Pharisees, because you love the uppermost seats in the synagogues, and salutations in the marketplace.
Luke	Lk	49	11	44	Woe to you, because you are as sepulchres that appear not, and men that walk over are not aware.
Luke	Lk	49	11	45	And one of the lawyers answering, saith to him: Master, in saying these things, thou reproachest us also.
Luke	Lk	49	11	46	But he said: Woe to you lawyers also, because you load men with burdens which they cannot bear, and you yourselves touch not the packs with one of your fingers.
Luke	Lk	49	11	47	Woe to you who build the monuments of the prophets: and your fathers killed them.
Luke	Lk	49	11	48	Truly you bear witness that you consent to the doings of your fathers: for they indeed killed them, and you build their sepulchres.
Luke	Lk	49	11	49	For this cause also the wisdom of God said: I will send to them prophets and apostles; and some of them they will kill and persecute.
Luke	Lk	49	11	50	That the blood of all the prophets which was shed from the foundation of the world, may be required of this generation,
Luke	Lk	49	11	51	From the blood of Abel unto the blood of Zacharias, who was slain between the altar and the temple: Yea I say to you, It shall be required of this generation.
Luke	Lk	49	11	52	Woe to you lawyers, for you have taken away the key of knowledge: you yourselves have not entered in, and those that were entering in, you have hindered.
Luke	Lk	49	11	53	And as he was saying these things to them, the Pharisees and the lawyers began violently to urge him, and to oppress his mouth about many things,
Luke	Lk	49	11	54	Lying in wait for him, and seeking to catch something from his mouth, that they might accuse him.
Luke	Lk	49	12	1	And when great multitudes stood about him, so that they trod one upon another, he began to say to his disciples: Beware ye of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.
Luke	Lk	49	12	2	For there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed: nor hidden, that shall not be known.
Luke	Lk	49	12	3	For whatsoever things you have spoken in darkness, shall be published in the light: and that which you have spoken in the ear in the chambers, shall be preached on the housetops.
Luke	Lk	49	12	4	And I say to you, my friends: Be not afraid of them who kill the body, and after that have no more that they can do.
Luke	Lk	49	12	5	But I will shew you whom you shall fear: fear ye him, who after he hath killed, hath power to cast into hell. Yea, I say to you, fear him.
Luke	Lk	49	12	6	Are not five sparrows sold for two farthings, and not one of them is forgotten before God?
Luke	Lk	49	12	7	Yea, the very hairs of your head are all numbered. Fear not therefore: you are of more value than many sparrows.
Luke	Lk	49	12	8	And I say to you, Whosoever shall confess me before men, him shall the Son of man also confess before the angels of God.
Luke	Lk	49	12	9	But he that shall deny me before men, shall be denied before the angels of God.
Luke	Lk	49	12	10	And whosoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but to him that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven.
Luke	Lk	49	12	11	And when they shall bring you into the synagogues, and to magistrates and powers, be not solicitous how or what you shall answer, or what you shall say;
Luke	Lk	49	12	12	For the Holy Ghost shall teach you in the same hour what you must say.
Luke	Lk	49	12	13	And one of the multitude said to him: Master, speak to my brother that he divide the inheritance with me.
Luke	Lk	49	12	14	But he said to him: Man, who hath appointed me judge, or divider, over you?
Luke	Lk	49	12	15	And he said to them: Take heed and beware of all covetousness; for a man's life doth not consist in the abundance of things which he possesseth.
Luke	Lk	49	12	16	And he spoke a similitude to them, saying: The land of a certain rich man brought forth plenty of fruits.
Luke	Lk	49	12	17	And he thought within himself, saying: What shall I do, because I have no room where to bestow my fruits?
Luke	Lk	49	12	18	And he said: This will I do: I will pull down my barns, and will build greater; and into them will I gather all things that are grown to me, and my goods.
Luke	Lk	49	12	19	And I will say to my soul: Soul, thou hast much goods laid up for many years take thy rest; eat, drink, make good cheer.
Luke	Lk	49	12	20	But God said to him: Thou fool, this night do they require thy soul of thee: and whose shall those things be which thou hast provided?
Luke	Lk	49	12	21	So is he that layeth up treasure for himself, and is not rich towards God.
Luke	Lk	49	12	22	And he said to his disciples: Therefore I say to you, be not solicitous for your life, what you shall eat; nor for your body, what you shall put on.
Luke	Lk	49	12	23	The life is more than the meat, and the body is more than the raiment.
Luke	Lk	49	12	24	Consider the ravens, for they sow not, neither do they reap, neither have they storehouse nor barn, and God feedeth them. How much are you more valuable than they?
Luke	Lk	49	12	25	And which of you, by taking thought, can add to his stature one cubit?
Luke	Lk	49	12	26	If then ye be not able to do so much as the least thing, why are you solicitous for the rest?
Luke	Lk	49	12	27	Consider the lilies, how they grow: they labour not, neither do they spin. But I say to you, not even Solomon in all his glory was clothed like one of these.
Luke	Lk	49	12	28	Now if God clothe in this manner the grass that is today in the field, and tomorrow is cast into the oven; how much more you, O ye of little faith?
Luke	Lk	49	12	29	And seek not you what you shall eat, or what you shall drink: and be not lifted up on high.
Luke	Lk	49	12	30	For all these things do the nations of the world seek. But your Father knoweth that you have need of these things.
Luke	Lk	49	12	31	But seek ye first the kingdom of God and his justice, and all these things shall be added unto you.
Luke	Lk	49	12	32	Fear not, little flock, for it hath pleased your Father to give you a kingdom.
Luke	Lk	49	12	33	Sell what you possess and give alms. Make to yourselves bags which grow not old, a treasure in heaven which faileth not: where no thief approacheth, nor moth corrupteth.
Luke	Lk	49	12	34	For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.
Luke	Lk	49	12	35	Let your loins be girt, and lamps burning in your hands.
Luke	Lk	49	12	36	And you yourselves like to men who wait for their lord, when he shall return from the wedding; that when he cometh and knocketh, they may open to him immediately.
Luke	Lk	49	12	37	Blessed are those servants, whom the Lord when he cometh, shall find watching. Amen I say to you, that he will gird himself, and make them sit down to meat, and passing will minister unto them.
Luke	Lk	49	12	38	And if he shall come in the second watch, or come in the third watch, and find them so, blessed are those servants.
Luke	Lk	49	12	39	But this know ye, that if the householder did know at what hour the thief would come, he would surely watch, and would not suffer his house to be broken open.
Luke	Lk	49	12	40	Be you then also ready: for at what hour you think not, the Son of man will come.
Luke	Lk	49	12	41	And Peter said to him: Lord, dost thou speak this parable to us, or likewise to all?
Luke	Lk	49	12	42	And the Lord said: Who (thinkest thou) is the faithful and wise steward, whom his lord setteth over his family, to give them their measure of wheat in due season?
Luke	Lk	49	12	43	Blessed is that servant, whom when his lord shall come, he shall find so doing.
Luke	Lk	49	12	44	Verily I say to you, he will set him over all that he possesseth.
Luke	Lk	49	12	45	But if that servant shall say in his heart: My lord is long a coming; and shall begin to strike the menservants and maidservants, and to eat and to drink and be drunk:
Luke	Lk	49	12	46	The lord of that servant will come in the day that he hopeth not, and at the hour that he knoweth not, and shall separate him, and shall appoint him his portion with unbelievers.
Luke	Lk	49	12	47	And that servant who knew the will of his lord, and prepared not himself, and did not according to his will, shall be beaten with many stripes.
Luke	Lk	49	12	48	But he that knew not, and did things worthy of stripes, shall be beaten with few stripes. And unto whomsoever much is given, of him much shall be required: and to whom they have committed much, of him they will demand the more.
Luke	Lk	49	12	49	I am come to cast fire on the earth; and what will I, but that it be kindled?
Luke	Lk	49	12	50	And I have a baptism wherewith I am to be baptized: and how am I straitened until it be accomplished?
Luke	Lk	49	12	51	Think ye, that I am come to give peace on earth? I tell you, no; but separation.
Luke	Lk	49	12	52	For there shall be from henceforth five in one house divided: three against two, and two against three.
Luke	Lk	49	12	53	The father shall be divided against the son, and the son against his father, the mother against the daughter, and the daughter against the mother, the mother in law against her daughter in law, and the daughter in law against her mother in law.
Luke	Lk	49	12	54	And he said also to the multitudes: When you see a cloud rising from the west, presently you say: A shower is coming: and so it happeneth:
Luke	Lk	49	12	55	And when ye see the south wind blow, you say: There will be heat: and it cometh to pass.
Luke	Lk	49	12	56	You hypocrites, you know how to discern the face of the heaven and of the earth: but how is it that you do not discern this time?
Luke	Lk	49	12	57	And why even of yourselves, do you not judge that which is just?
Luke	Lk	49	12	58	And when thou goest with thy adversary to the prince, whilst thou art in the way, endeavour to be delivered from him: lest perhaps he draw thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the exacter, and the exacter cast thee into prison.
Luke	Lk	49	12	59	I say to thee, thou shalt not go out thence, until thou pay the very last mite.
Luke	Lk	49	13	1	And there were present, at that very time, some that told him of the Galileans, whose blood Pilate had mingled with their sacrifices.
Luke	Lk	49	13	2	And he answering, said to them: Think you that these Galileans were sinners above all the men of Galilee, because they suffered such things?
Luke	Lk	49	13	3	No, I say to you: but unless you shall do penance, you shall all likewise perish.
Luke	Lk	49	13	4	Or those eighteen upon whom the tower fell in Siloe, and slew them: think you, that they also were debtors above all the men that dwelt in Jerusalem?
Luke	Lk	49	13	5	No, I say to you; but except you do penance, you shall all likewise perish.
Luke	Lk	49	13	6	He spoke also this parable: A certain man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard, and he came seeking fruit on it, and found none.
Luke	Lk	49	13	7	And he said to the dresser of the vineyard: Behold, for these three years I come seeking fruit on this fig tree, and I find none. Cut it down therefore: why cumbereth it the ground?
Luke	Lk	49	13	8	But he answering, said to him: Lord, let it alone this year also, until I dig about it, and dung it.
Luke	Lk	49	13	9	And if happily it bear fruit: but if not, then after that thou shalt cut it down.
Luke	Lk	49	13	10	And he was teaching in their synagogue on their sabbath.
Luke	Lk	49	13	11	And behold there was a woman, who had a spirit of infirmity eighteen years: and she was bowed together, neither could she look upwards at all.
Luke	Lk	49	13	12	Whom when Jesus saw, he called her unto him, and said to her: Woman, thou art delivered from thy infirmity.
Luke	Lk	49	13	13	And he laid his hands upon her, and immediately she was made straight, and glorified God.
Luke	Lk	49	13	14	And the ruler of the synagogue (being angry that Jesus had healed on the sabbath) answering, said to the multitude: Six days there are wherein you ought to work. In them therefore come, and be healed; and not on the sabbath day.
Luke	Lk	49	13	15	And the Lord answering him, said: Ye hypocrites, doth not every one of you, on the sabbath day, loose his ox or his ass from the manger, and lead them to water?
Luke	Lk	49	13	16	And ought not this daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath bound, lo, these eighteen years, be loosed from this bond on the sabbath day?
Luke	Lk	49	13	17	And when he said these things, all his adversaries were ashamed: and all the people rejoiced for all the things that were gloriously done by him.
Luke	Lk	49	13	18	He said therefore: To what is the kingdom of God like, and whereunto shall I resemble it?
Luke	Lk	49	13	19	It is like to a grain of mustard seed, which a man took and cast into his garden, and it grew and became a great tree, and the birds of the air lodged in the branches thereof.
Luke	Lk	49	13	20	And again he said: Whereunto shall I esteem the kingdom of God to be like?
Luke	Lk	49	13	21	It is like to leaven, which a woman took and hid in three measures of meal, till the whole was leavened.
Luke	Lk	49	13	22	And he went through the cities and towns teaching, and making his journey to Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	13	23	And a certain man said to him: Lord, are they few that are saved? But he said to them:
Luke	Lk	49	13	24	Strive to enter by the narrow gate; for many, I say to you, shall seek to enter, and shall not be able.
Luke	Lk	49	13	25	But when the master of the house shall be gone in, and shall shut the door, you shall begin to stand without, and knock at the door, saying: Lord, open to us. And he answering, shall say to you: I know you not, whence you are.
Luke	Lk	49	13	26	Then you shall begin to say: We have eaten and drunk in thy presence, and thou hast taught in our streets.
Luke	Lk	49	13	27	And he shall say to you: I know you not, whence you are: depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity.
Luke	Lk	49	13	28	There shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth, when you shall see Abraham and Isaac and Jacob, and all the prophets, in the kingdom of God, and you yourselves thrust out.
Luke	Lk	49	13	29	And there shall come from the east and the west, and the north and the south; and shall sit down in the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	13	30	And behold, they are last that shall be first; and they are first that shall be last.
Luke	Lk	49	13	31	The same day, there came some of the Pharisees, saying to him: Depart, and get thee hence, for Herod hath a mind to kill thee.
Luke	Lk	49	13	32	And he said to them: Go and tell that fox, Behold, I cast out devils, and do cures today and tomorrow, and the third day I am consummated.
Luke	Lk	49	13	33	Nevertheless I must walk today and tomorrow, and the day following, because it cannot be that a prophet perish, out of Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	13	34	Jerusalem, Jerusalem, that killest the prophets, and stonest them that are sent to thee, how often would I have gathered thy children as the bird doth her brood under her wings, and thou wouldest not?
Luke	Lk	49	13	35	Behold your house shall be left to you desolate. And I say to you, that you shall not see me till the time come, when you shall say: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord.
Luke	Lk	49	14	1	And it came to pass, when Jesus went into the house of one of the chief of the Pharisees, on the sabbath day, to eat bread, that they watched him.
Luke	Lk	49	14	2	And behold, there was a certain man before him that had the dropsy.
Luke	Lk	49	14	3	And Jesus answering, spoke to the lawyers and Pharisees, saying: Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath day?
Luke	Lk	49	14	4	But they held their peace. But he taking him, healed him, and sent him away.
Luke	Lk	49	14	5	And answering them, he said: Which of you shall have an ass or an ox fall into a pit, and will not immediately draw him out, on the sabbath day?
Luke	Lk	49	14	6	And they could not answer him to these things.
Luke	Lk	49	14	7	And he spoke a parable also to them that were invited, marking how they chose the first seats at the table, saying to them:
Luke	Lk	49	14	8	When thou art invited to a wedding, sit not down in the first place, lest perhaps one more honourable than thou be invited by him:
Luke	Lk	49	14	9	And he that invited thee and him, come and say to thee, Give this man place: and then thou begin with shame to take the lowest place.
Luke	Lk	49	14	10	But when thou art invited, go, sit down in the lowest place; that when he who invited thee, cometh, he may say to thee: Friend, go up higher. Then shalt thou have glory before them that sit at table with thee.
Luke	Lk	49	14	11	Because every one that exalteth himself, shall be humbled; and he that humbleth himself, shall be exalted.
Luke	Lk	49	14	12	And he said to him also that had invited him: When thou makest a dinner or a supper, call not thy friends, nor thy brethren, nor thy kinsmen, nor thy neighbours who are rich; lest perhaps they also invite thee again, and a recompense be made to thee.
Luke	Lk	49	14	13	But when thou makest a feast, call the poor, the maimed, the lame, and the blind;
Luke	Lk	49	14	14	And thou shalt be blessed, because they have not wherewith to make thee recompense: for recompense shall be made thee at the resurrection of the just.
Luke	Lk	49	14	15	When one of them that sat at table with him, had heard these things, he said to him: Blessed is he that shall eat bread in the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	14	16	But he said to him: A certain man made a great supper, and invited many.
Luke	Lk	49	14	17	And he sent his servant at the hour of supper to say to them that were invited, that they should come, for now all things are ready.
Luke	Lk	49	14	18	And they began all at once to make excuse. The first said to him: I have bought a farm, and I must needs go out and see it: I pray thee, hold me excused.
Luke	Lk	49	14	19	And another said: I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I go to try them: I pray thee, hold me excused.
Luke	Lk	49	14	20	And another said: I have married a wife, and therefore I cannot come.
Luke	Lk	49	14	21	And the servant returning, told these things to his lord. Then the master of the house, being angry, said to his servant: Go out quickly into the streets and lanes of the city, and bring in hither the poor, and the feeble, and the blind, and the lame.
Luke	Lk	49	14	22	And the servant said: Lord, it is done as thou hast commanded, and yet there is room.
Luke	Lk	49	14	23	And the Lord said to the servant: Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in, that my house may be filled.
Luke	Lk	49	14	24	But I say unto you, that none of those men that were invited, shall taste of my supper.
Luke	Lk	49	14	25	And there went great multitudes with him. And turning, he said to them:
Luke	Lk	49	14	26	If any man come to me, and hate not his father, and mother, and wife, and children, and brethren, and sisters, yea and his own life also, he cannot be my disciple.
Luke	Lk	49	14	27	And whosoever doth not carry his cross and come after me, cannot be my disciple.
Luke	Lk	49	14	28	For which of you having a mind to build a tower, doth not first sit down, and reckon the charges that are necessary, whether he have wherewithal to finish it:
Luke	Lk	49	14	29	Lest, after he hath laid the foundation, and is not able to finish it, all that see it begin to mock him,
Luke	Lk	49	14	30	Saying: This man began to build, and was not able to finish.
Luke	Lk	49	14	31	Or what king, about to go to make war against another king, doth not first sit down, and think whether he be able, with ten thousand, to meet him that, with twenty thousand, cometh against him?
Luke	Lk	49	14	32	Or else, whilst the other is yet afar off, sending an embassy, he desireth conditions of peace.
Luke	Lk	49	14	33	So likewise every one of you that doth not renounce all that he possesseth, cannot be my disciple.
Luke	Lk	49	14	34	Salt is good. But if the salt shall lose its savour, wherewith shall it be seasoned?
Luke	Lk	49	14	35	It is neither profitable for the land nor for the dunghill, but shall be cast out. He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.
Luke	Lk	49	15	1	Now the publicans and sinners drew near unto him to hear him.
Luke	Lk	49	15	2	And the Pharisees and the scribes murmured, saying: This man receiveth sinners, and eateth with them.
Luke	Lk	49	15	3	And he spoke to them this parable, saying:
Luke	Lk	49	15	4	What man of you that hath an hundred sheep: and if he shall lose one of them, doth he not leave the ninety-nine in the desert, and go after that which was lost, until he find it?
Luke	Lk	49	15	5	And when he hath found it, lay it upon his shoulders, rejoicing:
Luke	Lk	49	15	6	And coming home, call together his friends and neighbours, saying to them: Rejoice with me, because I have found my sheep that was lost?
Luke	Lk	49	15	7	I say to you, that even so there shall be joy in heaven upon one sinner that doth penance, more than upon ninety-nine just who need not penance.
Luke	Lk	49	15	8	Or what woman having ten groats; if she lose one groat, doth not light a candle, and sweep the house, and seek diligently until she find it?
Luke	Lk	49	15	9	And when she hath found it, call together her friends and neighbours, saying: Rejoice with me, because I have found the groat which I had lost.
Luke	Lk	49	15	10	So I say to you, there shall be joy before the angels of God upon one sinner doing penance.
Luke	Lk	49	15	11	And he said: A certain man had two sons:
Luke	Lk	49	15	12	And the younger of them said to his father: Father, give me the portion of substance that falleth to me. And he divided unto them his substance.
Luke	Lk	49	15	13	And not many days after, the younger son, gathering all together, went abroad into a far country: and there wasted his substance, living riotously.
Luke	Lk	49	15	14	And after he had spent all, there came a mighty famine in that country; and he began to be in want.
Luke	Lk	49	15	15	And he went and cleaved to one of the citizens of that country. And he sent him into his farm to feed swine.
Luke	Lk	49	15	16	And he would fain have filled his belly with the husks the swine did eat; and no man gave unto him.
Luke	Lk	49	15	17	And returning to himself, he said: How many hired servants in my father's house abound with bread, and I here perish with hunger?
Luke	Lk	49	15	18	I will arise, and will go to my father, and say to him: Father, I have sinned against heaven, and before thee:
Luke	Lk	49	15	19	I am not worthy to be called thy son: make me as one of thy hired servants.
Luke	Lk	49	15	20	And rising up he came to his father. And when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and was moved with compassion, and running to him fell upon his neck, and kissed him.
Luke	Lk	49	15	21	And the son said to him: Father, I have sinned against heaven, and before thee, I am not now worthy to be called thy son.
Luke	Lk	49	15	22	And the father said to his servants: Bring forth quickly the first robe, and put it on him, and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet:
Luke	Lk	49	15	23	And bring hither the fatted calf, and kill it, and let us eat and make merry:
Luke	Lk	49	15	24	Because this my son was dead, and is come to life again: was lost, and is found. And they began to be merry.
Luke	Lk	49	15	25	Now his elder son was in the field, and when he came and drew nigh to the house, he heard music and dancing:
Luke	Lk	49	15	26	And he called one of the servants, and asked what these things meant.
Luke	Lk	49	15	27	And he said to him: Thy brother is come, and thy father hath killed the fatted calf, because he hath received him safe.
Luke	Lk	49	15	28	And he was angry, and would not go in. His father therefore coming out began to entreat him.
Luke	Lk	49	15	29	And he answering, said to his father: Behold, for so many years do I serve thee, and I have never transgressed thy commandment, and yet thou hast never given me a kid to make merry with my friends:
Luke	Lk	49	15	30	But as soon as this thy son is come, who hath devoured his substance with harlots, thou hast killed for him the fatted calf.
Luke	Lk	49	15	31	But he said to him: Son, thou art always with me, and all I have is thine.
Luke	Lk	49	15	32	But it was fit that we should make merry and be glad, for this thy brother was dead and is come to life again; he was lost, and is found.
Luke	Lk	49	16	1	And he said also to his disciples: There was a certain rich man who had a steward: and the same was accused unto him, that he had wasted his goods.
Luke	Lk	49	16	2	And he called him, and said to him: How is it that I hear this of thee? give an account of thy stewardship: for now thou canst be steward no longer.
Luke	Lk	49	16	3	And the steward said within himself: What shall I do, because my lord taketh away from me the stewardship? To dig I am not able; to beg I am ashamed.
Luke	Lk	49	16	4	I know what I will do, that when I shall be removed from the stewardship, they may receive me into their houses.
Luke	Lk	49	16	5	Therefore calling together every one of his lord's debtors, he said to the first: How much dost thou owe my lord?
Luke	Lk	49	16	6	But he said: An hundred barrels of oil. And he said to him: Take thy bill and sit down quickly, and write fifty.
Luke	Lk	49	16	7	Then he said to another: And how much dost thou owe? Who said: An hundred quarters of wheat. He said to him: Take thy bill, and write eighty.
Luke	Lk	49	16	8	And the lord commended the unjust steward, forasmuch as he had done wisely: for the children of this world are wiser in their generation than the children of light.
Luke	Lk	49	16	9	And I say to you: Make unto you friends of the mammon of iniquity; that when you shall fail, they may receive you into everlasting dwellings.
Luke	Lk	49	16	10	He that is faithful in that which is least, is faithful also in that which is greater: and he that is unjust in that which is little, is unjust also in that which is greater.
Luke	Lk	49	16	11	If then you have not been faithful in the unjust mammon; who will trust you with that which is the true?
Luke	Lk	49	16	12	And if you have not been faithful in that which is another's; who will give you that which is your own?
Luke	Lk	49	16	13	No servant can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or he will hold to the one, and despise the other. You cannot serve God and mammon.
Luke	Lk	49	16	14	Now the Pharisees, who were covetous, heard all these things: and they derided him.
Luke	Lk	49	16	15	And he said to them: You are they who justify yourselves before men, but God knoweth your hearts; for that which is high to men, is an abomination before God.
Luke	Lk	49	16	16	The law and the prophets were until John; from that time the kingdom of God is preached, and every one useth violence towards it.
Luke	Lk	49	16	17	And it is easier for heaven and earth to pass, than one tittle of the law to fall.
Luke	Lk	49	16	18	Every one that putteth away his wife, and marrieth another, committeth adultery: and he that marrieth her that is put away from her husband, committeth adultery.
Luke	Lk	49	16	19	There was a certain rich man, who was clothed in purple and fine linen; and feasted sumptuously every day.
Luke	Lk	49	16	20	And there was a certain beggar, named Lazarus, who lay at his gate, full of sores,
Luke	Lk	49	16	21	Desiring to be filled with the crumbs that fell from the rich man's table, and no one did give him; moreover the dogs came, and licked his sores.
Luke	Lk	49	16	22	And it came to pass, that the beggar died, and was carried by the angels into Abraham's bosom. And the rich man also died: and he was buried in hell.
Luke	Lk	49	16	23	And lifting up his eyes when he was in torments, he saw Abraham afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom:
Luke	Lk	49	16	24	And he cried, and said: Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water, to cool my tongue: for I am tormented in this flame.
Luke	Lk	49	16	25	And Abraham said to him: Son, remember that thou didst receive good things in thy lifetime, and likewise Lazarus evil things, but now he is comforted; and thou art tormented.
Luke	Lk	49	16	26	And besides all this, between us and you, there is fixed a great chaos: so that they who would pass from hence to you, cannot, nor from thence come hither.
Luke	Lk	49	16	27	And he said: Then, father, I beseech thee, that thou wouldst send him to my father's house, for I have five brethren,
Luke	Lk	49	16	28	That he may testify unto them, lest they also come into this place of torments.
Luke	Lk	49	16	29	And Abraham said to him: They have Moses and the prophets; let them hear them.
Luke	Lk	49	16	30	But he said: No, father Abraham: but if one went to them from the dead, they will do penance.
Luke	Lk	49	16	31	And he said to him: If they hear not Moses and the prophets, neither will they believe, if one rise again from the dead.
Luke	Lk	49	17	1	And he said to his disciples: It is impossible that scandals should not come: but woe to him through whom they come.
Luke	Lk	49	17	2	It were better for him, that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and he cast into the sea, than that he should scandalize one of these little ones.
Luke	Lk	49	17	3	Take heed to yourselves. If thy brother sin against thee, reprove him: and if he do penance, forgive him.
Luke	Lk	49	17	4	And if he sin against thee seven times in a day, and seven times in a day be converted unto thee, saying, I repent; forgive him.
Luke	Lk	49	17	5	And the apostles said to the Lord: Increase our faith.
Luke	Lk	49	17	6	And the Lord said: If you had faith like to a grain of mustard seed, you might say to this mulberry tree, Be thou rooted up, and be thou transplanted into the sea: and it would obey you.
Luke	Lk	49	17	7	But which of you having a servant ploughing, or feeding cattle, will say to him, when he is come from the field: Immediately go, sit down to meat:
Luke	Lk	49	17	8	And will not rather say to him: Make ready my supper, and gird thyself, and serve me, whilst I eat and drink, and afterwards thou shalt eat and drink?
Luke	Lk	49	17	9	Doth he thank that servant, for doing the things which he commanded him?
Luke	Lk	49	17	10	I think not. So you also, when you shall have done all these things that are commanded you, say: We are unprofitable servants; we have done that which we ought to do.
Luke	Lk	49	17	11	And it came to pass, as he was going to Jerusalem, he passed through the midst of Samaria and Galilee.
Luke	Lk	49	17	12	And as he entered into a certain town, there met him ten men that were lepers, who stood afar off;
Luke	Lk	49	17	13	And lifted up their voice, saying: Jesus, master, have mercy on us.
Luke	Lk	49	17	14	Whom when he saw, he said: Go, shew yourselves to the priests. And it came to pass, as they went, they were made clean.
Luke	Lk	49	17	15	And one of them, when he saw that he was made clean, went back, with a loud voice glorifying God.
Luke	Lk	49	17	16	And he fell on his face before his feet, giving thanks: and this was a Samaritan.
Luke	Lk	49	17	17	And Jesus answering, said, Were not ten made clean? and where are the nine?
Luke	Lk	49	17	18	There is no one found to return and give glory to God, but this stranger.
Luke	Lk	49	17	19	And he said to him: Arise, go thy way; for thy faith hath made thee whole.
Luke	Lk	49	17	20	And being asked by the Pharisees, when the kingdom of God should come? he answered them, and said: The kingdom of God cometh not with observation:
Luke	Lk	49	17	21	Neither shall they say: Behold here, or behold there. For lo, the kingdom of God is within you.
Luke	Lk	49	17	22	And he said to his disciples: The days will come, when you shall desire to see one day of the Son of man; and you shall not see it.
Luke	Lk	49	17	23	And they will say to you: See here, and see there. Go ye not after, nor follow them:
Luke	Lk	49	17	24	For as the lightning that lighteneth from under heaven, shineth unto the parts that are under heaven, so shall the Son of man be in his day.
Luke	Lk	49	17	25	But first he must suffer many things, and be rejected by this generation.
Luke	Lk	49	17	26	And as it came to pass in the days of Noe, so shall it be also in the days of the Son of man.
Luke	Lk	49	17	27	They did eat and drink, they married wives, and were given in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark: and the flood came and destroyed them all.
Luke	Lk	49	17	28	Likewise as it came to pass, in the days of Lot: they did eat and drink, they bought and sold, they planted and built.
Luke	Lk	49	17	29	And in the day that Lot went out of Sodom, it rained fire and brimstone from heaven, and destroyed them all.
Luke	Lk	49	17	30	Even thus shall it be in the day when the Son of man shall be revealed.
Luke	Lk	49	17	31	In that hour, he that shall be on the housetop, and his goods in the house, let him not go down to take them away: and he that shall be in the field, in like manner, let him not return back.
Luke	Lk	49	17	32	Remember Lot's wife.
Luke	Lk	49	17	33	Whosoever shall seek to save his life, shall lose it: and whosoever shall lose it, shall preserve it.
Luke	Lk	49	17	34	I say to you: in that night there shall be two men in one bed; the one shall be taken, and the other shall be left.
Luke	Lk	49	17	35	Two women shall be grinding together: the one shall be taken, and the other shall be left: two men shall be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other shall be left.
Luke	Lk	49	17	36	They answering, say to him: Where, Lord?
Luke	Lk	49	17	37	Who said to them: Wheresoever the body shall be, thither will the eagles also be gathered together.
Luke	Lk	49	18	1	And he spoke also a parable to them, that we ought always to pray, and not to faint,
Luke	Lk	49	18	2	Saying: There was a judge in a certain city, who feared not God, nor regarded man.
Luke	Lk	49	18	3	And there was a certain widow in that city, and she came to him, saying: Avenge me of my adversary.
Luke	Lk	49	18	4	And he would not for a long time. But afterwards he said within himself: Although I fear not God, nor regard man,
Luke	Lk	49	18	5	Yet because this widow is troublesome to me, I will avenge her, lest continually coming she weary me.
Luke	Lk	49	18	6	And the Lord said: Hear what the unjust judge saith.
Luke	Lk	49	18	7	And will not God revenge his elect who cry to him day and night: and will he have patience in their regard?
Luke	Lk	49	18	8	I say to you, that he will quickly revenge them. But yet the Son of man, when he cometh, shall he find, think you, faith on earth?
Luke	Lk	49	18	9	And to some who trusted in themselves as just, and despised others, he spoke also this parable:
Luke	Lk	49	18	10	Two men went up into the temple to pray: the one a Pharisee, and the other a publican.
Luke	Lk	49	18	11	The Pharisee standing, prayed thus with himself: O God, I give thee thanks that I am not as the rest of men, extortioners, unjust, adulterers, as also is this publican.
Luke	Lk	49	18	12	I fast twice in a week: I give tithes of all that I possess.
Luke	Lk	49	18	13	And the publican, standing afar off, would not so much as lift up his eyes towards heaven; but struck his breast, saying: O God, be merciful to me a sinner.
Luke	Lk	49	18	14	I say to you, this man went down into his house justified rather than the other: because every one that exalteth himself, shall be humbled: and he that humbleth himself, shall be exalted.
Luke	Lk	49	18	15	And they brought unto him also infants, that he might touch them. Which when the disciples saw, they rebuked them.
Luke	Lk	49	18	16	But Jesus, calling them together, said: Suffer children to come to me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	18	17	Amen, I say to you: Whosoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a child, shall not enter into it.
Luke	Lk	49	18	18	And a certain ruler asked him, saying: Good master, what shall I do to possess everlasting life?
Luke	Lk	49	18	19	And Jesus said to him: Why dost thou call me good? None is good but God alone.
Luke	Lk	49	18	20	Thou knowest the commandments: Thou shalt not kill: Thou shalt not commit adultery: Thou shalt not steal: Thou shalt not bear false witness: Honour thy father and mother.
Luke	Lk	49	18	21	Who said: All these things have I kept from my youth.
Luke	Lk	49	18	22	Which when Jesus had heard, he said to him: Yet one thing is wanting to thee: sell all whatever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, follow me.
Luke	Lk	49	18	23	He having heard these things, became sorrowful; for he was very rich.
Luke	Lk	49	18	24	And Jesus seeing him become sorrowful, said: How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	18	25	For it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	18	26	And they that heard it, said: Who then can be saved?
Luke	Lk	49	18	27	He said to them: The things that are impossible with men, are possible with God.
Luke	Lk	49	18	28	Then Peter said: Behold, we have left all things, and have followed thee.
Luke	Lk	49	18	29	Who said to them: Amen, I say to you, there is no man that hath left house, or parents, or brethren, or wife, or children, for the kingdom of God's sake,
Luke	Lk	49	18	30	Who shall not receive much more in this present time, and in the world to come life everlasting.
Luke	Lk	49	18	31	Then Jesus took unto him the twelve, and said to them: Behold, we go up to Jerusalem, and all things shall be accomplished which were written by the prophets concerning the Son of man.
Luke	Lk	49	18	32	For he shall be delivered to the Gentiles, and shall be mocked, and scourged, and spit upon:
Luke	Lk	49	18	33	And after they have scourged him, they will put him to death; and the third day he shall rise again.
Luke	Lk	49	18	34	And they understood none of these things, and this word was hid from them, and they understood not the things that were said.
Luke	Lk	49	18	35	Now it came to pass, when he drew nigh to Jericho, that a certain blind man sat by the way side, begging.
Luke	Lk	49	18	36	And when he heard the multitude passing by, he asked what this meant.
Luke	Lk	49	18	37	And they told him, that Jesus of Nazareth was passing by.
Luke	Lk	49	18	38	And he cried out, saying: Jesus, son of David, have mercy on me.
Luke	Lk	49	18	39	And they that went before, rebuked him, that he should hold his peace: but he cried out much more: Son of David, have mercy on me.
Luke	Lk	49	18	40	And Jesus standing, commanded him to be brought unto him. And when he was come near, he asked him,
Luke	Lk	49	18	41	Saying: What wilt thou that I do to thee? But he said: Lord, that I may see.
Luke	Lk	49	18	42	And Jesus said to him: Receive thy sight: thy faith hath made thee whole.
Luke	Lk	49	18	43	And immediately he saw, and followed him, glorifying God. And all the people, when they saw it, gave praise to God.
Luke	Lk	49	19	1	And entering in, he walked through Jericho.
Luke	Lk	49	19	2	And behold, there was a man named Zacheus, who was the chief of the publicans, and he was rich.
Luke	Lk	49	19	3	And he sought to see Jesus who he was, and he could not for the crowd, because he was low of stature.
Luke	Lk	49	19	4	And running before, he climbed up into a sycamore tree, that he might see him; for he was to pass that way.
Luke	Lk	49	19	5	And when Jesus was come to the place, looking up, he saw him, and said to him: Zacheus, make haste and come down; for this day I must abide in thy house.
Luke	Lk	49	19	6	And he made haste and came down; and received him with joy.
Luke	Lk	49	19	7	And when all saw it, they murmured, saying, that he was gone to be a guest with a man that was a sinner.
Luke	Lk	49	19	8	But Zacheus standing, said to the Lord: Behold, Lord, the half of my goods I give to the poor; and if I have wronged any man of any thing, I restore him fourfold.
Luke	Lk	49	19	9	Jesus said to him: This day is salvation come to this house, because he also is a son of Abraham.
Luke	Lk	49	19	10	For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.
Luke	Lk	49	19	11	As they were hearing these things, he added and spoke a parable, because he was nigh to Jerusalem, and because they thought that the kingdom of God should immediately be manifested.
Luke	Lk	49	19	12	He said therefore: A certain nobleman went into a far country, to receive for himself a kingdom, and to return.
Luke	Lk	49	19	13	And calling his ten servants, he gave them ten pounds, and said to them: Trade till I come.
Luke	Lk	49	19	14	But his citizens hated him: and they sent an embassage after him, saying: We will not have this man to reign over us.
Luke	Lk	49	19	15	And it came to pass, that he returned, having received the kingdom: and he commanded his servants to be called, to whom he had given the money, that he might know how much every man had gained by trading.
Luke	Lk	49	19	16	And the first came, saying: Lord, thy pound hath gained ten pounds.
Luke	Lk	49	19	17	And he said to him: Well done, thou good servant, because thou hast been faithful in a little, thou shalt have power over ten cities.
Luke	Lk	49	19	18	And the second came, saying: Lord, thy pound hath gained five pounds.
Luke	Lk	49	19	19	And he said to him: Be thou also over five cities.
Luke	Lk	49	19	20	And another came, saying: Lord, behold here is thy pound, which I have kept laid up in a napkin;
Luke	Lk	49	19	21	For I feared thee, because thou art an austere man: thou takest up what thou didst not lay down, and thou reapest that which thou didst not sow.
Luke	Lk	49	19	22	He saith to him: Out of thy own mouth I judge thee, thou wicked servant. Thou knewest that I was an austere man, taking up what I laid not down, and reaping that which I did not sow:
Luke	Lk	49	19	23	And why then didst thou not give my money into the bank, that at my coming, I might have exacted it with usury?
Luke	Lk	49	19	24	And he said to them that stood by: Take the pound away from him, and give it to him that hath ten pounds.
Luke	Lk	49	19	25	And they said to him: Lord, he hath ten pounds.
Luke	Lk	49	19	26	But I say to you, that to every one that hath shall be given, and he shall abound: and from him that hath not, even that which he hath, shall be taken from him.
Luke	Lk	49	19	27	But as for those my enemies, who would not have me reign over them, bring them hither, and kill them before me.
Luke	Lk	49	19	28	And having said these things, he went before, going up to Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	19	29	And it came to pass, when he was come nigh to Bethphage and Bethania, unto the mount called Olivet, he sent two of his disciples,
Luke	Lk	49	19	30	Saying: Go into the town which is over against you, at your entering into which you shall find the colt of an ass tied, on which no man ever hath sitten: loose him, and bring him hither.
Luke	Lk	49	19	31	And if any man shall ask you: Why do you loose him? you shall say thus unto him: Because the Lord hath need of his service.
Luke	Lk	49	19	32	And they that were sent, went their way, and found the colt standing, as he had said unto them.
Luke	Lk	49	19	33	And as they were loosing the colt, the owners thereof said to them: Why loose you the colt?
Luke	Lk	49	19	34	But they said: Because the Lord hath need of him.
Luke	Lk	49	19	35	And they brought him to Jesus. And casting their garments on the colt, they set Jesus thereon.
Luke	Lk	49	19	36	And as he went, they spread their clothes underneath in the way.
Luke	Lk	49	19	37	And when he was now coming near the descent of mount Olivet, the whole multitude of his disciples began with joy to praise God with a loud voice, for all the mighty works they had seen,
Luke	Lk	49	19	38	Saying: Blessed be the king who cometh in the name of the Lord, peace in heaven, and glory on high!
Luke	Lk	49	19	39	And some of the Pharisees, from amongst the multitude, said to him: Master, rebuke thy disciples.
Luke	Lk	49	19	40	To whom he said: I say to you, that if these shall hold their peace, the stones will cry out.
Luke	Lk	49	19	41	And when he drew near, seeing the city, he wept over it, saying:
Luke	Lk	49	19	42	If thou also hadst known, and that in this thy day, the things that are to thy peace; but now they are hidden from thy eyes.
Luke	Lk	49	19	43	For the days shall come upon thee, and thy enemies shall cast a trench about thee, and compass thee round, and straiten thee on every side,
Luke	Lk	49	19	44	And beat thee flat to the ground, and thy children who are in thee: and they shall not leave in thee a stone upon a stone: because thou hast not known the time of thy visitation.
Luke	Lk	49	19	45	And entering into the temple, he began to cast out them that sold therein, and them that bought.
Luke	Lk	49	19	46	Saying to them: It is written: My house is the house of prayer. But you have made it a den of thieves.
Luke	Lk	49	19	47	And he was teaching daily in the temple. And the chief priests and the scribes and the rulers of the people sought to destroy him:
Luke	Lk	49	19	48	And they found not what to do to him: for all the people were very attentive to hear him.
Luke	Lk	49	20	1	And it came to pass, that on one of the days, as he was teaching the people in the temple, and preaching the gospel, the chief priests and the scribes, with the ancients, met together,
Luke	Lk	49	20	2	And spoke to him, saying: Tell us, by what authority dost thou these things? or, Who is he that hath given thee this authority?
Luke	Lk	49	20	3	And Jesus answering, said to them: I will also ask you one thing. Answer me:
Luke	Lk	49	20	4	The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or of men?
Luke	Lk	49	20	5	But they thought within themselves, saying: If we shall say, From heaven: he will say: Why then did you not believe him?
Luke	Lk	49	20	6	But if we say, Of men, the whole people will stone us: for they are persuaded that John was a prophet.
Luke	Lk	49	20	7	And they answered, that they knew not whence it was.
Luke	Lk	49	20	8	And Jesus said to them: Neither do I tell thee by what authority I do these things.
Luke	Lk	49	20	9	And he began to speak to the people this parable: A certain man planted a vineyard, and let it out to husbandmen: and he was abroad for a long time.
Luke	Lk	49	20	10	And at the season he sent a servant to the husbandmen, that they should give him of the fruit of the vineyard. Who, beating him, sent him away empty.
Luke	Lk	49	20	11	And again he sent another servant. But they beat him also, and treating him reproachfully, sent him away empty.
Luke	Lk	49	20	12	And again he sent the third: and they wounded him also, and cast him out.
Luke	Lk	49	20	13	Then the lord of the vineyard said: What shall I do? I will send my beloved son: it may be, when they see him, they will reverence him.
Luke	Lk	49	20	14	Whom when the husbandmen saw, they thought within themselves, saying: This is the heir, let us kill him, that the inheritance may be ours.
Luke	Lk	49	20	15	So casting him out of the vineyard, they killed him. What therefore will the lord of the vineyard do to them?
Luke	Lk	49	20	16	He will come, and will destroy these husbandmen, and will give the vineyard to others. Which they hearing, said to him: God forbid.
Luke	Lk	49	20	17	But he looking on them, said: What is this then that is written, The stone, which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner?
Luke	Lk	49	20	18	Whosoever shall fall upon that stone, shall be bruised: and upon whomsoever it shall fall, it will grind him to powder.
Luke	Lk	49	20	19	And the chief priests and the scribes sought to lay hands on him the same hour: but they feared the people, for they knew that he spoke this parable to them.
Luke	Lk	49	20	20	And being upon the watch, they sent spies, who should feign themselves just, that they might take hold of him in his words, that they might deliver him up to the authority and power of the governor.
Luke	Lk	49	20	21	And they asked him, saying: Master, we know that thou speakest and teachest rightly: and thou dost not respect any person, but teachest the way of God in truth.
Luke	Lk	49	20	22	Is it lawful for us to give tribute to Caesar, or no?
Luke	Lk	49	20	23	But he considering their guile, said to them: Why tempt you me?
Luke	Lk	49	20	24	shew me a penny. Whose image and inscription hath it? They answering, said to him, Caesar's.
Luke	Lk	49	20	25	And he said to them: Render therefore to Caesar the things that are Caesar's: and to God the things that are God's.
Luke	Lk	49	20	26	And they could not reprehend his word before the people: and wondering at his answer, they held their peace.
Luke	Lk	49	20	27	And there came to him some of the Sadducees, who deny that there is any resurrection, and they asked him,
Luke	Lk	49	20	28	Saying: Master, Moses wrote unto us, If any man's brother die, having a wife, and he leave no children, that his brother should take her to wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.
Luke	Lk	49	20	29	There were therefore seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and died without children.
Luke	Lk	49	20	30	And the next took her to wife, and he also died childless.
Luke	Lk	49	20	31	And the third took her. And in like manner all the seven, and they left no children, and died.
Luke	Lk	49	20	32	Last of all the woman died also.
Luke	Lk	49	20	33	In the resurrection therefore, whose wife of them shall she be? For all the seven had her to wife.
Luke	Lk	49	20	34	And Jesus said to them: The children of this world marry, and are given in marriage:
Luke	Lk	49	20	35	But they that shall be accounted worthy of that world, and of the resurrection from the dead, shall neither be married, nor take wives.
Luke	Lk	49	20	36	Neither can they die any more: for they are equal to the angels, and are the children of God, being the children of the resurrection.
Luke	Lk	49	20	37	Now that the dead rise again, Moses also shewed, at the bush, when he called the Lord, The God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob;
Luke	Lk	49	20	38	For he is not the God of the dead, but of the living: for all live to him.
Luke	Lk	49	20	39	And some of the scribes answering, said to him: Master, thou hast said well.
Luke	Lk	49	20	40	And after that they durst not ask him any more questions.
Luke	Lk	49	20	41	But he said to them: How say they that Christ is the son of David?
Luke	Lk	49	20	42	And David himself saith in the book of Psalms: The Lord said to my Lord, sit thou on my right hand,
Luke	Lk	49	20	43	Till I make thy enemies thy footstool.
Luke	Lk	49	20	44	David then calleth him Lord: and how is he his son?
Luke	Lk	49	20	45	And in the hearing of all the people, he said to his disciples:
Luke	Lk	49	20	46	Beware of the scribes, who desire to walk in long robes, and love salutations in the marketplace, and the first chairs in the synagogues, and the chief rooms at feasts:
Luke	Lk	49	20	47	Who devour the houses of widows, feigning long prayer. These shall receive greater damnation.
Luke	Lk	49	21	1	And looking on, he saw the rich men cast their gifts into the treasury.
Luke	Lk	49	21	2	And he saw also a certain poor widow casting in two brass mites.
Luke	Lk	49	21	3	And he said: Verily I say to you, that this poor widow hath cast in more than they all:
Luke	Lk	49	21	4	For all these have of their abundance cast into the offerings of God: but she of her want, hath cast in all the living that she had.
Luke	Lk	49	21	5	And some saying of the temple, that it was adorned with goodly stones and gifts, he said:
Luke	Lk	49	21	6	These things which you see, the days will come in which there shall not be left a stone upon a stone that shall not be thrown down.
Luke	Lk	49	21	7	And they asked him, saying: Master, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign when they shall begin to come to pass?
Luke	Lk	49	21	8	Who said: Take heed you be not seduced; for many will come in my name, saying, I am he; and the time is at hand: go ye not therefore after them.
Luke	Lk	49	21	9	And when you shall hear of wars and seditions, be not terrified: these things must first come to pass; but the end is not yet presently.
Luke	Lk	49	21	10	Then he said to them: Nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom.
Luke	Lk	49	21	11	And there shall be great earthquakes in divers places, and pestilences, and famines, and terrors from heaven; and there shall be great signs.
Luke	Lk	49	21	12	But before all these things, they will lay their hands upon you, and persecute you, delivering you up to the synagogues and into prisons, dragging you before kings and governors, for my name's sake.
Luke	Lk	49	21	13	And it shall happen unto you for a testimony.
Luke	Lk	49	21	14	Lay it up therefore into your hearts, not to meditate before how you shall answer:
Luke	Lk	49	21	15	For I will give you a mouth and wisdom, which all your adversaries shall not be able to resist and gainsay.
Luke	Lk	49	21	16	And you shall be betrayed by your parents and brethren, and kinsmen and friends; and some of you they will put to death.
Luke	Lk	49	21	17	And you shall be hated by all men for my name's sake.
Luke	Lk	49	21	18	But a hair of your head shall not perish.
Luke	Lk	49	21	19	In your patience you shall possess your souls.
Luke	Lk	49	21	20	And when you shall see Jerusalem compassed about with an army; then know that the desolation thereof is at hand.
Luke	Lk	49	21	21	Then let those who are in Judea, flee to the mountains; and those who are in the midst thereof, depart out: and those who are in the countries, not enter into it.
Luke	Lk	49	21	22	For these are the days of vengeance, that all things may be fulfilled, that are written.
Luke	Lk	49	21	23	But woe to them that are with child, and give suck in those days; for there shall be great distress in the land, and wrath upon this people.
Luke	Lk	49	21	24	And they shall fall by the edge of the sword; and shall be led away captives into all nations; and Jerusalem shall be trodden down by the Gentiles; till the times of the nations be fulfilled.
Luke	Lk	49	21	25	And there shall be signs in the sun, and in the moon, and in the stars; and upon the earth distress of nations, by reason of the confusion of the roaring of the sea and of the waves;
Luke	Lk	49	21	26	Men withering away for fear, and expectation of what shall come upon the whole world. For the powers of heaven shall be moved;
Luke	Lk	49	21	27	And then they shall see the Son of man coming in a cloud, with great power and majesty.
Luke	Lk	49	21	28	But when these things begin to come to pass, look up, and lift up your heads, because your redemption is at hand.
Luke	Lk	49	21	29	And he spoke to them in a similitude. See the fig tree, and all the trees:
Luke	Lk	49	21	30	When they now shoot forth their fruit, you know that summer is nigh;
Luke	Lk	49	21	31	So you also, when you shall see these things come to pass, know that the kingdom of God is at hand.
Luke	Lk	49	21	32	Amen, I say to you, this generation shall not pass away, till all things be fulfilled.
Luke	Lk	49	21	33	Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.
Luke	Lk	49	21	34	And take heed to yourselves, lest perhaps your hearts be overcharged with surfeiting and drunkenness, and the cares of this life, and that day come upon you suddenly.
Luke	Lk	49	21	35	For as a snare shall it come upon all that sit upon the face of the whole earth.
Luke	Lk	49	21	36	Watch ye, therefore, praying at all times, that you may be accounted worthy to escape all these things that are to come, and to stand before the Son of man.
Luke	Lk	49	21	37	And in the daytime, he was teaching in the temple; but at night, going out, he abode in the mount that is called Olivet.
Luke	Lk	49	21	38	And all the people came early in the morning to him in the temple, to hear him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	1	Now the feast of unleavened bread, which is called the pasch, was at hand.
Luke	Lk	49	22	2	And the chief priests and the scribes sought how they might put Jesus to death: but they feared the people.
Luke	Lk	49	22	3	And Satan entered into Judas, who was surnamed Iscariot, one of the twelve.
Luke	Lk	49	22	4	And he went, and discoursed with the chief priests and the magistrates, how he might betray him to them.
Luke	Lk	49	22	5	And they were glad, and covenanted to give him money.
Luke	Lk	49	22	6	And he promised. And he sought opportunity to betray him in the absence of the multitude.
Luke	Lk	49	22	7	And the day of the unleavened bread came, on which it was necessary that the pasch should be killed.
Luke	Lk	49	22	8	And he sent Peter and John, saying: Go, and prepare for us the pasch, that we may eat.
Luke	Lk	49	22	9	But they said: Where wilt thou that we prepare?
Luke	Lk	49	22	10	And he said to them: Behold, as you go into the city, there shall meet you a man carrying a pitcher of water: follow him into the house where he entereth in.
Luke	Lk	49	22	11	And you shall say to the goodman of the house: The master saith to thee, Where is the guest chamber, where I may eat the pasch with my disciples?
Luke	Lk	49	22	12	And he will shew you a large dining room, furnished; and there prepare.
Luke	Lk	49	22	13	And they going, found as he had said to them, and made ready the pasch.
Luke	Lk	49	22	14	And when the hour was come, he sat down, and the twelve apostles with him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	15	And he said to them: With desire I have desired to eat this pasch with you, before I suffer.
Luke	Lk	49	22	16	For I say to you, that from this time I will not eat it, till it be fulfilled in the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	22	17	And having taken the chalice, he gave thanks, and said: Take, and divide it among you:
Luke	Lk	49	22	18	For I say to you, that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine, till the kingdom of God come.
Luke	Lk	49	22	19	And taking bread, he gave thanks, and brake; and gave to them, saying: This is my body, which is given for you. Do this for a commemoration of me.
Luke	Lk	49	22	20	In like manner the chalice also, after he had supped, saying: This is the chalice, the new testament in my blood, which shall be shed for you.
Luke	Lk	49	22	21	But yet behold, the hand of him that betrayeth me is with me on the table.
Luke	Lk	49	22	22	And the Son of man indeed goeth, according to that which is determined: but yet, woe to that man by whom he shall be betrayed.
Luke	Lk	49	22	23	And they began to inquire among themselves, which of them it was that should do this thing.
Luke	Lk	49	22	24	And there was also a strife amongst them, which of them should seem to be the greater.
Luke	Lk	49	22	25	And he said to them: The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them; and they that have power over them, are called beneficent.
Luke	Lk	49	22	26	But you not so: but he that is the greater among you, let him become as the younger; and he that is the leader, as he that serveth.
Luke	Lk	49	22	27	For which is greater, he that sitteth at table, or he that serveth? Is it not he that sitteth at table? But I am in the midst of you, as he that serveth:
Luke	Lk	49	22	28	And you are they who have continued with me in my temptations:
Luke	Lk	49	22	29	And I dispose to you, as my Father hath disposed to me, a kingdom;
Luke	Lk	49	22	30	That you may eat and drink at my table, in my kingdom: and may sit upon thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.
Luke	Lk	49	22	31	And the Lord said: Simon, Simon, behold Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat:
Luke	Lk	49	22	32	But I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and thou, being once converted, confirm thy brethren.
Luke	Lk	49	22	33	Who said to him: Lord, I am ready to go with thee, both into prison, and to death.
Luke	Lk	49	22	34	And he said: I say to thee, Peter, the cock shall not crow this day, till thou thrice deniest that thou knowest me. And he said to them:
Luke	Lk	49	22	35	When I sent you without purse, and scrip, and shoes, did you want anything?
Luke	Lk	49	22	36	But they said: Nothing. Then said he unto them: But now he that hath a purse, let him take it, and likewise a scrip; and he that hath not, let him sell his coat, and buy a sword.
Luke	Lk	49	22	37	For I say to you, that this that is written must yet be fulfilled in me: And with the wicked was he reckoned. For the things concerning me have an end.
Luke	Lk	49	22	38	But they said: Lord, behold here are two swords. And he said to them, It is enough.
Luke	Lk	49	22	39	And going out, he went, according to his custom, to the mount of Olives. And his disciples also followed him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	40	And when he was come to the place, he said to them: Pray, lest ye enter into temptation.
Luke	Lk	49	22	41	And he was withdrawn away from them a stone's cast; and kneeling down, he prayed,
Luke	Lk	49	22	42	Saying: Father, if thou wilt, remove this chalice from me: but yet not my will, but thine be done.
Luke	Lk	49	22	43	And there appeared to him an angel from heaven, strengthening him. And being in an agony, he prayed the longer.
Luke	Lk	49	22	44	And his sweat became as drops of blood, trickling down upon the ground.
Luke	Lk	49	22	45	And when he rose up from prayer, and was come to his disciples, he found them sleeping for sorrow.
Luke	Lk	49	22	46	And he said to them: Why sleep you? arise, pray, lest you enter into temptation.
Luke	Lk	49	22	47	As he was yet speaking, behold a multitude; and he that was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them, and drew near to Jesus, for to kiss him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	48	And Jesus said to him: Judas, dost thou betray the Son of man with a kiss?
Luke	Lk	49	22	49	And they that were about him, seeing what would follow, said to him: Lord, shall we strike with the sword?
Luke	Lk	49	22	50	And one of them struck the servant of the high priest, and cut off his right ear.
Luke	Lk	49	22	51	But Jesus answering, said: Suffer ye thus far. And when he had touched his ear, he healed him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	52	And Jesus said to the chief priests, and magistrates of the temple, and the ancients, that were come unto him: Are ye come out, as it were against a thief, with swords and clubs?
Luke	Lk	49	22	53	When I was daily with you in the temple, you did not stretch forth your hands against me: but this is your hour, and the power of darkness.
Luke	Lk	49	22	54	And apprehending him, they led him to the high priest's house. But Peter followed afar off.
Luke	Lk	49	22	55	And when they had kindled a fire in the midst of the hall, and were sitting about it, Peter was in the midst of them.
Luke	Lk	49	22	56	Whom when a certain servant maid had seen sitting at the light, and had earnestly beheld him, she said: This man also was with him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	57	But he denied him, saying: Woman, I know him not.
Luke	Lk	49	22	58	And after a little while, another seeing him, said: Thou also art one of them. But Peter said: O man, I am not.
Luke	Lk	49	22	59	And after the space, as it were of one hour, another certain man affirmed, saying: Of a truth, this man was also with him; for he is also a Galilean.
Luke	Lk	49	22	60	And Peter said: Man, I know not what thou sayest. And immediately, as he was yet speaking, the cock crew.
Luke	Lk	49	22	61	And the Lord turning looked on Peter. And Peter remembered the word of the Lord, as he had said: Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.
Luke	Lk	49	22	62	And Peter going out, wept bitterly.
Luke	Lk	49	22	63	And the men that held him, mocked him, and struck him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	64	And they blindfolded him, and smote his face. And they asked him, saying: Prophesy, who is it that struck thee?
Luke	Lk	49	22	65	And blaspheming, many other things they said against him.
Luke	Lk	49	22	66	And as soon as it was day, the ancients of the people, and the chief priests and scribes, came together; and they brought him into their council, saying: If thou be the Christ, tell us.
Luke	Lk	49	22	67	And he saith to them: If I shall tell you, you will not believe me.
Luke	Lk	49	22	68	And if I shall also ask you, you will not answer me, nor let me go.
Luke	Lk	49	22	69	But hereafter the Son of man shall be sitting on the right hand of the power of God.
Luke	Lk	49	22	70	Then said they all: Art thou then the Son of God? Who said: You say that I am.
Luke	Lk	49	22	71	And they said: What need we any further testimony? for we ourselves have heard it from his own mouth.
Luke	Lk	49	23	1	And the whole multitude of them rising up, led him to Pilate.
Luke	Lk	49	23	2	And they began to accuse him, saying: We have found this man perverting our nation, and forbidding to give tribute to Caesar, and saying that he is Christ the king.
Luke	Lk	49	23	3	And Pilate asked him, saying: Art thou the king of the Jews? But he answering, said: Thou sayest it.
Luke	Lk	49	23	4	And Pilate said to the chief priests and to the multitudes: I find no cause in this man.
Luke	Lk	49	23	5	But they were more earnest, saying: He stirreth up the people, teaching throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee to this place.
Luke	Lk	49	23	6	But Pilate hearing Galilee, asked if the man were of Galilee?
Luke	Lk	49	23	7	And when he understood that he was of Herod's jurisdiction, he sent him away to Herod, who was also himself at Jerusalem, in those days.
Luke	Lk	49	23	8	And Herod, seeing Jesus, was very glad; for he was desirous of a long time to see him, because he had heard many things of him; and he hoped to see some sign wrought by him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	9	And he questioned him in many words. But he answered him nothing.
Luke	Lk	49	23	10	And the chief priests and the scribes stood by, earnestly accusing him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	11	And Herod with his army set him at nought, and mocked him, putting on him a white garment, and sent him back to Pilate.
Luke	Lk	49	23	12	And Herod and Pilate were made friends, that same day; for before they were enemies one to another.
Luke	Lk	49	23	13	And Pilate, calling together the chief priests, and the magistrates, and the people,
Luke	Lk	49	23	14	Said to them: You have presented unto me this man, as one that perverteth the people; and behold I, having examined him before you, find no cause in this man, in those things wherein you accuse him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	15	No, nor Herod neither. For I sent you to him, and behold, nothing worthy of death is done to him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	16	I will chastise him therefore, and release him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	17	Now of necessity he was to release unto them one upon the feast day.
Luke	Lk	49	23	18	But the whole multitude together cried out, saying: Away with this man, and release unto us Barabbas:
Luke	Lk	49	23	19	Who, for a certain sedition made in the city, and for a murder, was cast into prison.
Luke	Lk	49	23	20	And Pilate again spoke to them, desiring to release Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	23	21	But they cried again, saying: Crucify him, crucify him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	22	And he said to them the third time: Why, what evil hath this man done? I find no cause of death in him. I will chastise him therefore, and let him go.
Luke	Lk	49	23	23	But they were instant with loud voices, requiring that he might be crucified; and their voices prevailed.
Luke	Lk	49	23	24	And Pilate gave sentence that it should be as they required.
Luke	Lk	49	23	25	And he released unto them him who for murder and sedition, had been cast into prison, whom they had desired; but Jesus he delivered up to their will.
Luke	Lk	49	23	26	And as they led him away, they laid hold of one Simon of Cyrene, coming from the country; and they laid the cross on him to carry after Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	23	27	And there followed him a great multitude of people, and of women, who bewailed and lamented him.
Luke	Lk	49	23	28	But Jesus turning to them, said: Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not over me; but weep for yourselves, and for your children.
Luke	Lk	49	23	29	For behold, the days shall come, wherein they will say: Blessed are the barren, and the wombs that have not borne, and the paps that have not given suck.
Luke	Lk	49	23	30	Then shall they begin to say to the mountains: Fall upon us; and to the hills: Cover us.
Luke	Lk	49	23	31	For if in the green wood they do these things, what shall be done in the dry?
Luke	Lk	49	23	32	And there were also two other malefactors led with him to be put to death.
Luke	Lk	49	23	33	And when they were come to the place which is called Calvary, they crucified him there; and the robbers, one on the right hand, and the other on the left.
Luke	Lk	49	23	34	And Jesus said: Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do. But they, dividing his garments, cast lots.
Luke	Lk	49	23	35	And the people stood beholding, and the rulers with them derided him, saying: He saved others; let him save himself, if he be Christ, the elect of God.
Luke	Lk	49	23	36	And the soldiers also mocked him, coming to him, and offering him vinegar,
Luke	Lk	49	23	37	And saying: If thou be the king of the Jews, save thyself.
Luke	Lk	49	23	38	And there was also a superscription written over him in letters of Greek, and Latin, and Hebrew: THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.
Luke	Lk	49	23	39	And one of those robbers who were hanged, blasphemed him, saying: If thou be Christ, save thyself and us.
Luke	Lk	49	23	40	But the other answering, rebuked him, saying: Neither dost thou fear God, seeing thou art condemned under the same condemnation?
Luke	Lk	49	23	41	And we indeed justly, for we receive the due reward of our deeds; but this man hath done no evil.
Luke	Lk	49	23	42	And he said to Jesus: Lord, remember me when thou shalt come into thy kingdom.
Luke	Lk	49	23	43	And Jesus said to him: Amen I say to thee, this day thou shalt be with me in paradise.
Luke	Lk	49	23	44	And it was almost the sixth hour; and there was darkness over all the earth until the ninth hour.
Luke	Lk	49	23	45	And the sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was rent in the midst.
Luke	Lk	49	23	46	And Jesus crying out with a loud voice, said: Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit. And saying this, he gave up the ghost.
Luke	Lk	49	23	47	Now the centurion, seeing what was done, glorified God, saying: Indeed this was a just man.
Luke	Lk	49	23	48	And all the multitude of them that were come together to that sight, and saw the things that were done, returned striking their breasts.
Luke	Lk	49	23	49	And all his acquaintance, and the women that had followed him from Galilee, stood afar off, beholding these things.
Luke	Lk	49	23	50	And behold there was a man named Joseph, who was a counsellor, a good and just man,
Luke	Lk	49	23	51	(The same had not consented to their counsel and doings;) of Arimathea, a city of Judea; who also himself looked for the kingdom of God.
Luke	Lk	49	23	52	This man went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	23	53	And taking him down, he wrapped him in fine linen, and laid him in a sepulchre that was hewed in stone, wherein never yet any man had been laid.
Luke	Lk	49	23	54	And it was the day of the Parasceve, and the sabbath drew on.
Luke	Lk	49	23	55	And the women that were come with him from Galilee, following after, saw the sepulchre, and how his body was laid.
Luke	Lk	49	23	56	And returning, they prepared spices and ointments; and on the sabbath day they rested, according to the commandment.
Luke	Lk	49	24	1	And on the first day of the week, very early in the morning, they came to the sepulchre, bringing the spices which they had prepared.
Luke	Lk	49	24	2	And they found the stone rolled back from the sepulchre.
Luke	Lk	49	24	3	And going in, they found not the body of the Lord Jesus.
Luke	Lk	49	24	4	And it came to pass, as they were astonished in their mind at this, behold, two men stood by them, in shining apparel.
Luke	Lk	49	24	5	And as they were afraid, and bowed down their countenance towards the ground, they said unto them: Why seek you the living with the dead?
Luke	Lk	49	24	6	He is not here, but is risen. Remember how he spoke unto you, when he was in Galilee,
Luke	Lk	49	24	7	Saying: The Son of man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and the third day rise again.
Luke	Lk	49	24	8	And they remembered his words.
Luke	Lk	49	24	9	And going back from the sepulchre, they told all these things to the eleven, and to all the rest.
Luke	Lk	49	24	10	And it was Mary Magdalen, and Joanna, and Mary of James, and the other women that were with them, who told these things to the apostles.
Luke	Lk	49	24	11	And these words seemed to them as idle tales; and they did not believe them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	12	But Peter rising up, ran to the sepulchre, and stooping down, he saw the linen cloths laid by themselves; and went away wondering in himself at that which was come to pass.
Luke	Lk	49	24	13	And behold, two of them went, the same day, to a town which was sixty furlongs from Jerusalem, named Emmaus.
Luke	Lk	49	24	14	And they talked together of all these things which had happened.
Luke	Lk	49	24	15	And it came to pass, that while they talked and reasoned with themselves, Jesus himself also drawing near, went with them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	16	But their eyes were held, that they should not know him.
Luke	Lk	49	24	17	And he said to them: What are these discourses that you hold one with another as you walk, and are sad?
Luke	Lk	49	24	18	And the one of them, whose name was Cleophas, answering, said to him: Art thou only a stranger to Jerusalem, and hast not known the things that have been done there in these days?
Luke	Lk	49	24	19	To whom he said: What things? And they said: Concerning Jesus of Nazareth, who was a prophet, mighty in work and word before God and all the people;
Luke	Lk	49	24	20	And how our chief priests and princes delivered him to be condemned to death, and crucified him.
Luke	Lk	49	24	21	But we hoped, that it was he that should have redeemed Israel: and now besides all this, today is the third day since these things were done.
Luke	Lk	49	24	22	Yea and certain women also of our company affrighted us, who before it was light, were at the sepulchre,
Luke	Lk	49	24	23	And not finding his body, came, saying, that they had also seen a vision of angels, who say that he is alive.
Luke	Lk	49	24	24	And some of our people went to the sepulchre, and found it so as the women had said, but him they found not.
Luke	Lk	49	24	25	Then he said to them: O foolish, and slow of heart to believe in all things which the prophets have spoken.
Luke	Lk	49	24	26	Ought not Christ to have suffered these things, and so to enter into his glory?
Luke	Lk	49	24	27	And beginning at Moses and all the prophets, he expounded to them in all the scriptures, the things that were concerning him.
Luke	Lk	49	24	28	And they drew nigh to the town, whither they were going: and he made as though he would go farther.
Luke	Lk	49	24	29	But they constrained him; saying: Stay with us, because it is towards evening, and the day is now far spent. And he went in with them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	30	And it came to pass, whilst he was at table with them, he took bread, and blessed, and brake, and gave to them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	31	And their eyes were opened, and they knew him: and he vanished out of their sight.
Luke	Lk	49	24	32	And they said one to the other: Was not our heart burning within us, whilst he spoke in this way, and opened to us the scriptures?
Luke	Lk	49	24	33	And rising up, the same hour, they went back to Jerusalem: and they found the eleven gathered together, and those that were staying with them,
Luke	Lk	49	24	34	Saying: The Lord is risen indeed, and hath appeared to Simon.
Luke	Lk	49	24	35	And they told what things were done in the way; and how they knew him in the breaking of the bread.
Luke	Lk	49	24	36	Now whilst they were speaking these things, Jesus stood in the midst of them, and saith to them: Peace be to you; it is I, fear not.
Luke	Lk	49	24	37	But they being troubled and frightened, supposed that they saw a spirit.
Luke	Lk	49	24	38	And he said to them: Why are you troubled, and why do thoughts arise in your hearts?
Luke	Lk	49	24	39	See my hands and feet, that it is I myself; handle, and see: for a spirit hath not flesh and bones, as you see me to have.
Luke	Lk	49	24	40	And when he had said this, he shewed them his hands and feet.
Luke	Lk	49	24	41	But while they yet believed not, and wondered for joy, he said: Have you any thing to eat?
Luke	Lk	49	24	42	And they offered him a piece of a broiled fish, and a honeycomb.
Luke	Lk	49	24	43	And when he had eaten before them, taking the remains, he gave to them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	44	And he said to them: These are the words which I spoke to you, while I was yet with you, that all things must needs be fulfilled, which are written in the law of Moses, and in the prophets, and in the psalms, concerning me.
Luke	Lk	49	24	45	Then he opened their understanding, that they might understand the scriptures.
Luke	Lk	49	24	46	And he said to them: Thus it is written, and thus it behoved Christ to suffer, and to rise again from the dead, the third day:
Luke	Lk	49	24	47	And that penance and remission of sins should be preached in his name, unto all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.
Luke	Lk	49	24	48	And you are witnesses of these things.
Luke	Lk	49	24	49	And I send the promise of my Father upon you: but stay you in the city till you be endued with power from on high.
Luke	Lk	49	24	50	And he led them out as far as Bethania: and lifting up his hands, he blessed them.
Luke	Lk	49	24	51	And it came to pass, whilst he blessed them, he departed from them, and was carried up to heaven.
Luke	Lk	49	24	52	And they adoring went back into Jerusalem with great joy.
Luke	Lk	49	24	53	And they were always in the temple, praising and blessing God. Amen.
John	Jn	50	1	1	In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.
John	Jn	50	1	2	The same was in the beginning with God.
John	Jn	50	1	3	All things were made by him: and without him was made nothing that was made.
John	Jn	50	1	4	In him was life, and the life was the light of men.
John	Jn	50	1	5	And the light shineth in darkness, and the darkness did not comprehend it.
John	Jn	50	1	6	There was a man sent from God, whose name was John.
John	Jn	50	1	7	This man came for a witness, to give testimony of the light, that all men might believe through him.
John	Jn	50	1	8	He was not the light, but was to give testimony of the light.
John	Jn	50	1	9	That was the true light, which enlighteneth every man that cometh into this world.
John	Jn	50	1	10	He was in the world, and the world was made by him, and the world knew him not.
John	Jn	50	1	11	He came unto his own, and his own received him not.
John	Jn	50	1	12	But as many as received him, he gave them power to be made the sons of God, to them that believe in his name.
John	Jn	50	1	13	Who are born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.
John	Jn	50	1	14	And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we saw his glory, the glory as it were of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.
John	Jn	50	1	15	John beareth witness of him, and crieth out, saying: This was he of whom I spoke: He that shall come after me, is preferred before me: because he was before me.
John	Jn	50	1	16	And of his fulness we all have received, and grace for grace.
John	Jn	50	1	17	For the law was given by Moses; grace and truth came by Jesus Christ.
John	Jn	50	1	18	No man hath seen God at any time: the only begotten Son who is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him.
John	Jn	50	1	19	And this is the testimony of John, when the Jews sent from Jerusalem priests and Levites to him, to ask him: Who art thou?
John	Jn	50	1	20	And he confessed, and did not deny: and he confessed: I am not the Christ.
John	Jn	50	1	21	And they asked him: What then? Art thou Elias? And he said: I am not. Art thou the prophet? And he answered: No.
John	Jn	50	1	22	They said therefore unto him: Who art thou, that we may give an answer to them that sent us? What sayest thou of thyself?
John	Jn	50	1	23	He said: I am the voice of one crying out in the wilderness, make straight the way of the Lord, as said the prophet Isaias.
John	Jn	50	1	24	And they that were sent, were of the Pharisees.
John	Jn	50	1	25	And they asked him, and said to him: Why then dost thou baptize, if thou be not Christ, nor Elias, nor the prophet?
John	Jn	50	1	26	John answered them, saying: I baptize with water; but there hath stood one in the midst of you, whom you know not.
John	Jn	50	1	27	The same is he that shall come after me, who is preferred before me: the latchet of whose shoe I am not worthy to loose.
John	Jn	50	1	28	These things were done in Bethania, beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing.
John	Jn	50	1	29	The next day, John saw Jesus coming to him, and he saith: Behold the Lamb of God, behold him who taketh away the sin of the world.
John	Jn	50	1	30	This is he, of whom I said: After me there cometh a man, who is preferred before me: because he was before me.
John	Jn	50	1	31	And I knew him not, but that he may be made manifest in Israel, therefore am I come baptizing with water.
John	Jn	50	1	32	And John gave testimony, saying: I saw the Spirit coming down, as a dove from heaven, and he remained upon him.
John	Jn	50	1	33	And I knew him not; but he who sent me to baptize with water, said to me: He upon whom thou shalt see the Spirit descending, and remaining upon him, he it is that baptizeth with the Holy Ghost.
John	Jn	50	1	34	And I saw, and I gave testimony, that this is the Son of God.
John	Jn	50	1	35	The next day again John stood, and two of his disciples.
John	Jn	50	1	36	And beholding Jesus walking, he saith: Behold the Lamb of God.
John	Jn	50	1	37	And the two disciples heard him speak, and they followed Jesus.
John	Jn	50	1	38	And Jesus turning, and seeing them following him, saith to them: What seek you? Who said to him, Rabbi, (which is to say, being interpreted, Master,) where dwellest thou?
John	Jn	50	1	39	He saith to them: Come and see. They came, and saw where he abode, and they stayed with him that day: now it was about the tenth hour.
John	Jn	50	1	40	And Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, was one of the two who had heard of John, and followed him.
John	Jn	50	1	41	He findeth first his brother Simon, and saith to him: We have found the Messias, which is, being interpreted, the Christ.
John	Jn	50	1	42	And he brought him to Jesus. And Jesus looking upon him, said: Thou art Simon the son of Jona: thou shalt be called Cephas, which is interpreted Peter.
John	Jn	50	1	43	On the following day, he would go forth into Galilee, and he findeth Philip. And Jesus saith to him: Follow me.
John	Jn	50	1	44	Now Philip was of Bethsaida, the city of Andrew and Peter.
John	Jn	50	1	45	Philip findeth Nathanael, and saith to him: We have found him of whom Moses in the law, and the prophets did write, Jesus the son of Joseph of Nazareth.
John	Jn	50	1	46	And Nathanael said to him: Can any thing of good come from Nazareth? Philip saith to him: Come and see.
John	Jn	50	1	47	Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him: and he saith of him: Behold an Israelite indeed, in whom there is no guile.
John	Jn	50	1	48	Nathanael saith to him: Whence knowest thou me? Jesus answered, and said to him: Before that Philip called thee, when thou wast under the fig tree, I saw thee.
John	Jn	50	1	49	Nathanael answered him, and said: Rabbi, thou art the Son of God, thou art the King of Israel.
John	Jn	50	1	50	Jesus answered, and said to him: Because I said unto thee, I saw thee under the fig tree, thou believest: greater things than these shalt thou see.
John	Jn	50	1	51	And he saith to him: Amen, amen I say to you, you shall see the heaven opened, and the angels of God ascending and descending upon the Son of man.
John	Jn	50	2	1	And the third day, there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee: and the mother of Jesus was there.
John	Jn	50	2	2	And Jesus also was invited, and his disciples, to the marriage.
John	Jn	50	2	3	And the wine failing, the mother of Jesus saith to him: They have no wine.
John	Jn	50	2	4	And Jesus saith to her: Woman, what is that to me and to thee? my hour is not yet come.
John	Jn	50	2	5	His mother saith to the waiters: Whatsoever he shall say to you, do ye.
John	Jn	50	2	6	Now there were set there six waterpots of stone, according to the manner of the purifying of the Jews, containing two or three measures apiece.
John	Jn	50	2	7	Jesus saith to them: Fill the waterpots with water. And they filled them up to the brim.
John	Jn	50	2	8	And Jesus saith to them: Draw out now, and carry to the chief steward of the feast. And they carried it.
John	Jn	50	2	9	And when the chief steward had tasted the water made wine, and knew not whence it was, but the waiters knew who had drawn the water; the chief steward calleth the bridegroom,
John	Jn	50	2	10	And saith to him: Every man at first setteth forth good wine, and when men have well drunk, then that which is worse. But thou hast kept the good wine until now.
John	Jn	50	2	11	This beginning of miracles did Jesus in Cana of Galilee; and manifested his glory, and his disciples believed in him.
John	Jn	50	2	12	After this he went down to Capharnaum, he and his mother, and his brethren, and his disciples: and they remained there not many days.
John	Jn	50	2	13	And the pasch of the Jews was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.
John	Jn	50	2	14	And he found in the temple them that sold oxen and sheep and doves, and the changers of money sitting.
John	Jn	50	2	15	And when he had made, as it were, a scourge of little cords, he drove them all out of the temple, the sheep also and the oxen, and the money of the changers he poured out, and the tables he overthrew.
John	Jn	50	2	16	And to them that sold doves he said: Take these things hence, and make not the house of my Father a house of traffic.
John	Jn	50	2	17	And his disciples remembered, that it was written: The zeal of thy house hath eaten me up.
John	Jn	50	2	18	The Jews, therefore, answered, and said to him: What sign dost thou shew unto us, seeing thou dost these things?
John	Jn	50	2	19	Jesus answered, and said to them: Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.
John	Jn	50	2	20	The Jews then said: Six and forty years was this temple in building; and wilt thou raise it up in three days?
John	Jn	50	2	21	But he spoke of the temple of his body.
John	Jn	50	2	22	When therefore he was risen again from the dead, his disciples remembered, that he had said this, and they believed the scripture, and the word that Jesus had said.
John	Jn	50	2	23	Now when he was at Jerusalem, at the pasch, upon the festival day, many believed in his name, seeing his signs which he did.
John	Jn	50	2	24	But Jesus did not trust himself unto them, for that he knew all men,
John	Jn	50	2	25	And because he needed not that any should give testimony of man: for he knew what was in man.
John	Jn	50	3	1	And there was a man of the Pharisees, named Nicodemus, a ruler of the Jews.
John	Jn	50	3	2	This man came to Jesus by night, and said to him: Rabbi, we know that thou art come a teacher from God; for no man can do these signs which thou dost, unless God be with him.
John	Jn	50	3	3	Jesus answered, and said to him: Amen, amen I say to thee, unless a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God.
John	Jn	50	3	4	Nicodemus saith to him: How can a man be born when he is old? can he enter a second time into his mother's womb, and be born again?
John	Jn	50	3	5	Jesus answered: Amen, amen I say to thee, unless a man be born again of water and the Holy Ghost, he cannot enter into the kingdom of God.
John	Jn	50	3	6	That which is born of the flesh, is flesh; and that which is born of the Spirit, is spirit.
John	Jn	50	3	7	Wonder not, that I said to thee, you must be born again.
John	Jn	50	3	8	The Spirit breatheth where he will; and thou hearest his voice, but thou knowest not whence he cometh, and whither he goeth: so is every one that is born of the Spirit.
John	Jn	50	3	9	Nicodemus answered, and said to him: How can these things be done?
John	Jn	50	3	10	Jesus answered, and said to him: Art thou a master in Israel, and knowest not these things?
John	Jn	50	3	11	Amen, amen I say to thee, that we speak what we know, and we testify what we have seen, and you receive not our testimony.
John	Jn	50	3	12	If I have spoken to you earthly things, and you believe not; how will you believe, if I shall speak to you heavenly things?
John	Jn	50	3	13	And no man hath ascended into heaven, but he that descended from heaven, the Son of man who is in heaven.
John	Jn	50	3	14	And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the desert, so must the Son of man be lifted up:
John	Jn	50	3	15	That whosoever believeth in him, may not perish; but may have life everlasting.
John	Jn	50	3	16	For God so loved the world, as to give his only begotten Son; that whosoever believeth in him, may not perish, but may have life everlasting.
John	Jn	50	3	17	For God sent not his Son into the world, to judge the world, but that the world may be saved by him.
John	Jn	50	3	18	He that believeth in him is not judged. But he that doth not believe, is already judged: because he believeth not in the name of the only begotten Son of God.
John	Jn	50	3	19	And this is the judgment: because the light is come into the world, and men loved darkness rather than the light: for their works were evil.
John	Jn	50	3	20	For every one that doth evil hateth the light, and cometh not to the light, that his works may not be reproved.
John	Jn	50	3	21	But he that doth truth, cometh to the light, that his works may be made manifest, because they are done in God.
John	Jn	50	3	22	After these things Jesus and his disciples came into the land of Judea: and there he abode with them, and baptized.
John	Jn	50	3	23	And John also was baptizing in Ennon near Salim; because there was much water there; and they came and were baptized.
John	Jn	50	3	24	For John was not yet cast into prison.
John	Jn	50	3	25	And there arose a question between some of John's disciples and the Jews concerning purification:
John	Jn	50	3	26	And they came to John, and said to him: Rabbi, he that was with thee beyond the Jordan, to whom thou gavest testimony, behold he baptizeth, and all men come to him.
John	Jn	50	3	27	John answered, and said: A man cannot receive any thing, unless it be given him from heaven.
John	Jn	50	3	28	You yourselves do bear me witness, that I said, I am not Christ, but that I am sent before him.
John	Jn	50	3	29	He that hath the bride, is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, who standeth and heareth him, rejoiceth with joy because of the bridegroom's voice. This my joy therefore is fulfilled.
John	Jn	50	3	30	He must increase, but I must decrease.
John	Jn	50	3	31	He that cometh from above, is above all. He that is of the earth, of the earth he is, and of the earth he speaketh. He that cometh from heaven, is above all.
John	Jn	50	3	32	And what he hath seen and heard, that he testifieth: and no man receiveth his testimony.
John	Jn	50	3	33	He that hath received his testimony, hath set to his seal that God is true.
John	Jn	50	3	34	For he whom God hath sent, speaketh the words of God: for God doth not give the Spirit by measure.
John	Jn	50	3	35	The Father loveth the Son: and he hath given all things into his hand.
John	Jn	50	3	36	He that believeth in the Son, hath life everlasting; but he that believeth not the Son, shall not see life; but the wrath of God abideth on him.
John	Jn	50	4	1	When Jesus therefore understood that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus maketh more disciples, and baptizeth more than John,
John	Jn	50	4	2	(Though Jesus himself did not baptize, but his disciples,)
John	Jn	50	4	3	He left Judea, and went again into Galilee.
John	Jn	50	4	4	And he was of necessity to pass through Samaria.
John	Jn	50	4	5	He cometh therefore to a city of Samaria, which is called Sichar, near the land which Jacob gave to his son Joseph.
John	Jn	50	4	6	Now Jacob's well was there. Jesus therefore being wearied with his journey, sat thus on the well. It was about the sixth hour.
John	Jn	50	4	7	There cometh a woman of Samaria, to draw water. Jesus saith to her: Give me to drink.
John	Jn	50	4	8	For his disciples were gone into the city to buy meats.
John	Jn	50	4	9	Then that Samaritan woman saith to him: How dost thou, being a Jew, ask of me to drink, who am a Samaritan woman? For the Jews do not communicate with the Samaritans.
John	Jn	50	4	10	Jesus answered, and said to her: If thou didst know the gift of God, and who he is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou perhaps wouldst have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water.
John	Jn	50	4	11	The woman saith to him: Sir, thou hast nothing wherein to draw, and the well is deep; from whence then hast thou living water?
John	Jn	50	4	12	Art thou greater than our father Jacob, who gave us the well, and drank thereof himself, and his children, and his cattle?
John	Jn	50	4	13	Jesus answered, and said to her: Whosoever drinketh of this water, shall thirst again; but he that shall drink of the water that I will give him, shall not thirst for ever:
John	Jn	50	4	14	But the water that I will give him, shall become in him a fountain of water, springing up into life everlasting.
John	Jn	50	4	15	The woman saith to him: Sir, give me this water, that I may not thirst, nor come hither to draw.
John	Jn	50	4	16	Jesus saith to her: Go, call thy husband, and come hither.
John	Jn	50	4	17	The woman answered, and said: I have no husband. Jesus said to her: Thou hast said well, I have no husband:
John	Jn	50	4	18	For thou hast had five husbands: and he whom thou now hast, is not thy husband. This thou hast said truly.
John	Jn	50	4	19	The woman saith to him: Sir, I perceive that thou art a prophet.
John	Jn	50	4	20	Our fathers adored on this mountain, and you say, that at Jerusalem is the place where men must adore.
John	Jn	50	4	21	Jesus saith to her: Woman, believe me, that the hour cometh, when you shall neither on this mountain, nor in Jerusalem, adore the Father.
John	Jn	50	4	22	You adore that which you know not: we adore that which we know; for salvation is of the Jews.
John	Jn	50	4	23	But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true adorers shall adore the Father in spirit and in truth. For the Father also seeketh such to adore him.
John	Jn	50	4	24	God is a spirit; and they that adore him, must adore him in spirit and in truth.
John	Jn	50	4	25	The woman saith to him: I know that the Messias cometh (who is called Christ). Therefore, when he is come, he will tell us all things.
John	Jn	50	4	26	Jesus saith to her: I am he, who am speaking with thee.
John	Jn	50	4	27	And immediately his disciples came; and they wondered that he talked with the woman. Yet no man said: What seekest thou? or, why talkest thou with her?
John	Jn	50	4	28	The woman therefore left her waterpot, and went her way into the city, and saith to the men there:
John	Jn	50	4	29	Come, and see a man who has told me all things whatsoever I have done. Is not he the Christ?
John	Jn	50	4	30	They went therefore out of the city, and came unto him.
John	Jn	50	4	31	In the mean time the disciples prayed him, saying: Rabbi, eat.
John	Jn	50	4	32	But he said to them: I have meat to eat, which you know not.
John	Jn	50	4	33	The disciples therefore said one to another: Hath any man brought him to eat?
John	Jn	50	4	34	Jesus saith to them: My meat is to do the will of him that sent me, that I may perfect his work.
John	Jn	50	4	35	Do you not say, There are yet four months, and then the harvest cometh? Behold, I say to you, lift up your eyes, and see the countries; for they are white already to harvest.
John	Jn	50	4	36	And he that reapeth receiveth wages, and gathereth fruit unto life everlasting: that both he that soweth, and he that reapeth, may rejoice together.
John	Jn	50	4	37	For in this is the saying true: That it is one man that soweth, and it is another that reapeth.
John	Jn	50	4	38	I have sent you to reap that in which you did not labour: others have laboured, and you have entered into their labours.
John	Jn	50	4	39	Now of that city many of the Samaritans believed in him, for the word of the woman giving testimony: He told me all things whatsoever I have done.
John	Jn	50	4	40	So when the Samaritans were come to him, they desired that he would tarry there. And he abode there two days.
John	Jn	50	4	41	And many more believed in him because of his own word.
John	Jn	50	4	42	And they said to the woman: We now believe, not for thy saying: for we ourselves have heard him, and know that this is indeed the Saviour of the world.
John	Jn	50	4	43	Now after two days, he departed thence, and went into Galilee.
John	Jn	50	4	44	For Jesus himself gave testimony that a prophet hath no honour in his own country.
John	Jn	50	4	45	And when he was come into Galilee, the Galileans received him, having seen all the things he had done at Jerusalem on the festival day; for they also went to the festival day.
John	Jn	50	4	46	He came again therefore into Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain ruler, whose son was sick at Capharnaum.
John	Jn	50	4	47	He having heard that Jesus was come from Judea into Galilee, went to him, and prayed him to come down, and heal his son; for he was at the point of death.
John	Jn	50	4	48	Jesus therefore said to him: Unless you see signs and wonders, you believe not.
John	Jn	50	4	49	The ruler saith to him: Lord, come down before that my son die.
John	Jn	50	4	50	Jesus saith to him: Go thy way; thy son liveth. The man believed the word which Jesus said to him, and went his way.
John	Jn	50	4	51	And as he was going down, his servants met him; and they brought word, saying, that his son lived.
John	Jn	50	4	52	He asked therefore of them the hour wherein he grew better. And they said to him: Yesterday, at the seventh hour, the fever left him.
John	Jn	50	4	53	The father therefore knew, that it was at the same hour that Jesus said to him, Thy son liveth; and himself believed, and his whole house.
John	Jn	50	4	54	This is again the second miracle that Jesus did, when he was come out of Judea into Galilee.
John	Jn	50	5	1	After these things was a festival day of the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.
John	Jn	50	5	2	Now there is at Jerusalem a pond, called Probatica, which in Hebrew is named Bethsaida, having five porches.
John	Jn	50	5	3	In these lay a great multitude of sick, of blind, of lame, of withered; waiting for the moving of the water.
John	Jn	50	5	4	And an angel of the Lord descended at certain times into the pond; and the water was moved. And he that went down first into the pond after the motion of the water, was made whole, of whatsoever infirmity he lay under.
John	Jn	50	5	5	And there was a certain man there, that had been eight and thirty years under his infirmity.
John	Jn	50	5	6	Him when Jesus had seen lying, and knew that he had been now a long time, he saith to him: Wilt thou be made whole?
John	Jn	50	5	7	The infirm man answered him: Sir, I have no man, when the water is troubled, to put me into the pond. For whilst I am coming, another goeth down before me.
John	Jn	50	5	8	Jesus saith to him: Arise, take up thy bed, and walk.
John	Jn	50	5	9	And immediately the man was made whole: and he took up his bed, and walked. And it was the sabbath that day.
John	Jn	50	5	10	The Jews therefore said to him that was healed: It is the sabbath; it is not lawful for thee to take up thy bed.
John	Jn	50	5	11	He answered them: He that made me whole, he said to me, Take up thy bed, and walk.
John	Jn	50	5	12	They asked him therefore: Who is that man who said to thee, Take up thy bed, and walk?
John	Jn	50	5	13	But he who was healed, knew not who it was; for Jesus went aside from the multitude standing in the place.
John	Jn	50	5	14	Afterwards, Jesus findeth him in the temple, and saith to him: Behold thou art made whole: sin no more, lest some worse thing happen to thee.
John	Jn	50	5	15	The man went his way, and told the Jews, that it was Jesus who had made him whole.
John	Jn	50	5	16	Therefore did the Jews persecute Jesus, because he did these things on the sabbath.
John	Jn	50	5	17	But Jesus answered them: My Father worketh until now; and I work.
John	Jn	50	5	18	Hereupon therefore the Jews sought the more to kill him, because he did not only break the sabbath, but also said God was his Father, making himself equal to God.
John	Jn	50	5	19	Then Jesus answered, and said to them: Amen, amen, I say unto you, the Son cannot do any thing of himself, but what he seeth the Father doing: for what things soever he doth, these the Son also doth in like manner.
John	Jn	50	5	20	For the Father loveth the Son, and sheweth him all things which himself doth: and greater works than these will he shew him, that you may wonder.
John	Jn	50	5	21	For as the Father raiseth up the dead, and giveth life: so the Son also giveth life to whom he will.
John	Jn	50	5	22	For neither doth the Father judge any man, but hath given all judgment to the Son.
John	Jn	50	5	23	That all men may honour the Son, as they honour the Father. He who honoureth not the Son, honoureth not the Father, who hath sent him.
John	Jn	50	5	24	Amen, amen I say unto you, that he who heareth my word, and believeth him that sent me, hath life everlasting; and cometh not into judgment, but is passed from death to life.
John	Jn	50	5	25	Amen, amen I say unto you, that the hour cometh, and now is, when the dead shall hear the voice of the Son of God, and they that hear shall live.
John	Jn	50	5	26	For as the Father hath life in himself, so he hath given the Son also to have life in himself:
John	Jn	50	5	27	And he hath given him power to do judgment, because he is the Son of man.
John	Jn	50	5	28	Wonder not at this; for the hour cometh, wherein all that are in the graves shall hear the voice of the Son of God.
John	Jn	50	5	29	And they that have done good things, shall come forth unto the resurrection of life; but they that have done evil, unto the resurrection of judgment.
John	Jn	50	5	30	I cannot of myself do any thing. As I hear, so I judge: and my judgment is just; because I seek not my own will, but the will of him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	5	31	If I bear witness of myself, my witness is not true.
John	Jn	50	5	32	There is another that beareth witness of me; and I know that the witness which he witnesseth of me is true.
John	Jn	50	5	33	You sent to John, and he gave testimony to the truth.
John	Jn	50	5	34	But I receive not testimony from man: but I say these things, that you may be saved.
John	Jn	50	5	35	He was a burning and a shining light: and you were willing for a time to rejoice in his light.
John	Jn	50	5	36	But I have a greater testimony than that of John: for the works which the Father hath given me to perfect; the works themselves, which I do, give testimony of me, that the Father hath sent me.
John	Jn	50	5	37	And the Father himself who hath sent me, hath given testimony of me: neither have you heard his voice at any time, nor seen his shape.
John	Jn	50	5	38	And you have not his word abiding in you: for whom he hath sent, him you believe not.
John	Jn	50	5	39	Search the scriptures, for you think in them to have life everlasting; and the same are they that give testimony of me.
John	Jn	50	5	40	And you will not come to me that you may have life.
John	Jn	50	5	41	I receive glory not from men.
John	Jn	50	5	42	But I know you, that you have not the love of God in you.
John	Jn	50	5	43	I am come in the name of my Father, and you receive me not: if another shall come in his own name, him you will receive.
John	Jn	50	5	44	How can you believe, who receive glory one from another: and the glory which is from God alone, you do not seek?
John	Jn	50	5	45	Think not that I will accuse you to the Father. There is one that accuseth you, Moses, in whom you trust.
John	Jn	50	5	46	For if you did believe Moses, you would perhaps believe me also; for he wrote of me.
John	Jn	50	5	47	But if you do not believe his writings, how will you believe my words?
John	Jn	50	6	1	After these things Jesus went over the sea of Galilee, which is that of Tiberias.
John	Jn	50	6	2	And a great multitude followed him, because they saw the miracles which he did on them that were diseased.
John	Jn	50	6	3	Jesus therefore went up into a mountain, and there he sat with his disciples.
John	Jn	50	6	4	Now the pasch, the festival day of the Jews, was near at hand.
John	Jn	50	6	5	When Jesus therefore had lifted up his eyes, and seen that a very great multitude cometh to him, he said to Philip: Whence shall we buy bread, that these may eat?
John	Jn	50	6	6	And this he said to try him; for he himself knew what he would do.
John	Jn	50	6	7	Philip answered him: Two hundred pennyworth of bread is not sufficient for them, that every one may take a little.
John	Jn	50	6	8	One of his disciples, Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, saith to him:
John	Jn	50	6	9	There is a boy here that hath five barley loaves, and two fishes; but what are these among so many?
John	Jn	50	6	10	Then Jesus said: Make the men sit down. Now there was much grass in the place. The men therefore sat down, in number about five thousand.
John	Jn	50	6	11	And Jesus took the loaves: and when he had given thanks, he distributed to them that were set down. In like manner also of the fishes, as much as they would.
John	Jn	50	6	12	And when they were filled, he said to his disciples: Gather up the fragments that remain, lest they be lost.
John	Jn	50	6	13	They gathered up therefore, and filled twelve baskets with the fragments of the five barley loaves, which remained over and above to them that had eaten.
John	Jn	50	6	14	Now those men, when they had seen what a miracle Jesus had done, said: This is of a truth the prophet, that is to come into the world.
John	Jn	50	6	15	Jesus therefore, when he knew that they would come to take him by force, and make him king, fled again into the mountain himself alone.
John	Jn	50	6	16	And when evening was come, his disciples went down to the sea.
John	Jn	50	6	17	And when they had gone up into a ship, they went over the sea to Capharnaum; and it was now dark, and Jesus was not come unto them.
John	Jn	50	6	18	And the sea arose, by reason of a great wind that blew.
John	Jn	50	6	19	When they had rowed therefore about five and twenty or thirty furlongs, they see Jesus walking upon the sea, and drawing nigh to the ship, and they were afraid.
John	Jn	50	6	20	But he saith to them: It is I; be not afraid.
John	Jn	50	6	21	They were willing therefore to take him into the ship; and presently the ship was at the land to which they were going.
John	Jn	50	6	22	The next day, the multitude that stood on the other side of the sea, saw that there was no other ship there but one, and that Jesus had not entered into the ship with his disciples, but that his disciples were gone away alone.
John	Jn	50	6	23	But other ships came in from Tiberias; nigh unto the place where they had eaten the bread, the Lord giving thanks.
John	Jn	50	6	24	When therefore the multitude saw that Jesus was not there, nor his disciples, they took shipping, and came to Capharnaum, seeking for Jesus.
John	Jn	50	6	25	And when they had found him on the other side of the sea, they said to him: Rabbi, when camest thou hither?
John	Jn	50	6	26	Jesus answered them, and said: Amen, amen I say to you, you seek me, not because you have seen miracles, but because you did eat of the loaves, and were filled.
John	Jn	50	6	27	Labour not for the meat which perisheth, but for that which endureth unto life everlasting, which the Son of man will give you. For him hath God, the Father, sealed.
John	Jn	50	6	28	They said therefore unto him: What shall we do, that we may work the works of God?
John	Jn	50	6	29	Jesus answered, and said to them: This is the work of God, that you believe in him whom he hath sent.
John	Jn	50	6	30	They said therefore to him: What sign therefore dost thou shew, that we may see, and may believe thee? What dost thou work?
John	Jn	50	6	31	Our fathers did eat manna in the desert, as it is written: He gave them bread from heaven to eat.
John	Jn	50	6	32	Then Jesus said to them: Amen, amen I say to you; Moses gave you not bread from heaven, but my Father giveth you the true bread from heaven.
John	Jn	50	6	33	For the bread of God is that which cometh down from heaven, and giveth life to the world.
John	Jn	50	6	34	They said therefore unto him: Lord, give us always this bread.
John	Jn	50	6	35	And Jesus said to them: I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall not hunger: and he that believeth in me shall never thirst.
John	Jn	50	6	36	But I said unto you, that you also have seen me, and you believe not.
John	Jn	50	6	37	All that the Father giveth to me shall come to me; and him that cometh to me, I will not cast out.
John	Jn	50	6	38	Because I came down from heaven, not to do my own will, but the will of him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	6	39	Now this is the will of the Father who sent me: that of all that he hath given me, I should lose nothing; but should raise it up again in the last day.
John	Jn	50	6	40	And this is the will of my Father that sent me: that every one who seeth the Son, and believeth in him, may have life everlasting, and I will raise him up in the last day.
John	Jn	50	6	41	The Jews therefore murmured at him, because he had said: I am the living bread which came down from heaven.
John	Jn	50	6	42	And they said: Is not this Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then saith he, I came down from heaven?
John	Jn	50	6	43	Jesus therefore answered, and said to them: Murmur not among yourselves.
John	Jn	50	6	44	No man can come to me, except the Father, who hath sent me, draw him; and I will raise him up in the last day.
John	Jn	50	6	45	It is written in the prophets: And they shall all be taught of God. Every one that hath heard of the Father, and hath learned, cometh to me.
John	Jn	50	6	46	Not that any man hath seen the Father; but he who is of God, he hath seen the Father.
John	Jn	50	6	47	Amen, amen I say unto you: He that believeth in me, hath everlasting life.
John	Jn	50	6	48	I am the bread of life.
John	Jn	50	6	49	Your fathers did eat manna in the desert, and are dead.
John	Jn	50	6	50	This is the bread which cometh down from heaven; that if any man eat of it, he may not die.
John	Jn	50	6	51	I am the living bread which came down from heaven.
John	Jn	50	6	52	If any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever; and the bread that I will give, is my flesh, for the life of the world.
John	Jn	50	6	53	The Jews therefore strove among themselves, saying: How can this man give us his flesh to eat?
John	Jn	50	6	54	Then Jesus said to them: Amen, amen I say unto you: Except you eat the flesh of the Son of man, and drink his blood, you shall not have life in you.
John	Jn	50	6	55	He that eateth my flesh, and drinketh my blood, hath everlasting life: and I will raise him up in the last day.
John	Jn	50	6	56	For my flesh is meat indeed: and my blood is drink indeed.
John	Jn	50	6	57	He that eateth my flesh, and drinketh my blood, abideth in me, and I in him.
John	Jn	50	6	58	As the living Father hath sent me, and I live by the Father; so he that eateth me, the same also shall live by me.
John	Jn	50	6	59	This is the bread that came down from heaven. Not as your fathers did eat manna, and are dead. He that eateth this bread, shall live for ever.
John	Jn	50	6	60	These things he said, teaching in the synagogue, in Capharnaum.
John	Jn	50	6	61	Many therefore of his disciples, hearing it, said: This saying is hard, and who can hear it?
John	Jn	50	6	62	But Jesus, knowing in himself, that his disciples murmured at this, said to them: Doth this scandalize you?
John	Jn	50	6	63	If then you shall see the Son of man ascend up where he was before?
John	Jn	50	6	64	It is the spirit that quickeneth: the flesh profiteth nothing. The words that I have spoken to you, are spirit and life.
John	Jn	50	6	65	But there are some of you that believe not. For Jesus knew from the beginning, who they were that did not believe, and who he was, that would betray him.
John	Jn	50	6	66	And he said: Therefore did I say to you, that no man can come to me, unless it be given him by my Father.
John	Jn	50	6	67	After this many of his disciples went back; and walked no more with him.
John	Jn	50	6	68	Then Jesus said to the twelve: Will you also go away?
John	Jn	50	6	69	And Simon Peter answered him: Lord, to whom shall we go? thou hast the words of eternal life.
John	Jn	50	6	70	And we have believed and have known, that thou art the Christ, the Son of God.
John	Jn	50	6	71	Jesus answered them: Have not I chosen you twelve; and one of you is a devil?
John	Jn	50	6	72	Now he meant Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon: for this same was about to betray him, whereas he was one of the twelve.
John	Jn	50	7	1	After these things Jesus walked in Galilee; for he would not walk in Judea, because the Jews sought to kill him.
John	Jn	50	7	2	Now the Jews' feast of tabernacles was at hand.
John	Jn	50	7	3	And his brethren said to him: Pass from hence, and go into Judea; that thy disciples also may see thy works which thou dost.
John	Jn	50	7	4	For there is no man that doth any thing in secret, and he himself seeketh to be known openly. If thou do these things, manifest thyself to the world.
John	Jn	50	7	5	For neither did his brethren believe in him.
John	Jn	50	7	6	Then Jesus said to them: My time is not yet come; but your time is always ready.
John	Jn	50	7	7	The world cannot hate you; but me it hateth: because I give testimony of it, that the works thereof are evil.
John	Jn	50	7	8	Go you up to this festival day, but I go not up to this festival day: because my time is not accomplished.
John	Jn	50	7	9	When he had said these things, he himself stayed in Galilee.
John	Jn	50	7	10	But after his brethren were gone up, then he also went up to the feast, not openly, but, as it were, in secret.
John	Jn	50	7	11	The Jews therefore sought him on the festival day, and said: Where is he?
John	Jn	50	7	12	And there was much murmuring among the multitude concerning him. For some said: He is a good man. And others said: No, but he seduceth the people.
John	Jn	50	7	13	Yet no man spoke openly of him, for fear of the Jews.
John	Jn	50	7	14	Now about the midst of the feast, Jesus went up into the temple, and taught.
John	Jn	50	7	15	And the Jews wondered, saying: How doth this man know letters, having never learned?
John	Jn	50	7	16	Jesus answered them, and said: My doctrine is not mine, but his that sent me.
John	Jn	50	7	17	If any man do the will of him; he shall know of the doctrine, whether it be of God, or whether I speak of myself.
John	Jn	50	7	18	He that speaketh of himself, seeketh his own glory: but he that seeketh the glory of him that sent him, he is true, and there is no injustice in him.
John	Jn	50	7	19	Did Moses not give you the law, and yet none of you keepeth the law?
John	Jn	50	7	20	Why seek you to kill me? The multitude answered, and said: Thou hast a devil; who seeketh to kill thee?
John	Jn	50	7	21	Jesus answered, and said to them: One work I have done; and you all wonder:
John	Jn	50	7	22	Therefore, Moses gave you circumcision (not because it is of Moses, but of the fathers;) and on the sabbath day you circumcise a man.
John	Jn	50	7	23	If a man receive circumcision on the sabbath day, that the law of Moses may not be broken; are you angry at me because I have healed the whole man on the sabbath day?
John	Jn	50	7	24	Judge not according to the appearance, but judge just judgment.
John	Jn	50	7	25	Some therefore of Jerusalem said: Is not this he whom they seek to kill?
John	Jn	50	7	26	And behold, he speaketh openly, and they say nothing to him. Have the rulers known for a truth, that this is the Christ?
John	Jn	50	7	27	But we know this man, whence he is: but when the Christ cometh, no man knoweth whence he is.
John	Jn	50	7	28	Jesus therefore cried out in the temple, teaching, and saying: You both know me, and you know whence I am: and I am not come of myself; but he that sent me, is true, whom you know not.
John	Jn	50	7	29	I know him, because I am from him, and he hath sent me.
John	Jn	50	7	30	They sought therefore to apprehend him: and no man laid hands on him, because his hour was not yet come.
John	Jn	50	7	31	But of the people many believed in him, and said: When the Christ cometh, shall he do more miracles, than these which this man doth?
John	Jn	50	7	32	The Pharisees heard the people murmuring these things concerning him: and the rulers and Pharisees sent ministers to apprehend him.
John	Jn	50	7	33	Jesus therefore said to them: Yet a little while I am with you: and then I go to him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	7	34	You shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, thither you cannot come.
John	Jn	50	7	35	The Jews therefore said among themselves: Whither will he go, that we shall not find him? will he go unto the dispersed among the Gentiles, and teach the Gentiles?
John	Jn	50	7	36	What is this saying that he hath said: You shall seek me, and shall not find me; and where I am, you cannot come?
John	Jn	50	7	37	And on the last, and great day of the festivity, Jesus stood and cried, saying: If any man thirst, let him come to me, and drink.
John	Jn	50	7	38	He that believeth in me, as the scripture saith, Out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.
John	Jn	50	7	39	Now this he said of the Spirit which they should receive, who believed in him: for as yet the Spirit was not given, because Jesus was not yet glorified.
John	Jn	50	7	40	Of that multitude therefore, when they had heard these words of his, some said: This is the prophet indeed.
John	Jn	50	7	41	Others said: This is the Christ. But some said: Doth the Christ come out of Galilee?
John	Jn	50	7	42	Doth not the scripture say: That Christ cometh of the seed of David, and from Bethlehem the town where David was?
John	Jn	50	7	43	So there arose a dissension among the people because of him.
John	Jn	50	7	44	And some of them would have apprehended him: but no man laid hands on him.
John	Jn	50	7	45	The ministers therefore came to the chief priests and the Pharisees. And they said to them: Why have you not brought him?
John	Jn	50	7	46	The ministers answered: Never did man speak like this man.
John	Jn	50	7	47	The Pharisees therefore answered them: Are you also seduced?
John	Jn	50	7	48	Hath any one of the rulers believed in him, or of the Pharisees?
John	Jn	50	7	49	But this multitude, that knoweth not the law, are accursed.
John	Jn	50	7	50	Nicodemus said to them, (he that came to him by night, who was one of them:)
John	Jn	50	7	51	Doth our law judge any man, unless it first hear him, and know what he doth?
John	Jn	50	7	52	They answered, and said to him: Art thou also a Galilean? Search the scriptures, and see, that out of Galilee a prophet riseth not.
John	Jn	50	7	53	And every man returned to his own house.
John	Jn	50	8	1	And Jesus went unto mount Olivet.
John	Jn	50	8	2	And early in the morning he came again into the temple, and all the people came to him, and sitting down he taught them.
John	Jn	50	8	3	And the scribes and the Pharisees bring unto him a woman taken in adultery: and they set her in the midst,
John	Jn	50	8	4	And said to him: Master, this woman was even now taken in adultery.
John	Jn	50	8	5	Now Moses in the law commanded us to stone such a one. But what sayest thou?
John	Jn	50	8	6	And this they said tempting him, that they might accuse him. But Jesus bowing himself down, wrote with his finger on the ground.
John	Jn	50	8	7	When therefore they continued asking him, he lifted up himself, and said to them: He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone at her.
John	Jn	50	8	8	And again stooping down, he wrote on the ground.
John	Jn	50	8	9	But they hearing this, went out one by one, beginning at the eldest. And Jesus alone remained, and the woman standing in the midst.
John	Jn	50	8	10	Then Jesus lifting up himself, said to her: Woman, where are they that accused thee? Hath no man condemned thee?
John	Jn	50	8	11	Who said: No man, Lord. And Jesus said: Neither will I condemn thee. Go, and now sin no more.
John	Jn	50	8	12	Again therefore, Jesus spoke to them, saying: I am the light of the world: he that followeth me, walketh not in darkness, but shall have the light of life.
John	Jn	50	8	13	The Pharisees therefore said to him: Thou givest testimony of thyself: thy testimony is not true.
John	Jn	50	8	14	Jesus answered, and said to them: Although I give testimony of myself, my testimony is true: for I know whence I came, and whither I go: but you know not whence I come, or whither I go.
John	Jn	50	8	15	You judge according to the flesh: I judge not any man.
John	Jn	50	8	16	And if I do judge, my judgment is true: because I am not alone, but I and the Father that sent me.
John	Jn	50	8	17	And in your law it is written, that the testimony of two men is true.
John	Jn	50	8	18	I am one that give testimony of myself: and the Father that sent me giveth testimony of me.
John	Jn	50	8	19	They said therefore to him: Where is thy Father? Jesus answered: Neither me do you know, nor my Father: if you did know me, perhaps you would know my Father also.
John	Jn	50	8	20	These words Jesus spoke in the treasury, teaching in the temple: and no man laid hands on him, because his hour was not yet come.
John	Jn	50	8	21	Again therefore Jesus said to them: I go, and you shall seek me, and you shall die in your sin. Whither I go, you cannot come.
John	Jn	50	8	22	The Jews therefore said: Will he kill himself, because he said: Whither I go, you cannot come?
John	Jn	50	8	23	And he said to them: You are from beneath, I am from above. You are of this world, I am not of this world.
John	Jn	50	8	24	Therefore I said to you, that you shall die in your sins. For if you believe not that I am he, you shall die in your sin.
John	Jn	50	8	25	They said therefore to him: Who art thou? Jesus said to them: The beginning, who also speak unto you.
John	Jn	50	8	26	Many things I have to speak and to judge of you. But he that sent me, is true: and the things I have heard of him, these same I speak in the world.
John	Jn	50	8	27	And they understood not, that he called God his Father.
John	Jn	50	8	28	Jesus therefore said to them: When you shall have lifted up the Son of man, then shall you know, that I am he, and that I do nothing of myself, but as the Father hath taught me, these things I speak:
John	Jn	50	8	29	And he that sent me, is with me, and he hath not left me alone: for I do always the things that please him.
John	Jn	50	8	30	When he spoke these things, many believed in him.
John	Jn	50	8	31	Then Jesus said to those Jews, who believed him: If you continue in my word, you shall be my disciples indeed.
John	Jn	50	8	32	And you shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.
John	Jn	50	8	33	They answered him: We are the seed of Abraham, and we have never been slaves to any man: how sayest thou: you shall be free?
John	Jn	50	8	34	Jesus answered them: Amen, amen I say unto you: that whosoever committeth sin, is the servant of sin.
John	Jn	50	8	35	Now the servant abideth not in the house for ever; but the son abideth for ever.
John	Jn	50	8	36	If therefore the son shall make you free, you shall be free indeed.
John	Jn	50	8	37	I know that you are the children of Abraham: but you seek to kill me, because my word hath no place in you.
John	Jn	50	8	38	I speak that which I have seen with my Father: and you do the things that you have seen with your father.
John	Jn	50	8	39	They answered, and said to him: Abraham is our father. Jesus saith to them: If you be the children of Abraham, do the works of Abraham.
John	Jn	50	8	40	But now you seek to kill me, a man who have spoken the truth to you, which I have heard of God. This Abraham did not.
John	Jn	50	8	41	You do the works of your father. They said therefore to him: We are not born of fornication: we have one Father, even God.
John	Jn	50	8	42	Jesus therefore said to them: If God were your Father, you would indeed love me. For from God I proceeded, and came; for I came not of myself, but he sent me:
John	Jn	50	8	43	Why do you not know my speech? Because you cannot hear my word.
John	Jn	50	8	44	You are of your father the devil, and the desires of your father you will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and he stood not in the truth; because truth is not in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father thereof.
John	Jn	50	8	45	But if I say the truth, you believe me not.
John	Jn	50	8	46	Which of you shall convict me of sin? If I say the truth to you, why do you not believe me?
John	Jn	50	8	47	He that is of God, heareth the words of God. Therefore you hear them not, because you are not of God.
John	Jn	50	8	48	The Jews therefore answered, and said to him: Do not we say well that thou art a Samaritan, and hast a devil?
John	Jn	50	8	49	Jesus answered: I have not a devil: but I honour my Father, and you have dishonoured me.
John	Jn	50	8	50	But I seek not my own glory: there is one that seeketh and judgeth.
John	Jn	50	8	51	Amen, amen I say to you: If any man keep my word, he shall not see death for ever.
John	Jn	50	8	52	The Jews therefore said: Now we know that thou hast a devil. Abraham is dead, and the prophets; and thou sayest: If any man keep my word, he shall not taste death for ever.
John	Jn	50	8	53	Art thou greater than our father Abraham, who is dead? and the prophets are dead. Whom dost thou make thyself?
John	Jn	50	8	54	Jesus answered: If I glorify myself, my glory is nothing. It is my Father that glorifieth me, of whom you say that he is your God.
John	Jn	50	8	55	And you have not known him, but I know him. And if I shall say that I know him not, I shall be like to you, a liar. But I do know him, and do keep his word.
John	Jn	50	8	56	Abraham your father rejoiced that he might see my day: he saw it, and was glad.
John	Jn	50	8	57	The Jews therefore said to him: Thou art not yet fifty years old, and hast thou seen Abraham?
John	Jn	50	8	58	Jesus said to them: Amen, amen I say to you, before Abraham was made, I am.
John	Jn	50	8	59	They took up stones therefore to cast at him. But Jesus hid himself, and went out of the temple.
John	Jn	50	9	1	And Jesus passing by, saw a man, who was blind from his birth:
John	Jn	50	9	2	And his disciples asked him: Rabbi, who hath sinned, this man, or his parents, that he should be born blind?
John	Jn	50	9	3	Jesus answered: Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents; but that the works of God should be made manifest in him.
John	Jn	50	9	4	I must work the works of him that sent me, whilst it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work.
John	Jn	50	9	5	As long as I am in the world, I am the light of the world.
John	Jn	50	9	6	When he had said these things, he spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and spread the clay on his eyes,
John	Jn	50	9	7	And said to him: Go, wash in the pool of Siloe, which is interpreted, Sent. He went therefore, and washed, and he came seeing.
John	Jn	50	9	8	The neighbours therefore, and they who had seen him before that he was a beggar, said: Is not this he that sat and begged? Some said: This is he.
John	Jn	50	9	9	But others said: No, but he is like him. But he said: I am he.
John	Jn	50	9	10	They said therefore to him: How were thy eyes opened?
John	Jn	50	9	11	He answered: That man that is called Jesus made clay, and anointed my eyes, and said to me: Go to the pool of Siloe, and wash. And I went, I washed, and I see.
John	Jn	50	9	12	And they said to him: Where is he? He saith: I know not.
John	Jn	50	9	13	They bring him that had been blind to the Pharisees.
John	Jn	50	9	14	Now it was the sabbath, when Jesus made the clay, and opened his eyes.
John	Jn	50	9	15	Again therefore the Pharisees asked him, how he had received his sight. But he said to them: He put clay upon my eyes, and I washed, and I see.
John	Jn	50	9	16	Some therefore of the Pharisees said: This man is not of God, who keepeth not the sabbath. But others said: How can a man that is a sinner do such miracles? And there was a division among them.
John	Jn	50	9	17	They say therefore to the blind man again: What sayest thou of him that hath opened thy eyes? And he said: He is a prophet.
John	Jn	50	9	18	The Jews then did not believe concerning him, that he had been blind, and had received his sight, until they called the parents of him that had received his sight,
John	Jn	50	9	19	And asked them, saying: Is this your son, who you say was born blind? How then doth he now see?
John	Jn	50	9	20	His parents answered them, and said: We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind:
John	Jn	50	9	21	But how he now seeth, we know not; or who hath opened his eyes, we know not: ask himself: he is of age, let him speak for himself.
John	Jn	50	9	22	These things his parents said, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had already agreed among themselves, that if any man should confess him to be Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.
John	Jn	50	9	23	Therefore did his parents say: He is of age, ask himself.
John	Jn	50	9	24	They therefore called the man again that had been blind, and said to him: Give glory to God. We know that this man is a sinner.
John	Jn	50	9	25	He said therefore to them: If he be a sinner, I know not: one thing I know, that whereas I was blind, now I see.
John	Jn	50	9	26	They said then to him: What did he to thee? How did he open thy eyes?
John	Jn	50	9	27	He answered them: I have told you already, and you have heard: why would you hear it again? will you also become his disciples?
John	Jn	50	9	28	They reviled him therefore, and said: Be thou his disciple; but we are the disciples of Moses.
John	Jn	50	9	29	We know that God spoke to Moses: but as to this man, we know not from whence he is.
John	Jn	50	9	30	The man answered, and said to them: Why, herein is a wonderful thing, that you know not from whence he is, and he hath opened my eyes.
John	Jn	50	9	31	Now we know that God doth not hear sinners: but if a man be a server of God, and doth his will, him he heareth.
John	Jn	50	9	32	From the beginning of the world it hath not been heard, that any man hath opened the eyes of one born blind.
John	Jn	50	9	33	Unless this man were of God, he could not do any thing.
John	Jn	50	9	34	They answered, and said to him: Thou wast wholly born in sins, and dost thou teach us? And they cast him out.
John	Jn	50	9	35	Jesus heard that they had cast him out: and when he had found him, he said to him: Dost thou believe in the Son of God?
John	Jn	50	9	36	He answered, and said: Who is he, Lord, that I may believe in him?
John	Jn	50	9	37	And Jesus said to him: Thou hast both seen him; and it is he that talketh with thee.
John	Jn	50	9	38	And he said: I believe, Lord. And falling down, he adored him.
John	Jn	50	9	39	And Jesus said: For judgment I am come into this world; that they who see not, may see; and they who see, may become blind.
John	Jn	50	9	40	And some of the Pharisees, who were with him, heard: and they said unto him: Are we also blind?
John	Jn	50	9	41	Jesus said to them: If you were blind, you should not have sin: but now you say: We see. Your sin remaineth.
John	Jn	50	10	1	Amen, amen I say to you: He that entereth not by the door into the sheepfold, but climbeth up another way, the same is a thief and a robber.
John	Jn	50	10	2	But he that entereth in by the door is the shepherd of the sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	3	To him the porter openeth; and the sheep hear his voice: and he calleth his own sheep by name, and leadeth them out.
John	Jn	50	10	4	And when he hath let out his own sheep, he goeth before them: and the sheep follow him, because they know his voice.
John	Jn	50	10	5	But a stranger they follow not, but fly from him, because they know not the voice of strangers.
John	Jn	50	10	6	This proverb Jesus spoke to them. But they understood not what he spoke to them.
John	Jn	50	10	7	Jesus therefore said to them again: Amen, amen I say to you, I am the door of the sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	8	All others, as many as have come, are thieves and robbers: and the sheep heard them not.
John	Jn	50	10	9	I am the door. By me, if any man enter in, he shall be saved: and he shall go in, and go out, and shall find pastures.
John	Jn	50	10	10	The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy. I am come that they may have life, and may have it more abundantly.
John	Jn	50	10	11	I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd giveth his life for his sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	12	But the hireling, and he that is not the shepherd, whose own the sheep are not, seeth the wolf coming, and leaveth the sheep, and flieth: and the wolf catcheth, and scattereth the sheep:
John	Jn	50	10	13	And the hireling flieth, because he is a hireling: and he hath no care for the sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	14	I am the good shepherd; and I know mine, and mine know me.
John	Jn	50	10	15	As the Father knoweth me, and I know the Father: and I lay down my life for my sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	16	And other sheep I have, that are not of this fold: them also I must bring, and they shall hear my voice, and there shall be one fold and one shepherd.
John	Jn	50	10	17	Therefore doth the Father love me: because I lay down my life, that I may take it again.
John	Jn	50	10	18	No man taketh it away from me: but I lay it down of myself, and I have power to lay it down: and I have power to take it up again. This commandment have I received of my Father.
John	Jn	50	10	19	A dissension rose again among the Jews for these words.
John	Jn	50	10	20	And many of them said: He hath a devil, and is mad: why hear you him?
John	Jn	50	10	21	Others said: These are not the words of one that hath a devil: Can a devil open the eyes of the blind?
John	Jn	50	10	22	And it was the feast of the dedication at Jerusalem: and it was winter.
John	Jn	50	10	23	And Jesus walked in the temple, in Solomon's porch.
John	Jn	50	10	24	The Jews therefore came round about him, and said to him: How long dost thou hold our souls in suspense? If thou be the Christ, tell us plainly.
John	Jn	50	10	25	Jesus answered them: I speak to you, and you believe not: the works that I do in the name of my Father, they give testimony of me.
John	Jn	50	10	26	But you do not believe, because you are not of my sheep.
John	Jn	50	10	27	My sheep hear my voice: and I know them, and they follow me.
John	Jn	50	10	28	And I give them life everlasting; and they shall not perish for ever, and no man shall pluck them out of my hand.
John	Jn	50	10	29	That which my Father hath given me, is greater than all: and no one can snatch them out of the hand of my Father.
John	Jn	50	10	30	I and the Father are one.
John	Jn	50	10	31	The Jews then took up stones to stone him.
John	Jn	50	10	32	Jesus answered them: Many good works I have shewed you from my Father; for which of these works do you stone me?
John	Jn	50	10	33	The Jews answered him: For a good work we stone thee not, but for blasphemy; and because that thou, being a man, maketh thyself God.
John	Jn	50	10	34	Jesus answered them: Is it not written in your law: I said you are gods?
John	Jn	50	10	35	If he called them gods, to whom the word of God was spoken, and the scripture cannot be broken;
John	Jn	50	10	36	Do you say of him whom the Father hath sanctified and sent into the world: Thou blasphemest, because I said, I am the Son of God?
John	Jn	50	10	37	If I do not the works of my Father, believe me not.
John	Jn	50	10	38	But if I do, though you will not believe me, believe the works: that you may know and believe that the Father is in me, and I in the Father.
John	Jn	50	10	39	They sought therefore to take him; and he escaped out of their hands.
John	Jn	50	10	40	And he went again beyond the Jordan, into that place where John was baptizing first; and there he abode.
John	Jn	50	10	41	And many resorted to him, and they said: John indeed did no sign.
John	Jn	50	10	42	But all things whatsoever John said of this man, were true. And many believed in him.
John	Jn	50	11	1	Now there was a certain man sick, named Lazarus, of Bethania, of the town of Mary and Martha her sister.
John	Jn	50	11	2	(And Mary was she that anointed the Lord with ointment, and wiped his feet with her hair: whose brother Lazarus was sick.)
John	Jn	50	11	3	His sisters therefore sent to him, saying: Lord, behold, he whom thou lovest is sick.
John	Jn	50	11	4	And Jesus hearing it, said to them: This sickness is not unto death, but for the glory of God: that the Son of God may be glorified by it.
John	Jn	50	11	5	Now Jesus loved Martha, and her sister Mary, and Lazarus.
John	Jn	50	11	6	When he had heard therefore that he was sick, he still remained in the same place two days.
John	Jn	50	11	7	Then after that, he said to his disciples: Let us go into Judea again.
John	Jn	50	11	8	The disciples say to him: Rabbi, the Jews but now sought to stone thee: and goest thou thither again?
John	Jn	50	11	9	Jesus answered: Are there not twelve hours of the day? If a man walk in the day, he stumbleth not, because he seeth the light of this world:
John	Jn	50	11	10	But if he walk in the night, he stumbleth, because the light is not in him.
John	Jn	50	11	11	These things he said; and after that he said to them: Lazarus our friend sleepeth; but I go that I may awake him out of sleep.
John	Jn	50	11	12	His disciples therefore said: Lord, if he sleep, he shall do well.
John	Jn	50	11	13	But Jesus spoke of his death; and they thought that he spoke of the repose of sleep.
John	Jn	50	11	14	Then therefore Jesus said to them plainly: Lazarus is dead.
John	Jn	50	11	15	And I am glad, for your sakes, that I was not there, that you may believe: but let us go to him.
John	Jn	50	11	16	Thomas therefore, who is called Didymus, said to his fellow disciples: Let us also go, that we may die with him.
John	Jn	50	11	17	Jesus therefore came, and found that he had been four days already in the grave.
John	Jn	50	11	18	(Now Bethania was near Jerusalem, about fifteen furlongs off.)
John	Jn	50	11	19	And many of the Jews were come to Martha and Mary, to comfort them concerning their brother.
John	Jn	50	11	20	Martha therefore, as soon as she heard that Jesus had come, went to meet him: but Mary sat at home.
John	Jn	50	11	21	Martha therefore said to Jesus: Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.
John	Jn	50	11	22	But now also I know that whatsoever thou wilt ask of God, God will give it thee.
John	Jn	50	11	23	Jesus saith to her: Thy brother shall rise again.
John	Jn	50	11	24	Martha saith to him: I know that he shall rise again, in the resurrection at the last day.
John	Jn	50	11	25	Jesus said to her: I am the resurrection and the life: he that believeth in me, although he be dead, shall live:
John	Jn	50	11	26	And every one that liveth, and believeth in me, shall not die for ever. Believest thou this?
John	Jn	50	11	27	She saith to him: Yea, Lord, I have believed that thou art Christ the Son of the living God, who art come into this world.
John	Jn	50	11	28	And when she had said these things, she went, and called her sister Mary secretly, saying: The master is come, and calleth for thee.
John	Jn	50	11	29	She, as soon as she heard this, riseth quickly, and cometh to him.
John	Jn	50	11	30	For Jesus was not yet come into the town: but he was still in that place where Martha had met him.
John	Jn	50	11	31	The Jews therefore, who were with her in the house, and comforted her, when they saw Mary that she rose up speedily and went out, followed her, saying: She goeth to the grave to weep there.
John	Jn	50	11	32	When Mary therefore was come where Jesus was, seeing him, she fell down at his feet, and saith to him: Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.
John	Jn	50	11	33	Jesus, therefore, when he saw her weeping, and the Jews that were come with her, weeping, groaned in the spirit, and troubled himself,
John	Jn	50	11	34	And said: Where have you laid him? They say to him: Lord, come and see.
John	Jn	50	11	35	And Jesus wept.
John	Jn	50	11	36	The Jews therefore said: Behold how he loved him.
John	Jn	50	11	37	But some of them said: Could not he that opened the eyes of the man born blind, have caused that this man should not die?
John	Jn	50	11	38	Jesus therefore again groaning in himself, cometh to the sepulchre. Now it was a cave; and a stone was laid over it.
John	Jn	50	11	39	Jesus saith: Take away the stone. Martha, the sister of him that was dead, saith to him: Lord, by this time he stinketh, for he is now of four days.
John	Jn	50	11	40	Jesus saith to her: Did not I say to thee, that if thou believe, thou shalt see the glory of God?
John	Jn	50	11	41	They took therefore the stone away. And Jesus lifting up his eyes said: Father, I give thee thanks that thou hast heard me.
John	Jn	50	11	42	And I knew that thou hearest me always; but because of the people who stand about have I said it, that they may believe that thou hast sent me.
John	Jn	50	11	43	When he had said these things, he cried with a loud voice: Lazarus, come forth.
John	Jn	50	11	44	And presently he that had been dead came forth, bound feet and hands with winding bands; and his face was bound about with a napkin. Jesus said to them: Loose him, and let him go.
John	Jn	50	11	45	Many therefore of the Jews, who were come to Mary and Martha, and had seen the things that Jesus did, believed in him.
John	Jn	50	11	46	But some of them went to the Pharisees, and told them the things that Jesus had done.
John	Jn	50	11	47	The chief priests therefore, and the Pharisees, gathered a council, and said: What do we, for this man doth many miracles?
John	Jn	50	11	48	If we let him alone so, all will believe in him; and the Romans will come, and take away our place and nation.
John	Jn	50	11	49	But one of them, named Caiphas, being the high priest that year, said to them: You know nothing.
John	Jn	50	11	50	Neither do you consider that it is expedient for you that one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation perish not.
John	Jn	50	11	51	And this he spoke not of himself: but being the high priest of that year, he prophesied that Jesus should die for the nation.
John	Jn	50	11	52	And not only for the nation, but to gather together in one the children of God, that were dispersed.
John	Jn	50	11	53	From that day therefore they devised to put him to death.
John	Jn	50	11	54	Wherefore Jesus walked no more openly among the Jews; but he went into a country near the desert, unto a city that is called Ephrem, and there he abode with his disciples.
John	Jn	50	11	55	And the pasch of the Jews was at hand; and many from the country went up to Jerusalem, before the pasch to purify themselves.
John	Jn	50	11	56	They sought therefore for Jesus; and they discoursed one with another, standing in the temple: What think you that he is not come to the festival day? And the chief priests and Pharisees had given a commandment, that if any man knew where he was, he should tell, that they might apprehend him.
John	Jn	50	12	1	Jesus therefore, six days before the pasch, came to Bethania, where Lazarus had been dead, whom Jesus raised to life.
John	Jn	50	12	2	And they made him a supper there: and Martha served: but Lazarus was one of them that were at table with him.
John	Jn	50	12	3	Mary therefore took a pound of ointment of right spikenard, of great price, and anointed the feet of Jesus, and wiped his feet with her hair; and the house was filled with the odour of the ointment.
John	Jn	50	12	4	Then one of his disciples, Judas Iscariot, he that was about to betray him, said:
John	Jn	50	12	5	Why was not this ointment sold for three hundred pence, and given to the poor?
John	Jn	50	12	6	Now he said this, not because he cared for the poor; but because he was a thief, and having the purse, carried the things that were put therein.
John	Jn	50	12	7	Jesus therefore said: Let her alone, that she may keep it against the day of my burial.
John	Jn	50	12	8	For the poor you have always with you; but me you have not always.
John	Jn	50	12	9	A great multitude therefore of the Jews knew that he was there; and they came, not for Jesus' sake only, but that they might see Lazarus, whom he had raised from the dead.
John	Jn	50	12	10	But the chief priests thought to kill Lazarus also:
John	Jn	50	12	11	Because many of the Jews, by reason of him, went away, and believed in Jesus.
John	Jn	50	12	12	And on the next day, a great multitude that was to come to the festival day, when they had heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem,
John	Jn	50	12	13	Took branches of palm trees, and went forth to meet him, and cried: Hosanna, blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord, the king of Israel.
John	Jn	50	12	14	And Jesus found a young ass, and sat upon it, as it is written:
John	Jn	50	12	15	Fear not, daughter of Sion: behold, thy king cometh, sitting on an ass's colt.
John	Jn	50	12	16	These things his disciples did not know at the first; but when Jesus was glorified, then they remembered that these things were written of him, and that they had done these things to him.
John	Jn	50	12	17	The multitude therefore gave testimony, which was with him, when he called Lazarus out of the grave, and raised him from the dead.
John	Jn	50	12	18	For which reason also the people came to meet him, because they heard that he had done this miracle.
John	Jn	50	12	19	The Pharisees therefore said among themselves: Do you see that we prevail nothing? behold, the whole world is gone after him.
John	Jn	50	12	20	Now there were certain Gentiles among them, who came up to adore on the festival day.
John	Jn	50	12	21	These therefore came to Philip, who was of Bethsaida of Galilee, and desired him, saying: Sir, we would see Jesus.
John	Jn	50	12	22	Philip cometh, and telleth Andrew. Again Andrew and Philip told Jesus.
John	Jn	50	12	23	But Jesus answered them, saying: The hour is come, that the Son of man should be glorified.
John	Jn	50	12	24	Amen, amen I say to you, unless the grain of wheat falling into the ground die,
John	Jn	50	12	25	Itself remaineth alone. But if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit. He that loveth his life shall lose it; and he that hateth his life in this world, keepeth it unto life eternal.
John	Jn	50	12	26	If any man minister to me, let him follow me; and where I am, there also shall my minister be. If any man minister to me, him will my Father honour.
John	Jn	50	12	27	Now is my soul troubled. And what shall I say? Father, save me from this hour. But for this cause I came unto this hour.
John	Jn	50	12	28	Father, glorify thy name. A voice therefore came from heaven: I have both glorified it, and will glorify it again.
John	Jn	50	12	29	The multitude therefore that stood and heard, said that it thundered. Others said: An angel spoke to him.
John	Jn	50	12	30	Jesus answered, and said: This voice came not because of me, but for your sakes.
John	Jn	50	12	31	Now is the judgment of the world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out.
John	Jn	50	12	32	And I, if I be lifted up from the earth, will draw all things to myself.
John	Jn	50	12	33	(Now this he said, signifying what death he should die.)
John	Jn	50	12	34	The multitude answered him: We have heard out of the law, that Christ abideth for ever; and how sayest thou: The Son of man must be lifted up? Who is this Son of man?
John	Jn	50	12	35	Jesus therefore said to them: Yet a little while, the light is among you. Walk whilst you have the light, that the darkness overtake you not. And he that walketh in darkness, knoweth not whither he goeth.
John	Jn	50	12	36	Whilst you have the light, believe in the light, that you may be the children of light. These things Jesus spoke; and he went away, and hid himself from them.
John	Jn	50	12	37	And whereas he had done so many miracles before them, they believed not in him:
John	Jn	50	12	38	That the saying of Isaias the prophet might be fulfilled, which he said: Lord, who hath believed our hearing? and to whom hath the arm of the Lord been revealed?
John	Jn	50	12	39	Therefore they could not believe, because Isaias said again:
John	Jn	50	12	40	He hath blinded their eyes, and hardened their heart, that they should not see with their eyes, nor understand with their heart, and be converted, and I should heal them.
John	Jn	50	12	41	These things said Isaias, when he saw his glory, and spoke of him.
John	Jn	50	12	42	However, many of the chief men also believed in him; but because of the Pharisees they did not confess him, that they might not be cast out of the synagogue.
John	Jn	50	12	43	For they loved the glory of men more than the glory of God.
John	Jn	50	12	44	But Jesus cried, and said: He that believeth in me, doth not believe in me, but in him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	12	45	And he that seeth me, seeth him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	12	46	I am come a light into the world; that whosoever believeth in me, may not remain in darkness.
John	Jn	50	12	47	And if any man hear my words, and keep them not, I do not judge him: for I came not to judge the world, but to save the world.
John	Jn	50	12	48	He that despiseth me, and receiveth not my words, hath one that judgeth him; the word that I have spoken, the same shall judge him in the last day.
John	Jn	50	12	49	For I have not spoken of myself; but the Father who sent me, he gave me commandment what I should say, and what I should speak.
John	Jn	50	12	50	And I know that his commandment is life everlasting. The things therefore that I speak, even as the Father said unto me, so do I speak.
John	Jn	50	13	1	Before the festival day of the pasch, Jesus knowing that his hour was come, that he should pass out of this world to the Father: having loved his own who were in the world, he loved them unto the end.
John	Jn	50	13	2	And when supper was done, (the devil having now put into the heart of Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon, to betray him,)
John	Jn	50	13	3	Knowing that the Father had given him all things into his hands, and that he came from God, and goeth to God;
John	Jn	50	13	4	He riseth from supper, and layeth aside his garments, and having taken a towel, girded himself.
John	Jn	50	13	5	After that, he putteth water into a basin, and began to wash the feet of the disciples, and to wipe them with the towel wherewith he was girded.
John	Jn	50	13	6	He cometh therefore to Simon Peter. And Peter saith to him: Lord, dost thou wash my feet?
John	Jn	50	13	7	Jesus answered, and said to him: What I do thou knowest not now; but thou shalt know hereafter.
John	Jn	50	13	8	Peter saith to him: Thou shalt never wash my feet. Jesus answered him: If I wash thee not, thou shalt have no part with me.
John	Jn	50	13	9	Simon Peter saith to him: Lord, not only my feet, but also my hands and my head.
John	Jn	50	13	10	Jesus saith to him: He that is washed, needeth not but to wash his feet, but is clean wholly. And you are clean, but not all.
John	Jn	50	13	11	For he knew who he was that would betray him; therefore he said: You are not all clean.
John	Jn	50	13	12	Then after he had washed their feet, and taken his garments, being set down again, he said to them: Know you what I have done to you?
John	Jn	50	13	13	You call me Master, and Lord; and you say well, for so I am.
John	Jn	50	13	14	If then I being your Lord and Master, have washed your feet; you also ought to wash one another's feet.
John	Jn	50	13	15	For I have given you an example, that as I have done to you, so you do also.
John	Jn	50	13	16	Amen, amen I say to you: The servant is not greater than his lord; neither is the apostle greater than he that sent him.
John	Jn	50	13	17	If you know these things, you shall be blessed if you do them.
John	Jn	50	13	18	I speak not of you all: I know whom I have chosen. But that the scripture may be fulfilled: He that eateth bread with me, shall lift up his heel against me.
John	Jn	50	13	19	At present I tell you, before it come to pass: that when it shall come to pass, you may believe that I am he.
John	Jn	50	13	20	Amen, amen I say to you, he that receiveth whomsoever I send, receiveth me; and he that receiveth me, receiveth him that sent me.
John	Jn	50	13	21	When Jesus had said these things, he was troubled in spirit; and he testified, and said: Amen, amen I say to you, one of you shall betray me.
John	Jn	50	13	22	The disciples therefore looked one upon another, doubting of whom he spoke.
John	Jn	50	13	23	Now there was leaning on Jesus' bosom one of his disciples, whom Jesus loved.
John	Jn	50	13	24	Simon Peter therefore beckoned to him, and said to him: Who is it of whom he speaketh?
John	Jn	50	13	25	He therefore, leaning on the breast of Jesus, saith to him: Lord, who is it?
John	Jn	50	13	26	Jesus answered: He it is to whom I shall reach bread dipped. And when he had dipped the bread, he gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon.
John	Jn	50	13	27	And after the morsel, Satan entered into him. And Jesus said to him: That which thou dost, do quickly.
John	Jn	50	13	28	Now no man at the table knew to what purpose he said this unto him.
John	Jn	50	13	29	For some thought, because Judas had the purse, that Jesus had said to him: Buy those things which we have need of for the festival day: or that he should give something to the poor.
John	Jn	50	13	30	He therefore having received the morsel, went out immediately. And it was night.
John	Jn	50	13	31	When he therefore was gone out, Jesus said: Now is the Son of man glorified, and God is glorified in him.
John	Jn	50	13	32	If God be glorified in him, God also will glorify him in himself; and immediately will he glorify him.
John	Jn	50	13	33	Little children, yet a little while I am with you. You shall seek me; and as I said to the Jews: Whither I go you cannot come; so I say to you now.
John	Jn	50	13	34	A new commandment I give unto you: That you love one another, as I have loved you, that you also love one another.
John	Jn	50	13	35	By this shall all men know that you are my disciples, if you have love one for another.
John	Jn	50	13	36	Simon Peter saith to him: Lord, whither goest thou? Jesus answered: Whither I go, thou canst not follow me now; but thou shalt follow hereafter.
John	Jn	50	13	37	Peter saith to him: Why cannot I follow thee now? I will lay down my life for thee.
John	Jn	50	13	38	Jesus answered him: Wilt thou lay down thy life for me? Amen, amen I say to thee, the cock shall not crow, till thou deny me thrice.
John	Jn	50	14	1	Let not your heart be troubled. You believe in God, believe also in me.
John	Jn	50	14	2	In my Father's house there are many mansions. If not, I would have told you: because I go to prepare a place for you.
John	Jn	50	14	3	And if I shall go, and prepare a place for you, I will come again, and will take you to myself; that where I am, you also may be.
John	Jn	50	14	4	And whither I go you know, and the way you know.
John	Jn	50	14	5	Thomas saith to him: Lord, we know not whither thou goest; and how can we know the way?
John	Jn	50	14	6	Jesus saith to him: I am the way, and the truth, and the life. No man cometh to the Father, but by me.
John	Jn	50	14	7	If you had known me, you would without doubt have known my Father also: and from henceforth you shall know him, and you have seen him.
John	Jn	50	14	8	Philip saith to him: Lord, shew us the Father, and it is enough for us.
John	Jn	50	14	9	Jesus saith to him: Have I been so long a time with you; and have you not known me? Philip, he that seeth me seeth the Father also. How sayest thou, shew us the Father?
John	Jn	50	14	10	Do you not believe, that I am in the Father, and the Father in me? The words that I speak to you, I speak not of myself. But the Father who abideth in me, he doth the works.
John	Jn	50	14	11	Believe you not that I am in the Father, and the Father in me?
John	Jn	50	14	12	Otherwise believe for the very works' sake. Amen, amen I say to you, he that believeth in me, the works that I do, he also shall do; and greater than these shall he do.
John	Jn	50	14	13	Because I go to the Father: and whatsoever you shall ask the Father in my name, that will I do: that the Father may be glorified in the Son.
John	Jn	50	14	14	If you shall ask me any thing in my name, that I will do.
John	Jn	50	14	15	If you love me, keep my commandments.
John	Jn	50	14	16	And I will ask the Father, and he shall give you another Paraclete, that he may abide with you for ever.
John	Jn	50	14	17	The spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, nor knoweth him: but you shall know him; because he shall abide with you, and shall be in you.
John	Jn	50	14	18	I will not leave you orphans, I will come to you.
John	Jn	50	14	19	Yet a little while: and the world seeth me no more. But you see me: because I live, and you shall live.
John	Jn	50	14	20	In that day you shall know, that I am in my Father, and you in me, and I in you.
John	Jn	50	14	21	He that hath my commandments, and keepeth them; he it is that loveth me. And he that loveth me, shall be loved of my Father: and I will love him, and will manifest myself to him.
John	Jn	50	14	22	Judas saith to him, not the Iscariot: Lord, how is it, that thou wilt manifest thyself to us, and not to the world?
John	Jn	50	14	23	Jesus answered, and said to him: If any one love me, he will keep my word, and my Father will love him, and we will come to him, and will make our abode with him.
John	Jn	50	14	24	He that loveth me not, keepeth not my words. And the word which you have heard, is not mine; but the Father's who sent me.
John	Jn	50	14	25	These things have I spoken to you, abiding with you.
John	Jn	50	14	26	But the Paraclete, the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he will teach you all things, and bring all things to your mind, whatsoever I shall have said to you.
John	Jn	50	14	27	Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, do I give unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, nor let it be afraid.
John	Jn	50	14	28	You have heard that I said to you: I go away, and I come unto you. If you loved me, you would indeed be glad, because I go to the Father: for the Father is greater than I.
John	Jn	50	14	29	And now I have told you before it comes to pass: that when it shall come to pass, you may believe.
John	Jn	50	14	30	I will not now speak many things with you. For the prince of this world cometh, and in me he hath not any thing.
John	Jn	50	14	31	But that the world may know, that I love the Father: and as the Father hath given me commandment, so do I: Arise, let us go hence.
John	Jn	50	15	1	I am the true vine; and my Father is the husbandman.
John	Jn	50	15	2	Every branch in me, that beareth not fruit, he will take away: and every one that beareth fruit, he will purge it, that it may bring forth more fruit.
John	Jn	50	15	3	Now you are clean by reason of the word, which I have spoken to you.
John	Jn	50	15	4	Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, unless it abide in the vine, so neither can you, unless you abide in me.
John	Jn	50	15	5	I am the vine: you the branches: he that abideth in me, and I in him, the same beareth much fruit: for without me you can do nothing.
John	Jn	50	15	6	If any one abide not in me, he shall be cast forth as a branch, and shall wither, and they shall gather him up, and cast him into the fire, and he burneth.
John	Jn	50	15	7	If you abide in me, and my words abide in you, you shall ask whatever you will, and it shall be done unto you.
John	Jn	50	15	8	In this is my Father glorified; that you bring forth very much fruit, and become my disciples.
John	Jn	50	15	9	As the Father hath loved me, I also have loved you. Abide in my love.
John	Jn	50	15	10	If you keep my commandments, you shall abide in my love; as I also have kept my Father's commandments, and do abide in his love.
John	Jn	50	15	11	These things I have spoken to you, that my joy may be in you, and your joy may be filled.
John	Jn	50	15	12	This is my commandment, that you love one another, as I have loved you.
John	Jn	50	15	13	Greater love than this no man hath, that a man lay down his life for his friends.
John	Jn	50	15	14	You are my friends, if you do the things that I command you.
John	Jn	50	15	15	I will not now call you servants: for the servant knoweth not what his lord doth. But I have called you friends: because all things whatsoever I have heard of my Father, I have made known to you.
John	Jn	50	15	16	You have not chosen me: but I have chosen you; and have appointed you, that you should go, and should bring forth fruit; and your fruit should remain: that whatsoever you shall ask of the Father in my name, he may give it you.
John	Jn	50	15	17	These things I command you, that you love one another.
John	Jn	50	15	18	If the world hate you, know ye, that it hath hated me before you.
John	Jn	50	15	19	If you had been of the world, the world would love its own: but because you are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you.
John	Jn	50	15	20	Remember my word that I said to you: The servant is not greater than his master. If they have persecuted me, they will also persecute you: if they have kept my word, they will keep yours also.
John	Jn	50	15	21	But all these things they will do to you for my name's sake: because they know not him who sent me.
John	Jn	50	15	22	If I had not come, and spoken to them, they would not have sin; but now they have no excuse for their sin.
John	Jn	50	15	23	He that hateth me, hateth my Father also.
John	Jn	50	15	24	If I had not done among them the works that no other man hath done, they would not have sin; but now they have both seen and hated both me and my Father.
John	Jn	50	15	25	But that the word may be fulfilled which is written in their law: They hated me without cause.
John	Jn	50	15	26	But when the Paraclete cometh, whom I will send you from the Father, the Spirit of truth, who proceedeth from the Father, he shall give testimony of me.
John	Jn	50	15	27	And you shall give testimony, because you are with me from the beginning.
John	Jn	50	16	1	These things have I spoken to you, that you may not be scandalized.
John	Jn	50	16	2	They will put you out of the synagogues: yea, the hour cometh, that whosoever killeth you, will think that he doth a service to God.
John	Jn	50	16	3	And these things will they do to you; because they have not known the Father, nor me.
John	Jn	50	16	4	But these things I have told you, that when the hour shall come, you may remember that I told you of them.
John	Jn	50	16	5	But I told you not these things from the beginning, because I was with you. And now I go to him that sent me, and none of you asketh me: Whither goest thou?
John	Jn	50	16	6	But because I have spoken these things to you, sorrow hath filled your heart.
John	Jn	50	16	7	But I tell you the truth: it is expedient to you that I go: for if I go not, the Paraclete will not come to you; but if I go, I will send him to you.
John	Jn	50	16	8	And when he is come, he will convict the world of sin, and of justice, and of judgment.
John	Jn	50	16	9	Of sin: because they believed not in me.
John	Jn	50	16	10	And of justice: because I go to the Father; and you shall see me no longer.
John	Jn	50	16	11	And of judgment: because the prince of this world is already judged.
John	Jn	50	16	12	I have yet many things to say to you: but you cannot bear them now.
John	Jn	50	16	13	But when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will teach you all truth. For he shall not speak of himself; but what things soever he shall hear, he shall speak; and the things that are to come, he shall shew you.
John	Jn	50	16	14	He shall glorify me; because he shall receive of mine, and shall shew it to you.
John	Jn	50	16	15	All things whatsoever the Father hath, are mine. Therefore I said, that he shall receive of mine, and shew it to you.
John	Jn	50	16	16	A little while, and now you shall not see me; and again a little while, and you shall see me: because I go to the Father.
John	Jn	50	16	17	Then some of the disciples said one to another: What is this that he saith to us: A little while, and you shall not see me; and again a little while, and you shall see me, and, because I go to the Father?
John	Jn	50	16	18	They said therefore: What is this that he saith, A little while? we know not what he speaketh.
John	Jn	50	16	19	And Jesus knew that they had a mind to ask him; and he said to them: Of this do you inquire among yourselves, because I said: A little while, and you shall not see me; and again a little while, and you shall see me?
John	Jn	50	16	20	Amen, amen I say to you, that you shall lament and weep, but the world shall rejoice; and you shall be made sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy.
John	Jn	50	16	21	A woman, when she is in labour, hath sorrow, because her hour is come; but when she hath brought forth the child, she remembereth no more the anguish, for joy that a man is born into the world.
John	Jn	50	16	22	So also you now indeed have sorrow; but I will see you again, and your heart shall rejoice; and your joy no man shall take from you.
John	Jn	50	16	23	And in that day you shall not ask me any thing. Amen, amen I say to you: if you ask the Father any thing in my name, he will give it you.
John	Jn	50	16	24	Hitherto you have not asked any thing in my name. Ask, and you shall receive; that your joy may be full.
John	Jn	50	16	25	These things I have spoken to you in proverbs. The hour cometh, when I will no more speak to you in proverbs, but will shew you plainly of the Father.
John	Jn	50	16	26	In that day you shall ask in my name; and I say not to you, that I will ask the Father for you:
John	Jn	50	16	27	For the Father himself loveth you, because you have loved me, and have believed that I came out from God.
John	Jn	50	16	28	I came forth from the Father, and am come into the world: again I leave the world, and I go to the Father.
John	Jn	50	16	29	His disciples say to him: Behold, now thou speakest plainly, and speakest no proverb.
John	Jn	50	16	30	Now we know that thou knowest all things, and thou needest not that any man should ask thee. By this we believe that thou camest forth from God.
John	Jn	50	16	31	Jesus answered them: Do you now believe?
John	Jn	50	16	32	Behold, the hour cometh, and it is now come, that you shall be scattered every man to his own, and shall leave me alone; and yet I am not alone, because the Father is with me.
John	Jn	50	16	33	These things I have spoken to you, that in me you may have peace. In the world you shall have distress: but have confidence, I have overcome the world.
John	Jn	50	17	1	These things Jesus spoke, and lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said: Father, the hour is come, glorify thy Son, that thy Son may glorify thee.
John	Jn	50	17	2	As thou hast given him power over all flesh, that he may give eternal life to all whom thou hast given him.
John	Jn	50	17	3	Now this is eternal life: That they may know thee, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent.
John	Jn	50	17	4	I have glorified thee on the earth; I have finished the work which thou gavest me to do.
John	Jn	50	17	5	And now glorify thou me, O Father, with thyself, with the glory which I had, before the world was, with thee.
John	Jn	50	17	6	I have manifested thy name to the men whom thou hast given me out of the world. Thine they were, and to me thou gavest them; and they have kept thy word.
John	Jn	50	17	7	Now they have known, that all things which thou hast given me, are from thee:
John	Jn	50	17	8	Because the words which thou gavest me, I have given to them; and they have received them, and have known in very deed that I came out from thee, and they have believed that thou didst send me.
John	Jn	50	17	9	I pray for them: I pray not for the world, but for them whom thou hast given me: because they are thine:
John	Jn	50	17	10	And all my things are thine, and thine are mine; and I am glorified in them.
John	Jn	50	17	11	And now I am not in the world, and these are in the world, and I come to thee. Holy Father, keep them in thy name whom thou has given me; that they may be one, as we also are.
John	Jn	50	17	12	While I was with them, I kept them in thy name. Those whom thou gavest me have I kept; and none of them is lost, but the son of perdition, that the scripture may be fulfilled.
John	Jn	50	17	13	And now I come to thee; and these things I speak in the world, that they may have my joy filled in themselves.
John	Jn	50	17	14	I have given them thy word, and the world hath hated them, because they are not of the world; as I also am not of the world.
John	Jn	50	17	15	I pray not that thou shouldst take them out of the world, but that thou shouldst keep them from evil.
John	Jn	50	17	16	They are not of the world, as I also am not of the world.
John	Jn	50	17	17	Sanctify them in truth. Thy word is truth.
John	Jn	50	17	18	As thou hast sent me into the world, I also have sent them into the world.
John	Jn	50	17	19	And for them do I sanctify myself, that they also may be sanctified in truth.
John	Jn	50	17	20	And not for them only do I pray, but for them also who through their word shall believe in me;
John	Jn	50	17	21	That they all may be one, as thou, Father, in me, and I in thee; that they also may be one in us; that the world may believe that thou hast sent me.
John	Jn	50	17	22	And the glory which thou hast given me, I have given to them; that they may be one, as we also are one:
John	Jn	50	17	23	I in them, and thou in me; that they may be made perfect in one: and the world may know that thou hast sent me, and hast loved them, as thou hast also loved me.
John	Jn	50	17	24	Father, I will that where I am, they also whom thou hast given me may be with me; that they may see my glory which thou hast given me, because thou hast loved me before the creation of the world.
John	Jn	50	17	25	Just Father, the world hath not known thee; but I have known thee: and these have known that thou hast sent me.
John	Jn	50	17	26	And I have made known thy name to them, and will make it known; that the love wherewith thou hast loved me, may be in them, and I in them.
John	Jn	50	18	1	When Jesus had said these things, he went forth with his disciples over the brook Cedron, where there was a garden, into which he entered with his disciples.
John	Jn	50	18	2	And Judas also, who betrayed him, knew the place; because Jesus had often resorted thither together with his disciples.
John	Jn	50	18	3	Judas therefore having received a band of soldiers and servants from the chief priests and the Pharisees, cometh thither with lanterns and torches and weapons.
John	Jn	50	18	4	Jesus therefore, knowing all things that should come upon him, went forth, and said to them: Whom seek ye?
John	Jn	50	18	5	They answered him: Jesus of Nazareth. Jesus saith to them: I am he. And Judas also, who betrayed him, stood with them.
John	Jn	50	18	6	As soon therefore as he had said to them: I am he; they went backward, and fell to the ground.
